    <node id="United States">
      <data key="d0">United States</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The United States is a North American country with diverse agricultural regions influenced by varying topography, soil types, and climates, containing over 18,000 different types of soils. Prevailing winds typically come from the north and west, influencing the recommended placement of windbreaks. The western regions are noted for grass production due to low rainfall, and the north-central sections are suitable for rye and hairy vetch cover crops.

The agricultural history of the United States includes homesteading, the impact of the Depression, post-World War II suburbanization, and the ongoing loss of farmland to development. Farming principles such as overseeding red clover are applied, and there is an increasing demand for fish products, with farm-raised shrimp accounting for nearly one-third of the total shrimp supply consumed. The country is also experiencing an increase in the number of small farms.

The United States has a significant beekeeping industry that faces challenges such as certain ant species, the spread of Africanized bees (which first arrived in 1991), tracheal mites (leading to colony losses in the late 1980s), and Varroa mites (spread to at least 40 states by 1992). Terramycin is the only legally allowed antibiotic for use in beehives under federal regulations. The United States is also home to the American Apitherapy Society, although the number of managed honey bee colonies has dropped from 5 million in the 1940s to 2.5 million today.

The USDA has defined eleven climate zones for the United States, and various agencies like the USDA, IRS, and National Small Farm Commission apply definitions of farms and farmers there. Notably, 94% of farms in the U.S. fit the National Small Farm Commission's definition of "small." Four companies process 87 percent of all beef in the United States. The SARE program has four regional U.S. offices, and the Night crawler (Lumbricus terrestris) earthworm is not native to the United States, but it has successfully adapted there.

The United States is the location where the Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) movement was founded, and where the trend of integrating agriculture into housing developments is growing. It is the setting for various organizations and agricultural initiatives. As many as 50,000 gardens have been created due to Barker's idea being adopted by hundreds of organizations. The grassroots food movement is expanding "across the nation" to reestablish local grain economies, and the growth in farmers' markets, CSAs, and the broader movement is taking place there. 163 university leaders had signed the Talloires Declaration by 2010, indicating significant participation in the campus sustainability movement. The amenities enjoyed by the family at Seeds of Solidarity, such as lights and running water, are mentioned in comparison to conditions in other countries. 25% of all pharmacy prescriptions in 1993 were substances extracted from plants. Numerous cities are changing their laws to permit backyard chickens, indicating a national trend. Many communities, including major cities like Boston, New York City, and Los Angeles, now permit backyard chickens.

The United States is the potential maximum scale for a web of connecting threads within a sustainable community food system. It is also the country where food waste is a significant issue, according to studies from the University of Arizona and data from the EPA. The country is the primary location where domesticated wild rice is grown, with most production occurring in California. It is the country in which the history and evolution of the community gardening movement, from the Progressive Era to modern day, is discussed. Holyoke, Massachusetts has the highest concentration of Puerto Ricans in the United States, outside of Puerto Rico itself. It is also the country where a national program of 'Youth Community Food Farms' could be implemented. The story critiques its meat market practices, such as keeping middle cuts for domestic consumption while exporting the rest, and importing meat from distant countries like Brazil and Argentina. Hunger and gleaning are primary focuses, with over 40 million people facing hunger. SoSA delivers food to the 'lower 48' states. The childhood obesity epidemic is a major crisis and where the Farm to School movement is active in all 50 states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d47a7d4e49c6e48a2727071f21a879ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6dd73e41a475c9933ac4783be5f57a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0fadd2de5cdd877a432eba713a59ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2b2fd01aa45dadaa82a243d140ec5f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17984d082222b7d2f1526b0b77119804&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27bb80a716045bb643a01fd3aae1d84b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8965f3e3965322fdf5c53aebddde1e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-123973bb8732b383c984f14c89a9aa5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445fbff3137d26bce84d879934fb156e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c58f4785be38b80316bcdb547edbe48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d4150698732f393c235b8b3e1cb2d88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82372fd5a606e148caa2a0647673892b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d711f27560f7987b017b85fa9c8a2e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16e699b4bb77d0bdc27d883c3cafa88c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c07830327394a77dc9e8ac1a53acd63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498630940c856e5feff77c3e963f5210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e410bfae74fb6896e8e0079e060cf83d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-940d85de3b7092a6c76b3ef360a50ea0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df7ec17c31731168941c83b97fd64a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b652e467f32b1db6fbb1cf5b9315586e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-347d33c4b812366f78a72782c922f5f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5bf9269446157b7f585b574d80342a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ecda741e6aebaebfb4bbcd928bb80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d971c6976ab8e71370d85b346b00f467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51cfeabc3f21e3329484ec062ac1c4b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3d99de4967b60e7e74b3639abc430c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff2a1270133813dbf92927fcbf14a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef9c9aefa244f3e5e6f50b424cd984c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0013e0bf73a3def4eb11a0a48ef9234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1ce27dcb115879ec30587ba69b4095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d94881bd64e92c01d329307d5d40738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b73ca7de046e79c23f93a20f80755db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cbfa7273b78ee011a6cb142bb82745a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db735f250cad30d060b6ea644151e172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9d28e4a28ca972c9e289441c78c0be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbeff72000d21039cdbac6ba65f75077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c4a3f4f76cd87581e1acc8d4a5d71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ebc646508b0f93fb43f529856b4d56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a748f8974ea30d2229e5c6357765d4da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9465e78f869f57a714827f88ed9c132</data>
