    <node id="Forage">
      <data key="d0">Forage</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Forage refers to plant material that serves as food for animals, with specific definitions for livestock and bees. For grazing livestock, forage is plant material, such as pasture grasses, and an adequate supply can reduce an animal's need for free-standing water. It is also the subject of the Forage Information System. In the context of bees, forage refers to the flowering plants that produce nectar and pollen, which are essential food sources for their nutrition. The availability of this forage is dependent on the climate and region. For a hive's success, it is important that forage is available within a 1-to-2-mile radius and that the area is not already saturated with other bee colonies. Bees have a sophisticated method of communicating about their food sources, using a "dance language" to convey the type, quality, distance, and direction of the forage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a5bf9269446157b7f585b574d80342a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66bbc17b9fd4fb132a3a76abd2df0690</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stings">
      <data key="d0">Stings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An inherent risk and important consideration in beekeeping, discussed as a topic for beginners in the book.&lt;SEP&gt;Stings are a defensive behavior of honey bees, described as a primary 'down side' and a 'minor irritation' for beekeepers. This behavior is essential for the bees' survival, as it allows them to protect their honey from predators. Getting stung is presented as an unavoidable aspect of beekeeping.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0a5bf9269446157b7f585b574d80342a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3025455da6b06dabe347fe4878bb963</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
