    <node id="Miticides">
      <data key="d0">Miticides</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of chemical mentioned alongside insecticides, herbicides, and fungicides, which can have diverse effects on honey bees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d711f27560f7987b017b85fa9c8a2e56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bee Colony/Hive">
      <data key="d0">Bee Colony/Hive</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The basic unit of a beekeeping operation, which is vulnerable to pesticide damage. Actions such as moving, confining, or feeding the colony are key management practices. The health of the hive is indicated by its population and behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d711f27560f7987b017b85fa9c8a2e56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Spray Damage">
      <data key="d0">Spray Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The harm caused to bee colonies by pesticide sprays. Avoidance is the primary defense, but beekeepers can take steps to mitigate damage if exposure is unavoidable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d711f27560f7987b017b85fa9c8a2e56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Corn Pollen">
      <data key="d0">Corn Pollen</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A resource from the corn crop that is very attractive to honey bees, drawing them to forage in areas that are often sprayed with insecticides.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d711f27560f7987b017b85fa9c8a2e56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contaminated Stores">
      <data key="d0">Contaminated Stores</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Refers to nectar or pollen within the hive that has been contaminated with pesticides. These stores can kill bees within the hive even if the foragers were not immediately affected in the field.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d711f27560f7987b017b85fa9c8a2e56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Insecticide Poisoning">
      <data key="d0">Insecticide Poisoning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The specific affliction a bee colony suffers after exposure to insecticides. Symptoms include a sudden drop in forager population, dead bees at the hive entrance, and abnormal crawling behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d711f27560f7987b017b85fa9c8a2e56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
