    <node id="Miticur/amitraz">
      <data key="d0">Miticur/amitraz</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Miticur/amitraz is a chemical miticide used to treat infestations of both tracheal and varroa mites in honey bees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Queen(s)">
      <data key="d0">Queen(s)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The queen is the sole reproductive female in a honey bee colony. The text references her life span, development, physical characteristics, role in brood development, and the process of replacing her (requeening).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hive(s)">
      <data key="d0">Hive(s)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A hive is the man-made structure where a honey bee colony lives. The text details its various components like bottom boards, covers, frames, and stands, as well as management aspects like ventilation, location, and reversing bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Extractors">
      <data key="d0">Extractors</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Extractors are mechanical devices, typically using centrifugal force, to remove honey from the comb without destroying it. The text lists different types, such as radial and tangential.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nucleus Hives (nucs)">
      <data key="d0">Nucleus Hives (nucs)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A nucleus hive (or nuc) is a small, functioning honey bee colony, complete with a queen, workers, brood, and food stores on several frames. It is a common way to acquire bees to start a new hive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee2dbfbb5c1a5664034bad31b4143c62</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740472</data>
    </node>
