    <node id="Gardening">
      <data key="d0">Gardening</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Gardening is the practice of cultivating plants and serves as a central category for various publications and resources. It encompasses a range of home and market gardening techniques, including square foot gardening, organic methods, and no-till gardening. While gardening is sometimes debated as being either an elitist activity or a beneficial tool, it is largely presented as a means for whimsical, educational, and artistic fun. The practice offers a way to renew a sense of community, connect with nature, find personal renewal, and gain tangible control over one's food supply. Gardening is a prominent sub-category for publishers focused on country living skills and plant cultivation, such as Storey Publishing, Countryman Press, and Ten Speed Press, as well as for resources like the magazine Organic Gardening, HortIdeas, and Greenweb.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-727af20c5834776e4c44ee5e64fd02aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34502be14cbf099cb7c93ccf9aeb56c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5aeb69db517fc797c325acc9dcb88413&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66bbc17b9fd4fb132a3a76abd2df0690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2920f4362eb05a4692fa915ca812b425</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740833</data>
    </node>
