    </node>
    <node id="Madison">
      <data key="d0">Madison</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A city that is home to the University of Wisconsin-Extension, a co-publisher of the 'Alternative Field Crops Manual'.&lt;SEP&gt;Madison, a city in Wisconsin, is a central case study for urban agriculture. It is the location of the Troy Gardens project, which is a cohousing and community garden initiative. The city supported this project by providing a loan for the purchase of the site through its Community Development Block Grant program. In 2004, Madison reversed its poultry ban, allowing residents to keep a maximum of four chickens. The city's mayor, Dave Cieslewicz, championed the practice of keeping backyard chickens for community sustainability and food justice, and he discussed urban agriculture on his blog, cityofmadison.com.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d94881bd64e92c01d329307d5d40738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aaa683758c365cd82a3b03895da095e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0adcf3a18e5a064a6ed2b9d46dff75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f65dcd9bf73d5a51e1f5f20d7e1772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6524af1074c6309e3cd8d13cbf621c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2920f4362eb05a4692fa915ca812b425</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740833</data>
    </node>
