    <node id="100-mile diet">
      <data key="d0">100-mile diet</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A dietary concept and movement, started by Alisa Smith and J.B. Mackinnon, that involves consuming only food produced within a 100-mile radius of one's home. It has influenced a new sensibility about local and regional food."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ae240ee8f1e0681df991703ff2ca94b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Victory Garden">
      <data key="d0">Victory Garden</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A concept of home and neighborhood food production, historically significant during the early 20th century. At their peak in 1944, they provided about 40% of the vegetables and fruit consumed by Americans. The text proposes reviving this idea."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"A concept of home gardening for food production, mentioned in the introduction by Tim Beatley as a historical practice worth rediscovering in the current economic and cultural climate."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A type of garden promoted during wartime to increase food production, discussed as an evolution from the 'War Garden' in a Landscape Journal article.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e0df78d09fb33ee041307abbce7d33e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae240ee8f1e0681df991703ff2ca94b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dbce12e45fe13ef4f6973f92e57e779</data>
