    <node id="Greg Peterson">
      <data key="d0">Greg Peterson</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">"A representative for The Urban Farm."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"The operator of 'The Urban Farm' in Phoenix, Arizona. He demonstrates high-yield agriculture on a small, one-third-of-an-acre lot by planting over 70 fruit trees and raising chickens and vegetables."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Greg Peterson is the representative for The Urban Farm organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062d9ac74f75199c91576d982ab5a9f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae240ee8f1e0681df991703ff2ca94b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Urban Farm">
      <data key="d0">The Urban Farm</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">"An enterprise operated by Greg Peterson on a small lot in Phoenix, Arizona. It serves as a model for urban agriculture, featuring over 70 fruit trees, and hosts classes, fruit tree sales, and other agricultural activities."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization with a website www.urbanfarm.org. Its representative is Greg Peterson. No physical address is provided."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The Urban Farm is an organization represented by Greg Peterson, with a web presence at www.urbanfarm.org.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062d9ac74f75199c91576d982ab5a9f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae240ee8f1e0681df991703ff2ca94b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Phoenix">
      <data key="d0">Phoenix</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">"A city in Arizona that is the location of Greg Peterson's 'The Urban Farm'."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A city mentioned as the source for Diablo Burger's bread and cookies, illustrating the logistical network of local sourcing. A couple from Phoenix also provided a positive comment about the restaurant.&lt;SEP&gt;Phoenix is a major city in Arizona, located near Peoria where McClendon's Select farm is based.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-087cef03c5ab256c59a3f536c4533b6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae240ee8f1e0681df991703ff2ca94b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db735f250cad30d060b6ea644151e172</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tim Beatley">
      <data key="d0">Tim Beatley</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Based on the information provided, Tim Beatley is the author of the text excerpt and several specific sections within it. He advocates for replacing globalized food production with resilient, community-based food systems. Tim Beatley is credited with writing the introductory text on the historical context of home gardens, the section on the South Village development, a description of The Intervale in Burlington, Vermont, and an introduction to the Marine Stewardship Council. He is also described as a friend and teaching cohort of the author in the field of food systems planning who contributed significantly to expanding the project's vision. His name is mentioned multiple times, indicating a significant role in the overall work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0809b82d4ca6415545d8263dbdcfcf73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae240ee8f1e0681df991703ff2ca94b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfd05a12ef78763e74306325feeb5eac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60071a35b7d93bd331a3e0d32f9f3fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa8b612642fa385d2af41e902aa75d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef2c308d995bae34c938de2dff3f5cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dbce12e45fe13ef4f6973f92e57e779</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Add-On Value">
      <data key="d0">Add-On Value</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A business principle that involves processing a raw commodity into a new, finished product to increase its market value, gross income, and net profit. Examples given include turning berries into jam, hogs into sausage, and using various parts of elk or ratites."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7e2a281158355949bfa9c35a51c5622a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740810</data>
    </node>
