    <node id="Sausage">
      <data key="d0">Sausage</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sausage is a value-added, processed meat product made from hogs, used as a primary example to illustrate the benefits of direct marketing and value-added processing. It is presented as a highly profitable alternative to selling live animals, raw meat, or other raw commodities. Specifically, "whole hog sausage" that is direct-marketed to consumers can dramatically increase an enterprise's net profit. One example provided is an 80 percent lean sausage sold by the author at a flat rate of $2.50 per pound. In addition to its financial advantages, sausage also offers the practical benefit of ease of storage, as it fits more easily into a freezer than a whole carcass.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a603ecfe84d863d026d6d7309cc4add3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-473f8348a15ba74f2e21ca4cc96c583e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db06dd0bc574d59f7ffa8848b9ae23fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5deb38ed9dc0a60bcac768fbb7955c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740812</data>
    </node>
