    <node id="Schools">
      <data key="d0">Schools</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Schools serve multiple, interconnected roles related to community health and the local food system. Identified as the "front line" in combating childhood obesity, these educational institutions are increasingly joining the local food movement by incorporating fresh, local food, sometimes with the assistance of organizations like ASAP. This makes schools a key part of the institutional market for local food. Beyond consumption, schools act as crucial venues for outreach. They are targeted by farms for promotional events and tours, such as "School Day," where visits from children can encourage their parents to return and make purchases. Additionally, schools are key locations where young, successful farmers can share their stories to inspire potential new farmers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fee18f76430d121ab613984069f209e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba841e41630d5b5e46b271cb1a11d579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aaeba6a87de6589129068300a4f26db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740842</data>
    </node>
