    <node id="Elizabeth Keen">
      <data key="d0">Elizabeth Keen</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Elizabeth Keen is a farmer and representative for Indian Line Farm in South Egremont, Massachusetts, which is one of the first Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) programs in the United States. Along with her partner, Al Thorp, Elizabeth Keen was able to purchase the farm's buildings and secure a long-term land lease through a partnership with the community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f188db350c6a6f2fdb22a9e9283e4dc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-951f3a20705ad68da0aafd6377f51f52</data>
