    <node id="Ad Gazettes">
      <data key="d0">Ad Gazettes</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of publication, mentioned alongside magazines, that may have negotiable advertising rates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Travel Agencies">
      <data key="d0">Travel Agencies</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Also referred to as touring companies, these are businesses the farm should contact to arrange group tours, potentially for a fee per person or busload.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clubs">
      <data key="d0">Clubs</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of community group that can be targeted to arrange and host tours of the farm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Boy or Girl Scouts">
      <data key="d0">Boy or Girl Scouts</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific example of a children's organization the farm can collaborate with on fundraising initiatives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Church or Service Group">
      <data key="d0">Church or Service Group</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of community organization that can partner with the farm to sponsor a fundraiser.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Field Day">
      <data key="d0">Field Day</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An event a farm can sponsor to attract fellow farmers by providing an explanation of its profitable farming methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Value-Added Workshop">
      <data key="d0">Value-Added Workshop</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A paid class or workshop hosted at the farm where people are charged a fee to learn a skill, allowing the farm to market its expertise as well as its products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pumpkin-Carving Contest">
      <data key="d0">Pumpkin-Carving Contest</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A seasonal event suggested for Halloween, where the entry fee is the cost of the pumpkin, designed to attract families and generate sales.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fall Garlic Planting">
      <data key="d0">Fall Garlic Planting</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"A seasonal event at Indian Line Farm that involves CSA members helping with farm work, illustrating community engagement."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-951f3a20705ad68da0aafd6377f51f52</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Supported Agriculture (CSA)">
      <data key="d0">Community Supported Agriculture (CSA)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A farming model where members ('shareholders') pay upfront for a share of a farm's produce, sharing in the risks and rewards. The text outlines key strategies for success, including relationship building, transparency, cooperation between farms, and creating variations to support low-income communities."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"A food production and distribution model where consumers buy 'shares' in a farm's harvest in advance. The text identifies this model as a key feature of pioneering farms like Indian Line Farm and modern developments like South Village."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Appalachian Sustainable Development (ASD)">
      <data key="d0">Appalachian Sustainable Development (ASD)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Based on the information provided, Appalachian Sustainable Development (ASD) is a nonprofit community organization based in Southwest Virginia that also operates in the Appalachian region of Tennessee. The organization's mission is to revitalize rural economies by building a local, sustainable food and forestry system.

To achieve its goals, ASD provides a range of services, including farmer education, mentoring, market development, and distribution. A key part of its work involves transitioning tobacco farmers to certified organic farming methods, and its expertise is cited as an example for new farmers, such as advising them to start with less-perishable crops like hard squashes. The organization created the Appalachian Harvest brand to market its products and by 2010, it had developed a network of about 70 organic farmers and 30 beef producers.

As a distributor of organic produce, ASD forms mutually beneficial partnerships with other organizations. For example, it partners with Lynchburg Grows, supplying them with produce at wholesale prices to ensure reliability and quality for their CSA program.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0809b82d4ca6415545d8263dbdcfcf73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ebf31ca8cf0e8a5dbe6d09c3efa272&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcbabc72a18ceaedb14452609db7d256&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efae0d6c5dabc751b9ceb56518857dff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497b3487d00eabefe426a10fa32f8010</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Milwaukee">
      <data key="d0">Milwaukee</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Milwaukee, a city in the United States, is the base for the urban agriculture organization Growing Power. The organization was founded in Milwaukee by Will Allen, who purchased the last remaining farm within the city limits to launch the initiative. Growing Power's main operations, including its urban farm, innovative greenhouses, and aquaponics system, are located on the city's North Side. The organization interacts with the local community and aims to prove the viability of its model. After observing the economic benefits of the farm, the city of Milwaukee has become a more willing partner and is now interested in positioning itself as the "urban agriculture capital of the U.S." Additionally, Milwaukee is the location of the Rainbow Farmers' Cooperative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1f62a42d98fb088984d8c0a7a0d293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0adcf3a18e5a064a6ed2b9d46dff75f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e970626c7a63b367949cb5600957bcab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48fbe13ccbab1daf20dc4c993f911dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8965f3e3965322fdf5c53aebddde1e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf60421969007759eb279ddb028ec67b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Jones Valley Urban Farm">
      <data key="d0">The Jones Valley Urban Farm</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">"The Jones Valley Urban Farm, located in Knoxville, Tennessee, experimented with different tactics to make its CSA accessible to low-income populations, including offering highly discounted shares and a work-for-share program."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Knoxville, Tennessee">
      <data key="d0">Knoxville, Tennessee</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Knoxville, Tennessee, is a city that is home to both the Jones Valley Urban Farm and the Beardsley Community Farm. The city actively supported the establishment of the Beardsley Community Farm by providing 7 acres of park land to the Community Action Committee (CAC). This farm was created with the mission to promote food security, combat crime, and provide a food source in a food desert.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bcbabc72a18ceaedb14452609db7d256&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c9669112f71f37c0273243e8cc59e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfd05a12ef78763e74306325feeb5eac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South Village">
      <data key="d0">South Village</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">South Village is a new, planned housing development and community located at 130 Allen Road East in South Burlington, Vermont. Designed as a New Urbanist community, it is pioneering an approach that integrates farming and sustainability principles directly into its design. Agriculture serves as a primary amenity, featuring a working farm and a CSA (Community Supported Agriculture). The development is situated on a 220-acre site, with 75% of the land conserved for natural landscapes. Legally, South Village is organized as a low-profit limited liability corporation (LLLC) and its representative is Will Raap.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South Burlington, Vermont">
      <data key="d0">South Burlington, Vermont</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">"A city in Vermont, identified as the location of the South Village development."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"South Burlington, Vermont is the location of the innovative South Village housing development."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A city in Vermont that is the location of the South Village housing development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="School Day">
      <data key="d0">School Day</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A promotional event sponsored by the farm in partnership with local elementary schools, where children receive a free small pumpkin to encourage future family visits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Egg Hunt">
      <data key="d0">Egg Hunt</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An Easter-themed event to attract visitors to the farm, which can be combined with the sale of value-added products like decorated eggs or pet rabbits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Classified Ad">
      <data key="d0">Classified Ad</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of advertisement placed in newspapers and magazines. The text advises it should have a catchy headline and contact information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Display Advertising">
      <data key="d0">Display Advertising</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A visual form of advertising for publications that should include a catchy headline, a brief description, contact information, and an image, using white space effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="On-line Catalog Sales">
      <data key="d0">On-line Catalog Sales</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An e-commerce sales method to consider as the farm business expands, using its website to sell products directly to customers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Petting Zoo">
      <data key="d0">Petting Zoo</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An activity suggested to be added to a farm to help make it a destination for visitors, especially families with children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bed-and-Breakfast">
      <data key="d0">Bed-and-Breakfast</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A lodging service recommended as an option to offer on the farm to attract visitors and turn the property into a destination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Craft Shop">
      <data key="d0">Craft Shop</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A potential on-farm business, possibly featuring works of local artists, suggested as an additional activity to attract people and generate revenue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2afc9b5400cf61bfbec7b607b711ba96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Drought">
      <data key="d0">The Drought</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A severe weather event that ruined seed germination for Greensgrow Farm's hydroponic operation, serving as a key case study on the importance of transparency and managing shareholder expectations in a CSA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Basket Program">
      <data key="d0">Market Basket Program</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A program by Growing Power that serves as a variation on the traditional CSA model. It allows customers to order a basket weekly and pay upon pickup, making fresh produce more accessible to low-income families without a large up-front cost.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rainbow Farmer's Cooperative">
      <data key="d0">Rainbow Farmer's Cooperative</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A cooperative that provides wholesale produce prices to Growing Power, enabling them to offer their Market Baskets at a cost 25 to 30 percent below supermarket prices.&lt;SEP&gt;Founded in 1993 by Will Allen and four other farmers, this cooperative comprises about 300 small-scale farmers across the Midwest and Southeast. It pools, packages, and markets various agricultural products, providing logistics and marketing support to its members and increasing their share of sales revenue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75f4b1f56482ca88dc86d76611131fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa54079f022f9b869fe9a285cb16fa6a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Andres Duany">
      <data key="d0">Andres Duany</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A leading proponent and practitioner of New Urbanism who coined the phrase 'Agriculture is the new golf' to describe the trend of integrating farms into housing developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="New Urbanism">
      <data key="d0">New Urbanism</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"An urban design philosophy that promotes the creation of walkable, mixed-use, and environmentally friendly neighborhoods as an alternative to suburban sprawl."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A design and planning trend that advocates for compact, mixed-use, walkable communities as an alternative to car-dependent suburbanization. South Village is an example of a New Urbanist community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ed McMahon">
      <data key="d0">Ed McMahon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual from the Urban Land Institute who estimates there are at least two hundred developments in the U.S. that incorporate agriculture as a key component.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Urban Land Institute">
      <data key="d0">Urban Land Institute</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A nonprofit research and education organization specializing in land use and urban development.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization associated with Ed McMahon that tracks trends in land use and real estate development, including those incorporating agriculture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38c9174dd4002f6529026fc7fd3c23f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Will Raap">
      <data key="d0">Will Raap</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Will Raap is an entrepreneur and advocate in the sustainable agriculture and food sector. He is the founder of both the Intervale Center and Gardener's Supply Company and serves as a representative for Intervale Community Farm and South Village. Raap was instrumental in the development of these communities; he assisted in designing South Village to include a working farm and a CSA with the goal of embedding farmers into the community. For the Intervale, he set an ambitious early goal for its farms to supply 10% of the local food and emphasized that restoring the soil through composting was an essential precondition for its success.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f188db350c6a6f2fdb22a9e9283e4dc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c977e0c22629a3b90f1214c2370c4394&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd12c93ca420ae0dfd8107f51eec1886</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conservation Department">
      <data key="d0">Conservation Department</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A governmental body that may require farmers to obtain permits for certain operations, such as raising deer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Registration Association">
      <data key="d0">Registration Association</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An organization that farmers may need to join and pay fees to in order to register purebred stock, which is necessary for maintaining bloodline papers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Drought Years Of 1953 And 1954">
      <data key="d0">Drought Years Of 1953 And 1954</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A historical period of drought that caused great financial stress for farmers, used as an example of a poor time to start or expand a traditional agriculture operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rural Crises Of The 1980s">
      <data key="d0">Rural Crises Of The 1980s</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A historical period of economic hardship in rural areas that caused significant financial stress for farmers, mentioned as a risky time to begin a farming venture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="U-picks">
      <data key="d0">U-picks</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of direct-to-consumer sales operation where customers can harvest their own produce. These events require the farm to have liability insurance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Enterprise Selection">
      <data key="d0">Enterprise Selection</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The core process of deciding which crops or livestock to raise on a farm. The selection is based on comprehensive research into factors like soil type, water access, costs, regulations, and market potential.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Farm Liability Insurance">
      <data key="d0">Farm Liability Insurance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of insurance mentioned as a requirement for certain enterprises, such as U-picks and roadside stands, to protect against liability for customer injuries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Permits And Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Permits And Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal and administrative requirements that farmers must consider. These can include state rules for shipping plants, permits for raising certain animals, and health codes for food processing, all of which add to start-up costs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intervale">
      <data key="d0">Intervale</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A 350-acre area of low-lying land along the Winooski River floodplain within Burlington, VT. Formerly a dumping ground, it has been transformed into a center for sustainable urban agriculture, hosting numerous farms, gardens, and other facilities managed by the Intervale Center.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization co-founded by Will Raap, which was involved in the agricultural design of the South Village development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d83e7f9383ec8baa65b1a2fc070b1acd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED)">
      <data key="d0">Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A green building certification program that has certified the homes in South Village.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Energy Star">
      <data key="d0">Energy Star</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An energy efficiency certification program that has certified the homes in South Village.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South Village LLLC">
      <data key="d0">South Village LLLC</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A low-profit limited liability corporation established for South Village to lease land, serve as the homeowners association, and manage a stewardship fund for conservation efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="City of South Burlington">
      <data key="d0">City of South Burlington</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The municipal government of South Burlington, which granted a density bonus to the South Village developers in exchange for more affordable housing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prairie Crossing">
      <data key="d0">Prairie Crossing</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A conservation-oriented community in northern Illinois cited as an example of a development that includes agriculture and uses a real estate transfer tax for funding.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Northern Illinois">
      <data key="d0">Northern Illinois</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The geographical region where the Prairie Crossing community is located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hidden Springs">
      <data key="d0">Hidden Springs</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A conservation-oriented community in Boise, Idaho, mentioned as an example that uses a real estate transfer tax.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Water Management">
      <data key="d0">Water Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A critical factor in farm planning, concerning the sources of water (wells, ponds, rain) and the methods of distribution (irrigation, sprinklers, hoses) for crops and livestock.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Customer Amenities">
      <data key="d0">Customer Amenities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Features that enhance the customer experience to increase the customer base and profit, such as shaded rest areas, picnic spots, various food and drink options (pies, cider, hot chocolate), restrooms, and shopping bags.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Heirloom Apples">
      <data key="d0">Heirloom Apples</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific example of a crop enterprise. They are noted as being in high demand due to their superior flavor, making them a potentially profitable choice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chicken Pullets">
      <data key="d0">Chicken Pullets</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of livestock enterprise, specifically ready-to-lay chickens. They are mentioned as an option for a quick return, as they can begin laying eggs within a week of delivery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Farm Financial Planning">
      <data key="d0">Farm Financial Planning</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A critical business process for a farm enterprise. It involves creating a cash-flow budget, making short- and long-term projections, and calculating costs and potential returns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Start-up Costs">
      <data key="d0">Start-up Costs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The initial expenses required to begin a new farm enterprise. These include fees for permits, money for regulatory compliance, and the cost of acquiring seed, livestock, and equipment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Start-up Capital">
      <data key="d0">Start-up Capital</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The initial investment money needed to fund a new farm enterprise. The text emphasizes the importance of knowing how much capital is needed and how soon a return can be generated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Crop Protection Insurance">
      <data key="d0">Crop Protection Insurance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific type of insurance to protect against crop loss. The text notes that it is often harder to secure at a reasonable cost for alternative crops compared to traditional ones.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Boise, Idaho">
      <data key="d0">Boise, Idaho</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The city and state where the Hidden Springs community is located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serenbe">
      <data key="d0">Serenbe</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A conservation community in Georgia, near Atlanta, mentioned as an example of a development featuring agriculture as a primary amenity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Atlanta">
      <data key="d0">Atlanta</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A major city in Georgia near which the Serenbe community is located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Village Homes">
      <data key="d0">Village Homes</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A housing development described as being immersed in a garden where pesticides are forbidden. It serves as an example of including food production in neighborhood design.&lt;SEP&gt;An iconic green development from the 1970s in Davis, California, known for its extensive agricultural features like gardens, a vineyard, an orchard, and commercially harvested trees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Davis, California">
      <data key="d0">Davis, California</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The city and state where the Village Homes neighborhood is located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Burlington, Vermont">
      <data key="d0">Burlington, Vermont</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Burlington, Vermont, is a city described as a bastion of progressivity. It is home to The Intervale, an agricultural haven and a model for urban farming located within the city limits that serves the local population. Additionally, the South Village development is situated near the city, and Burlington is the location of the Gardener's Supply Company.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfd05a12ef78763e74306325feeb5eac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d83e7f9383ec8baa65b1a2fc070b1acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57c24510274e9c9fcb046e6b604285fd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740848</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Start-up Time">
      <data key="d0">Start-up Time</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A critical factor in the success of a farm, referring to the specific year or time an enterprise is launched. Starting in a bad year, like a drought, is warned against as it can cause great financial stress.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-766988b011c2a15c7312ce3e9bb55cf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Drought Years of 1953 and 1954">
      <data key="d0">Drought Years of 1953 and 1954</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A period of severe drought that caused great financial stress to farmers, used as an example of a bad time to start or expand a farming operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rural Crises of the 1980s">
      <data key="d0">Rural Crises of the 1980s</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A period of economic hardship in rural areas that caused significant financial stress to farmers, cited as an example of a difficult time to start in agriculture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conventional Farming">
      <data key="d0">Conventional Farming</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A farming method characterized by high-volume production with a low margin of profit, using any means possible to increase yields.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Management-intensive Grazing">
      <data key="d0">Management-intensive Grazing</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific production method for livestock that farmers are encouraged to consider. It involves carefully managing grazing patterns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="A New Farmer">
      <data key="d0">A New Farmer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An anonymous farmer mentioned as a cautionary example. This individual attempted to start a vegetable operation in July during a dry year without access to water, became discouraged, and quit farming, illustrating the importance of proper timing and planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Farm Infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">Farm Infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The physical structures and installations necessary for farming. The text mentions fencing, buildings, greenhouses, tunnels, and cloches as key components of infrastructure that need to be planned and built.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Soil Health">
      <data key="d0">Soil Health</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A central theme and indicator of success for the Innisfree project. It is measured by factors like soil carbon content, porosity, and water infiltration, and is improved through techniques like keyline subsoiling and the use of cover crops.&lt;SEP&gt;The condition and quality of the farm's soil. The text outlines several practices to improve soil health, such as conducting soil tests, gathering fertilizers like manure and leaves, starting compost heaps, and planting fall cover crops.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e066d43dafd3f92b15fb06eb4836e7c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740867</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Foundations">
      <data key="d0">Foundations</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A type of non-profit organization that provides funding. The legal structure of South Village was designed to make it possible for foundations to provide financial support through program-related investments."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Idaho">
      <data key="d0">Idaho</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">"A state in the United States mentioned as the location of the Hidden Springs conservation community in Boise."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"The state where the conservation group Lava Lake Land and Livestock is based."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f1544f96bf3906c3ffd91d3f551a278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1fa8277818b65f8d3d6665242021ad9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P-Patch Community Gardening Program">
      <data key="d0">P-Patch Community Gardening Program</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">"A community gardening program run by the Department of Neighborhoods in Seattle, WA. Its representative is Rich MacDonald."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Seattle's community gardening program, also known as the 'P-Patch Program,' which manages garden plots in over 70 locations for more than two thousand residents. It is city-supported and cultivates volunteer leadership.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Picardo Farm">
      <data key="d0">Picardo Farm</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A farm purchased by the city of Seattle in 1973, from which the 'P-Patch' program derives its name.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Jim Diers">
      <data key="d0">Jim Diers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Author of the book 'Neighborhood Power: Building Community the Seattle Way', which focuses on community building in Seattle.&lt;SEP&gt;The former director of the Seattle Department of Neighborhoods, who articulated the various community benefits provided by Seattle's community gardens program.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62dde44a553987a2d4deba0864e69eeb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Seattle Department of Neighborhoods">
      <data key="d0">Seattle Department of Neighborhoods</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A city department in Seattle, formerly led by Jim Diers, involved in community initiatives like the P-Patch program.&lt;SEP&gt;A municipal department in Seattle, Washington, that manages the P-Patch Community Garden Program, as detailed in its 2009 and 2010 fact sheets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62dde44a553987a2d4deba0864e69eeb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740817</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Richard MacDonald">
      <data key="d0">Richard MacDonald</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Richard MacDonald is the manager and supervisor of Seattle's P-Patch program. He oversees the management of the program and its volunteer leaders, emphasizing the importance of city support for community gardening. To ensure the viability of new projects, MacDonald requires that any proposal for a new community garden come from a group of committed leaders, not a single individual. He advises that a group of at least five or six people is necessary to start a new garden and works with these groups to develop a strategy. Furthermore, he believes the city's market-gardening program could be expanded if its pilot project is successful.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174591c0f94ab01a05c96941979500a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-959e33ece6a9fc720452b33659ca7996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f097aee6be0e05076e0e695419438a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Enterprise Integration">
      <data key="d0">Enterprise Integration</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A key concept in farm planning where different enterprises (crops and livestock) are chosen to support each other, reduce costs, and improve the overall health and productivity of the farm, as illustrated by the hogs and corn example.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Labor Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Labor Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A critical factor in planning a new farm enterprise. The text uses berries as an example of a crop with high labor requirements and discusses how models like U-pick operations can manage this factor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Production Method">
      <data key="d0">Production Method</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The overarching approach to raising crops and livestock. The text prompts farmers to consider and choose between various methods, including conventional, sustainable, natural, and organic, based on costs, yield, and market potential.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Marketing Program">
      <data key="d0">Marketing Program</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A crucial component of a farm's business plan. The text advises farmers to plan their marketing by considering how much they will sell, the number of customers needed, and whether a market already exists or needs to be developed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Farmer">
      <data key="d0">The Farmer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Represents the individual or family running the farm enterprise. This person is responsible for making key decisions regarding labor, machinery, marketing, pricing, and overall business strategy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Agricultural Machinery">
      <data key="d0">Agricultural Machinery</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Refers to the equipment needed for a farming enterprise, such as rototillers and tractors. The text emphasizes considering alternatives like renting or bartering and ensuring the farm's production volume justifies the investment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="University Or Extension Personnel">
      <data key="d0">University Or Extension Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Academic or government-affiliated experts who provide research, management support, and specialized knowledge about specific crops or animals to farmers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Laura Lawson">
      <data key="d0">Laura Lawson</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An author of a PhD dissertation from the University of California at Berkeley, cited by Iris Zippora Ahronowitz.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of the book 'City Bountiful', whose research is cited as evidence that community gardens thrive with government support.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62dde44a553987a2d4deba0864e69eeb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Southside Community Land Trust">
      <data key="d0">Southside Community Land Trust</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Southside Community Land Trust (SCLT), founded in 1981 in Providence, Rhode Island, is a neighborhood land trust and community partnership focused on community development through urban agriculture. Located at 109 Somerset Street in Providence, with Katherine Brown as its representative, SCLT is cited as a successful model for supporting community gardening without direct local government involvement. The organization serves a diverse population by managing numerous community gardens and operating "City Farm," an educational farm and community agriculture project. Additionally, the Southside Community Land Trust is recognized for its work in training new farmers through its farmer incubator programs, which feature term-limited four-year internships that include both farm and business training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170afca78fc7741f470417682836f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c38b37fe24e15bfa43a713c9e38509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62dde44a553987a2d4deba0864e69eeb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust">
      <data key="d0">South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust (SELROSLT) is a non-profit organization and community partnership located in Boston, MA, that was founded in 1991. Its primary mission is to acquire, own, improve, and maintain open spaces like community gardens and pocket parks in the South End and Lower Roxbury neighborhoods, having acquired its gardens from the city. SELROSLT is focused on protecting its land in perpetuity and is considered a successful model for supporting community gardening, with its long-term stability seen as crucial for the preservation of these green spaces. The organization protects 16 gardens, hosts the annual South End Garden Tour, and its representative is Betsy Johnson.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170afca78fc7741f470417682836f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd762b4d6c9647db05924d3e745a6991</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="World Wars I and II">
      <data key="d0">World Wars I and II</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Historical periods cited by Laura Lawson's research during which community gardens flourished due to support from federal and local governments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="City Bountiful">
      <data key="d0">City Bountiful</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A book written by Laura Lawson. Its research is cited as evidence that community gardens thrive when supported by federal and local governments, and decline when that support is withdrawn.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Citizen Leadership">
      <data key="d0">Citizen Leadership</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A management strategy utilized by the P-Patch program where volunteer residents are trained and cultivated to manage garden operations, maintenance, and community events, thereby increasing the program's civic capacity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P-Patch Gardeners">
      <data key="d0">P-Patch Gardeners</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The over two thousand participants in Seattle's P-Patch program. Demographics show 55% are low-income, 48% live in multi-family dwellings, and 77% have no other garden space. They are required to volunteer and collectively donate over 10 tons of food to food banks annually.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Farm Enterprise">
      <data key="d0">Farm Enterprise</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The overall farming business operation being planned. Its success depends on careful consideration of labor, machinery, industry support, marketing, and the farmer's own experience.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Crops And Livestock">
      <data key="d0">Crops And Livestock</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The products generated by the farm enterprise. The text suggests that having a variety of crops and livestock can help reduce a farmer's risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Industry Support">
      <data key="d0">Industry Support</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The network of resources available to a farmer, which includes access to plants, seeds, breeding stock, research, and expert personnel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Area Farmers And Associations">
      <data key="d0">Area Farmers And Associations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Local groups of farmers and agricultural associations that can be consulted for expert advice and support.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competition">
      <data key="d0">Competition</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A business and economic concept listed in the index as a factor for consideration in farming.&lt;SEP&gt;Refers to other farms in the region (within a 25, 50, or 100-mile radius) that are engaged in a similar enterprise. A farmer must analyze their marketing methods and sales volume.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4725469cd4458c0f5eeeefdfccd30dd9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Route Sales">
      <data key="d0">Route Sales</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A marketing method where products are delivered along a regular route to businesses or other customers. The text suggests combining this with other errands to lower costs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Local Stores">
      <data key="d0">Local Stores</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Potential buyers for farm products. However, their ability to buy from local farmers may be limited if their purchasing decisions are tied to an out-of-state headquarters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contract Selling">
      <data key="d0">Contract Selling</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A sales method that locks in a sales price with a buyer. The text warns that clauses for grades and quality are often subject to discount, making it a risky option.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-097e0f884a6200b04603c0d37b1e67fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rhode Island">
      <data key="d0">Rhode Island</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">"A state in the New England region of the United States."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A US state mentioned as a location that has some of the most prominent community garden land trusts, alongside cities like Philadelphia and Chicago.&lt;SEP&gt;The state where the Southside Community Land Trust is located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc825bb5fbec77abff4a02be6fc5fcec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
