    </node>
    <node id="MacDonald">
      <data key="d0">MacDonald</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A city staff member who explains the strategies for assisting community gardens, noting that support varies based on the neighborhood's resources and challenges. MacDonald also mentions the use of AmeriCorps volunteers for low-resource groups.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Benjamin Chrisinger">
      <data key="d0">Benjamin Chrisinger</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Benjamin Chrisinger is a researcher credited with contributing information and research for several topics. His contributions include research on the Warren Wilson College Farm, the 'Farm to College Movements', Nuestras Raíces, and the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust. Additionally, Benjamin Chrisinger is mentioned as having a connection to Boston.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0809b82d4ca6415545d8263dbdcfcf73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f8baa196ceabfc9bc0a6cc79c04127e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d971c6976ab8e71370d85b346b00f467</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AmeriCorps">
      <data key="d0">AmeriCorps</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Based on the information provided, AmeriCorps is a U.S. federal government program dedicated to national and public service. It functions as a service organization that places individuals in jobs to address community needs across various sectors, including education, public safety, health, and the environment. The organization encompasses several programs, such as Vista, NCCC, and FoodCorps, which is a branch of AmeriCorps.

AmeriCorps members and volunteers are involved in numerous community projects, with a particular focus on food and gardening initiatives. For example, the organization provides up to six staff members to help run the Beardsley Community Farm and fills a full-time garden teacher position at the Abernethy school, where its members also developed a standards-aligned garden curriculum. Its volunteers provide mentoring and support at the City Seeds Urban Farm alongside Gateway Greening staff, assist low-resource groups like school and church youth groups with starting and maintaining gardens, and are encouraged to prioritize relationship-building. An AmeriCorps summer project focused on gleaning was also featured as a case study in the USDA's "A Citizen's Guide to Food Recovery." Additionally, AmeriCorps maintains strong partnerships with other organizations, such as Janus Youth, providing volunteers for their programs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38c9174dd4002f6529026fc7fd3c23f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0809b82d4ca6415545d8263dbdcfcf73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c46a7f814f9b988da76a9ac71bdab30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aab30ee2b8630558ddd6575d42c69264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d3d51c80e398fde0d7a70a89888fa0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a81765c57d711272f41bff8f406f472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e716e5bd5f06009e0468b77709b834d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79fcf59d7b63a10ed28124a2923fc0f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a815073ae837fa29833af41e55990ca</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Boston Architectural College">
      <data key="d0">Boston Architectural College</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An educational institution whose design-build class collaborated with the gardeners of the Worcester Street Community Garden to design a garden pavilion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South End">
      <data key="d0">South End</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A historic and diverse neighborhood in Boston, Massachusetts. It is one of the primary areas served by the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust and the location of the annual garden tour.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lower Roxbury">
      <data key="d0">Lower Roxbury</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A historic and diverse neighborhood in Boston, Massachusetts, and one of the two main areas served by the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust.&lt;SEP&gt;A neighborhood mentioned as the site of the small but productive Bessie Barnes garden. Historically, it was also the location of the first recorded school garden in the U.S. in 1891.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43ebc646508b0f93fb43f529856b4d56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chinatown">
      <data key="d0">Chinatown</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A neighborhood in Boston whose residents tend many of the plots in the nearby Berkeley Street Community Garden.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deborah Lemmer">
      <data key="d0">Deborah Lemmer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Deborah Lemmer is a marketer from Shaggy Shagbark Acres in Michigan. She is described as 'canny' and is known for demonstrating the process of spinning fiber directly from a live angora rabbit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Shaggy Shagbark Acres">
      <data key="d0">Shaggy Shagbark Acres</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Shaggy Shagbark Acres is a farm located in Michigan, operated by or associated with Deborah Lemmer. It is involved in raising fiber animals like angora rabbits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Michigan">
      <data key="d0">Michigan</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A US state that is home to the Michigan Integrated Food and Farming Systems, an organization dedicated to farmer support.&lt;SEP&gt;Michigan is a US state and the location of Shaggy Shagbark Acres, the farm mentioned in the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4725469cd4458c0f5eeeefdfccd30dd9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South Africa">
      <data key="d0">South Africa</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">South Africa is the country of origin for Boer goats, which are described as a prized but expensive breed of meat goat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Elk, Deer, And Bison">
      <data key="d0">Elk, Deer, And Bison</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Elk, deer, and bison are an enterprise category known for low-fat, high-protein meat. This enterprise requires a large initial investment. Products include meat, medicinal velvet from antlers, hides, and breeding stock.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Game Birds">
      <data key="d0">Game Birds</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"Game birds are a category of bird, mentioned alongside poultry, that can be processed at home according to state regulations."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Game birds are an enterprise category including pheasants and quail. They can be raised for breeding stock, meat, or for hunting purposes, with sales channels to restaurants, grocery stores, and hunters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab58b310c0ccf38821b52ac8254aeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Camelids">
      <data key="d0">Camelids</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of animals that includes llamas and alpacas, primarily raised for their fiber and for breeding markets. There is no significant meat market for them.&lt;SEP&gt;A family of animals, such as llamas and alpacas, mentioned in the index as a livestock category.&lt;SEP&gt;Camelids are an enterprise category including llamas and alpacas. They are primarily used for their fiber and for selling breeding stock. Llamas are also used as pack animals and as guard animals for sheep.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4725469cd4458c0f5eeeefdfccd30dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9d28e4a28ca972c9e289441c78c0be</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Boer Goats">
      <data key="d0">Boer Goats</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Boer goats are a specific, prized, and expensive breed of meat goat originating from South Africa. They are mentioned as a good option for crossbreeding.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e9fc423425c82be2483c04c11e6577f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South End Garden Tour">
      <data key="d0">South End Garden Tour</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The signature annual fundraising event for the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust. It has run for at least eighteen years and takes participants through various private and public gardens in Boston's South End.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Land Trust">
      <data key="d0">Land Trust</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A Land Trust is a non-profit organization that works to conserve land. The text uses two examples, SELROSLT and SCLT, to illustrate how land trusts can be used as a primary strategy to secure long-term protection for urban community gardens.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanism for preserving open space in perpetuity. The South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust is presented as a prime example of using a land trust to protect community gardens.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of organization that protects land from development by purchasing it, using long-term leases, or holding conservation easements. They can be national, regional, or local, with goals specific to their community. They are an important but underutilized tool for preserving community gardens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170afca78fc7741f470417682836f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Worcester Street Community Garden">
      <data key="d0">Worcester Street Community Garden</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific community garden project mentioned in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the 16 gardens protected by the SELROSLT. It is a large, neatly laid out garden with 110 plots, raised beds, and a distinctive abstract pavilion designed in collaboration with the Boston Architectural College.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38c9174dd4002f6529026fc7fd3c23f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Berkeley Street Community Garden">
      <data key="d0">Berkeley Street Community Garden</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Described as the 'queen' of the 16 gardens, this is one of the largest community gardens in Boston, with over 150 plots. Located near Chinatown, it is known for its intensive, three-dimensional growing systems created by gardeners.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="West Springfield Community Garden">
      <data key="d0">West Springfield Community Garden</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">One of the gardens protected by the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust, described as an 'explosion of vegetables and flowers'. It was founded by a neighborhood community development corporation for its tenants.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lenox/Kendall Community Garden">
      <data key="d0">Lenox/Kendall Community Garden</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A large open space garden protected by the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust, characterized by the predominance of collards and kale. It is gardened mostly by African-American community members.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bessie Barnes Community Garden">
      <data key="d0">Bessie Barnes Community Garden</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A 'working landscape' garden protected by the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust, featuring barbecue grills, tools, and pots.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bessie Barnes Memorial Park">
      <data key="d0">Bessie Barnes Memorial Park</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A garden protected by the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust, located near the Bessie Barnes Community Garden. It offers a mini-haven of Oriental design for quiet meditation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48fec31f78ae747d4c7614c6c15fff42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dexter Cattle">
      <data key="d0">Dexter Cattle</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Dexter Cattle is a small breed of cattle suggested as a potential enterprise, especially for farmers looking into direct markets or less common breeds.</data>
