    <node id="Garden Tour">
      <data key="d0">Garden Tour</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An annual signature fund-raising event for SELROSLT, in its eighteenth year in 2011. It takes participants through private and public gardens in Boston's South End to educate and inspire them about gardening.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Boston's South End">
      <data key="d0">Boston's South End</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A neighborhood in Boston, Massachusetts, which is the location of the annual Garden Tour. It is part of the area served by SELROSLT.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SELROSLT">
      <data key="d0">SELROSLT</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An organization that manages the Worcester Street Garden. It organized the replacement of toxic railroad tie raised beds with donated bluestone by securing volunteers.&lt;SEP&gt;Referred to as the South End/Lower Roxbury land trust, SELROSLT is an organization that manages 16 gardens in the area, dealing with policy issues such as the allocation of multiple plots to individual gardeners.&lt;SEP&gt;The South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust is a neighborhood-based nonprofit land trust that preserves community gardens from development. It operates on a small budget of $50,000 entirely with volunteers and was formed in response to development pressures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-603aed086b5eda0ec62eae7fa8c0f1b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf60421969007759eb279ddb028ec67b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South End/Lower Roxbury">
      <data key="d0">South End/Lower Roxbury</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">South End/Lower Roxbury is a diverse geographical area and community in Boston that has experienced significant urban renewal projects and is currently facing gentrification. In response to empty spaces left by urban renewal, residents established numerous community gardens, including a notable one on Worcester Street. To preserve these gardens from development pressures, community gardeners organized to form the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust (SELROSLT). This land trust now manages and protects the community gardens while also advocating for affordable housing. Additionally, the South End/Lower Roxbury area is located in proximity to the Fenway Victory Garden, one of the last surviving gardens from the World War II era.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-603aed086b5eda0ec62eae7fa8c0f1b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170afca78fc7741f470417682836f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43ebc646508b0f93fb43f529856b4d56</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
