    <node id="Betsy Johnson">
      <data key="d0">Betsy Johnson</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Betsy Johnson is a cofounder and the director of the South End/Lower Roxbury Open Space Land Trust (SELROSLT), for which she also serves as a representative. A knowledgeable expert on the organization, she provides commentary on its history, formation, challenges like threats of eminent domain, and key success factors such as organizational stability. Johnson also highlights the practical importance of keeping gardens looking good year-round to maintain broad community support. Additionally, she is the former president and interim executive director of the American Community Gardening Association (ACGA). In this capacity, she is a strong advocate for community gardens, providing expert estimates on their numbers nationwide and arguing that they serve as important catalysts for other community food projects and social development, beyond just food production. Johnson has also been acknowledged for helping authors identify successful projects to serve as models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a170afca78fc7741f470417682836f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04d6e50411798e18bdf72f9c1734a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa8b612642fa385d2af41e902aa75d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07f097aee6be0e05076e0e695419438a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
