    </node>
    <node id="Urban Renewal">
      <data key="d0">Urban Renewal</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A period of city development policy in the 1960s in South End/Lower Roxbury where blighted properties were torn down with unfulfilled promises of rebuilding. This event created the empty spaces that later became community gardens and spurred the eventual formation of SELROSLT.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The City of Boston">
      <data key="d0">The City of Boston</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The municipal government entity that owned land in the South End/Lower Roxbury. In 1986, its redevelopment plan to bulldoze a community garden for an affordable housing project acted as the catalyst for gardeners and housing advocates to organize and form SELROSLT.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Housing Advocates">
      <data key="d0">Public Housing Advocates</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A group in South End/Lower Roxbury that was appalled by the city's development plans and joined forces with community gardeners to form a coalition, agreeing that both community gardens and affordable housing should be preserved.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pasture, Hay, and Cover Crops">
      <data key="d0">Pasture, Hay, and Cover Crops</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of crops essential for integrating livestock and other enterprises on a farm. While their direct market potential is low (except for baled hay), they are a necessary component of the farm ecosystem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb9d28e4a28ca972c9e289441c78c0be</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
