    <node id="Public Outrage and Media">
      <data key="d0">Public Outrage and Media</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The collective community and media response in New York City in 1999 when the city threatened to auction off 114 community gardens. This pressure was instrumental in leading to the deal where The Trust for Public Land and the New York Restoration Project saved the gardens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
