    <node id="Obesity">
      <data key="d0">Obesity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A major public health issue in the U.S. that is the subject of reports from the Department of Health and Human Services, CDC data, and news articles on city and state trends, such as in Alabama.&lt;SEP&gt;A public health issue discussed as a consequence of modern food systems, with reports from the CDC and articles by Bryan Walsh linking it to the economics of food.&lt;SEP&gt;A public health issue that the Los Angeles Neighborhood Land Trust (LANLT) aims to address through the creation of community gardens, which promote healthier eating and outdoor activity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0b1f6adc63dbe7f3160ab5bd7b25233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c0dfef7989eab5ae8b58770f9786cac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bdeb1a250cfa50c7c4dce2c38964661</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
    <node id="City of Boston">
      <data key="d0">City of Boston</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A municipal government that partners with the Food Project to implement the 'Bounty Bucks' program, aiming to make healthy food more available in the city.&lt;SEP&gt;The City of Boston is the municipal government that initially planned redevelopment threatening community gardens in 1986. After community pressure, it was forced to reconsider and eventually transferred ownership of eight gardens to SELROSLT for $1 each in 1991.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a170afca78fc7741f470417682836f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b688540c900515c3ef10df531de83587</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740819</data>
    </node>
