    <node id="Sweet Corn">
      <data key="d0">Sweet Corn</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A heavy nitrogen-feeding crop used in Dick Raymond's 2-year rotation. It is planted in the second year to take advantage of the nitrogen fixed by the previous year's peas and beans."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A crop used as an example to illustrate the importance of timeliness in farming. It has a very short one- to two-day harvest window for perfect quality, requiring careful planning like staggered planting.&lt;SEP&gt;A crop with agricultural economic data provided per acre, including a gross income of $1,363.00, total variable costs of $705.00, a net profit of $658.00, and requiring 71 labor hours.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee261677ef65b4f0bf53fae46bfcfb75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-473f8348a15ba74f2e21ca4cc96c583e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04b17869172fff33b1c7bc2284173657</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
