    </node>
    <node id="Beardsley Community Farm">
      <data key="d0">Beardsley Community Farm</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Beardsley Community Farm is an urban demonstration garden and established community agricultural project located in Knoxville, Tennessee. Founded in 1998, the farm's mission is to promote food security in low-income communities through education, sustainability, and community empowerment. To achieve this, it grows produce, raises bees and chickens, and offers educational programs on topics like gardening and food preservation. The farm is operated by a farm manager, AmeriCorps staff, and a notable volunteer force of over a thousand people, which it successfully recruits through effective branding and community outreach. As an established project, Beardsley Community Farm also advises new agricultural projects on long-term planning and knowledge sharing to avoid common pitfalls. The farm's listed representatives include former manager Ben Epperson and John Harris. It has also faced challenges, including vandalism of its apple orchard and blueberries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0809b82d4ca6415545d8263dbdcfcf73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d3d51c80e398fde0d7a70a89888fa0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfd05a12ef78763e74306325feeb5eac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Megan Bucknum">
      <data key="d0">Megan Bucknum</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Megan Bucknum is an environmental and food systems planner who serves as the Farm to School program associate at Fair Food Philadelphia. An alumna of the University of Virginia, where she was a graduate student, she formerly worked for the Wallace Center. Megan Bucknum contributed to a book as a researcher and writer and is credited as the co-author of the sections describing the Appalachian Center for Economic Networks (ACEnet) and the Beardsley Community Farm. She is also mentioned in the book's index.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0809b82d4ca6415545d8263dbdcfcf73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062d9ac74f75199c91576d982ab5a9f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa8b612642fa385d2af41e902aa75d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efae0d6c5dabc751b9ceb56518857dff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Soil Remediation">
      <data key="d0">Soil Remediation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A critical foundational activity for new urban gardens, involving improving soil quality, which may need to be done for a full year before growing produce."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The process of reducing or neutralizing contaminants in soil. The text discusses methods researched by The Food Project, such as using hyperaccumulator plants, adjusting soil pH, and using compost to bind lead.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfd05a12ef78763e74306325feeb5eac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safe Gardening Practices">
      <data key="d0">Safe Gardening Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A set of guidelines recommended by The Food Project to limit exposure to lead in contaminated soils. These practices include working with moist soil, wearing gloves, and washing hands and produce.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Northeast Regional Agricultural Engineering Services">
      <data key="d0">Northeast Regional Agricultural Engineering Services</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Northeast Regional Agricultural Engineering Services is a department at Cornell University cited for its publication, 'Used Farm Equipment', which emphasizes minimizing machinery costs to maximize profits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harold Tucker">
      <data key="d0">Harold Tucker</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Harold Tucker is the lubricants technical director at Phillips 66 Company. He is cited as an expert providing tips on the proper methods for winterizing and storing farm machinery after the harvest season.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Phillips 66 Company">
      <data key="d0">Phillips 66 Company</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Phillips 66 Company is a division of Phillips Petroleum. Its lubricants technical director, Harold Tucker, provides expertise on machinery maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Phillips Petroleum">
      <data key="d0">Phillips Petroleum</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Phillips Petroleum is a company located in Bartlesville, OK, and is the parent company of Phillips 66 Company.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bartlesville, Ok">
      <data key="d0">Bartlesville, Ok</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Bartlesville, OK is a location mentioned as the home of Phillips Petroleum company.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Economics Of Machinery">
      <data key="d0">Economics Of Machinery</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">'Economics of Machinery' is a major topic in the text, covering the principle of buying necessary machinery at the best price and ensuring its longevity through faithful maintenance. It includes discussions on machinery costs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Machinery Costs">
      <data key="d0">Machinery Costs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">'Machinery Costs' is a key concept discussed in the text, defined as a fixed cost of production. It is broken down into two types: ownership (fixed) costs and operating costs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ownership Costs">
      <data key="d0">Ownership Costs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">'Ownership Costs' are a type of machinery cost, also called fixed costs. They accrue regardless of equipment use and include depreciation, taxes, insurance, interest on loans, and storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Also referred to as fixed costs, this is a category of expenses associated with owning machinery. The text explains these costs as a percentage of the equipment's price, influenced by interest rates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community HANDS Project">
      <data key="d0">Community HANDS Project</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A program created by People's Grocery that focuses on nutrition education. Participants can become paid health and nutrition demonstrators who offer demonstrations to the wider community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Grub Box Program">
      <data key="d0">Grub Box Program</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) program offered by People's Grocery in partnership with Dig Deep Farms. It provides boxes of fresh produce to customers and is a key component of the 'Bite to Balance' case study.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="East Oakland">
      <data key="d0">East Oakland</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A geographical area in Oakland, California, where Highland Hospital, the nearest public hospital to West Oakland, is located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Food Deserts">
      <data key="d0">Food Deserts</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A term for areas with limited access to affordable and nutritious food. A neighborhood in Knoxville was identified as a major food desert, which was the primary motivation for creating the community farm."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;An area with limited access to affordable and nutritious food. A 1997 community assessment in Knoxville identified a neighborhood as a food desert, which spurred community action.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Food Assessment of Knoxville">
      <data key="d0">Community Food Assessment of Knoxville</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"A specific study conducted in 1997 that identified a food desert in Knoxville. The findings from this assessment were the direct catalyst for the creation of the Beardsley Community Farm."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A study conducted in 1997 that identified a major food desert in a Knoxville neighborhood, which served as a catalyst for the establishment of community food initiatives like the Beardsley Community Farm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8186cf72c91110756ec67bcc379a67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Knox County Community Action Committee (CAC)">
      <data key="d0">Knox County Community Action Committee (CAC)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">"A committee that was given park land by the city of Knoxville to build a community farm. It received funding from the USDA, runs the 'Green Thumb' program, and manages the Beardsley Community Farm."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The Knox County Community Action Committee (CAC) is an organization mentioned in the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c9669112f71f37c0273243e8cc59e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="United States Department of Agriculture (USDA)">
      <data key="d0">United States Department of Agriculture (USDA)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">"A federal department that provided funding to the Knox County Community Action Committee (CAC) to build a greenhouse for the community farm project."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Green Thumb Program">
      <data key="d0">Green Thumb Program</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A program created by the CAC to promote home gardening among low-income families by providing plants, soil, tools, and gardening assistance."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Postseason Shut-Down">
      <data key="d0">Postseason Shut-Down</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">'Postseason Shut-Down' is a process of winterizing machinery after the harvest. The steps include cleaning the engine and equipment, removing residual crops, changing oil, and lubrication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Used Farm Equipment">
      <data key="d0">Used Farm Equipment</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">'Used Farm Equipment' is the title of a publication from the Northeast Regional Agricultural Engineering Services at Cornell University. It provides guidance on minimizing machinery costs to maximize profits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harvest">
      <data key="d0">Harvest</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A crucial seasonal farming event. The text emphasizes that machinery should be overhauled, cleaned, and lubricated immediately after the harvest to prevent corrosion and damage during storage.&lt;SEP&gt;The harvest is a key annual farming event mentioned in the text. The use of specific machinery, like a combine, is often limited to this period, and post-harvest procedures like 'Postseason Shut-Down' are critical.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Government">
      <data key="d0">Government</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The government is an entity that imposes various fees, referred to as taxes (property, sales, income, Social Security), which are considered part of the ownership costs of farm machinery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Depreciation">
      <data key="d0">Depreciation</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"Depreciation is an accounting concept described as spreading the cost of an asset over its lifespan. The text advises setting aside an amount equal to the annual depreciation of machinery to build a cash reserve for its eventual replacement."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Depreciation is an ownership (or fixed) cost of machinery. It represents the decrease in the machinery's value over time, regardless of usage, and is an amount that should be set aside for future replacement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea8dd630733dc61f911a635a9b8f0c7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Taxes">
      <data key="d0">Taxes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A fixed cost mentioned in the text that is not included in the primary machinery cost formulas but must be added to determine the true total cost per acre for operating equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;Taxes are a type of ownership cost for machinery, imposed by the government. The text lists property, sales, income, and Social Security taxes as examples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Insurance">
      <data key="d0">Insurance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Insurance is an ownership cost for facilities and equipment, described as a form of risk management against potential business-ending events like fire, theft, or flood.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Interest">
      <data key="d0">Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Interest is an ownership cost that applies if a loan is taken out to buy machinery. The text advises carefully evaluating if the equipment's benefit justifies this added expense.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="John Harris">
      <data key="d0">John Harris</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">"The director of the CAC's Green Thumb program who emphasizes the importance of community presence and branding for the success of the Beardsley Community Farm."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A representative of Beardsley Community Farm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d3d51c80e398fde0d7a70a89888fa0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="University of Tennessee">
      <data key="d0">University of Tennessee</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">"A university that partners with the Beardsley Community Farm, assisting with its annual fundraisers."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Farm Fests">
      <data key="d0">Farm Fests</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"Popular festivals hosted by the Beardsley Community Farm to attract local residents. These events feature carnival-like activities, music, and educational components about food and agriculture."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
