    <node id="World-Wide Opportunities on Organic Farms (WWOOF)">
      <data key="d0">World-Wide Opportunities on Organic Farms (WWOOF)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">"An organization that facilitates internships on organic farms. Gladheart Farms uses WWOOF to find interns."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization that provides a network through which Gladheart Farms finds and offers internships to individuals interested in organic farming."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Summer Leadership Program">
      <data key="d0">Summer Leadership Program</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A program run by Beardsley Community Farm that employs low-income teens (aged 15-17) using a government grant. The program focuses on building demonstration projects related to sustainability."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-488bc663aa4ded0ca40ac601222c065d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEEDS, Inc.">
      <data key="d0">SEEDS, Inc.</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">SEEDS, Inc. is a grassroots non-profit organization based in Durham, North Carolina, led by Executive Director Lucy Harris. The organization focuses on supporting urban youth through gardening, community development, and environmental education. SEEDS, Inc. founded and operates the Durham Inner-City Gardeners (DIG) program, and as part of its educational initiatives, it organizes trips to farms owned by African-Americans. The organization also advocates for properly valuing its volunteers and giving back to them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6376ac179a2df4bf1471d8fed5f7bc23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc2a008e21cba06a8a9ad6e540ff138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lucy Harris">
      <data key="d0">Lucy Harris</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">"A representative for SEEDS, INC."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"The executive director of SEEDS, Inc. in Durham, North Carolina. She argues that a major mistake organizations make is undervaluing volunteers and not giving them as much as they receive."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The executive director of SEEDS, Inc. She emphasizes the importance of the youth leaders' role in the hiring process for the DIG program and speaks about the positive impact the program has on the participants' diets and awareness of food origins.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc2a008e21cba06a8a9ad6e540ff138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Michelle">
      <data key="d0">Michelle</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">"The wife of Michael Porterfield, who provided support for his determination to find land and start Gladheart Farms."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Storage Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Storage Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Storage facilities are a component of ownership costs, especially if a new one must be built. Storing machinery properly out of the weather is highlighted as a key way to save on future costs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d20bcb040d48598530ec2b7c42edba7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Northeast Regional Agricultural Engineering Service">
      <data key="d0">Northeast Regional Agricultural Engineering Service</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An organization that provides predictions and data on the ownership costs of new and used farm equipment, such as tractors, based on factors like interest rates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Co-ops">
      <data key="d0">Co-ops</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A business model recommended for small farmers to aggregate their products, share costs, and gain access to larger markets. Examples like Niman Ranch, Coleman Natural, and Country Natural Beef are provided as successful models.&lt;SEP&gt;Agricultural cooperatives mentioned as entities that may have tight schedules or 'small windows of opportunity' for harvests, which is a factor to consider when deciding whether to own equipment or rely on custom services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operating Costs">
      <data key="d0">Operating Costs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Also known as variable costs, this is the category of expenses incurred from the actual use of machinery. These costs include fuel, oil, lubrication, filters, repairs, and maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Preventive Maintenance">
      <data key="d0">Preventive Maintenance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A set of proactive procedures and programs designed to prolong the life and efficiency of farm equipment. The text details numerous tasks such as changing oil, lubricating parts, cleaning, and regular inspections.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of scheduled activities recommended for farm equipment, such as changing oil, filters, transmission fluid, and antifreeze, to prolong equipment life and control costs. It is highlighted as a key controllable element during the growing season.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8cfe86ed3c97ccb7c9629ee2dac08b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Custom Rate">
      <data key="d0">Custom Rate</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A pricing structure for farming services performed by a third party (custom operations). The text suggests using custom rate sheets as a tool for making economic decisions by comparing them to the cost of owning and operating one's own equipment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Engine">
      <data key="d0">Engine</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A critical component of machinery mentioned in the context of maintenance. It is susceptible to damage from contaminants and corrosion, and its oil paths must be inspected during preseason start-up.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Oil">
      <data key="d0">Oil</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A crucial fluid for machinery operation and longevity. The text emphasizes the importance of changing oil after harvest, observing its condition for contaminants, and using it for long-term storage and lubrication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d2c2f40ce23609da02bb09b06c26efd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lynchburg, Virginia">
      <data key="d0">Lynchburg, Virginia</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Lynchburg, Virginia, is a city located in the state's southern Piedmont region. It is home to the non-profit organization and urban agricultural center, Lynchburg Grows. In May 2009, the organization hosted an event in the city, specifically a workshop that was conducted by Will Allen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c9669112f71f37c0273243e8cc59e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e0df78d09fb33ee041307abbce7d33e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c0dfef7989eab5ae8b58770f9786cac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a815073ae837fa29833af41e55990ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475015ec5f08648d774910da2fb23967</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Durham, North Carolina">
      <data key="d0">Durham, North Carolina</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Durham, North Carolina, is the city where the non-profit organization SEEDS, Inc. and its program, the Durham Inner-City Gardeners (DIG), are based. The DIG program specifically serves teenagers from the city's poor neighborhoods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-adc2a008e21cba06a8a9ad6e540ff138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6376ac179a2df4bf1471d8fed5f7bc23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8965f3e3965322fdf5c53aebddde1e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b79b32f16bacae95e48f2f51ab5dee0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Boston, Massachusetts">
      <data key="d0">Boston, Massachusetts</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">"The city where the non-profit organization The Food Project is located."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A metropolitan region where The Food Project operates. The text highlights the dynamic between its low-income inner-city neighborhoods, like Roxbury, and its wealthier suburbs.&lt;SEP&gt;The metropolitan region where The Food Project, another youth-focused food organization, operates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07d81959e2e7dfd429fb34ce74beae5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aab30ee2b8630558ddd6575d42c69264&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34</data>
