      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Volunteer Management">
      <data key="d0">Volunteer Management</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A central theme of the text, which provides advice and examples on how to successfully recruit, manage, value, and handle liability for volunteers in community organizations."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A key operational challenge for nonprofits. The Food Project is presented as an exemplary model in this area, successfully managing thousands of volunteers and creating a guide for others.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8965f3e3965322fdf5c53aebddde1e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740829</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Farming">
      <data key="d0">Community Farming</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"An agricultural model exemplified by the Intervale, which focuses on the close proximity of farms to foster collaboration, resource sharing, mutual aid, and a strong social community among farmers."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"The overarching category for the organizations discussed, which involve farms operating within or near cities, often on public land, and relying on community involvement, volunteers, and interns."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c977e0c22629a3b90f1214c2370c4394&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4daf18984831b8673c2be0060612bd34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
