    <node id="Local Initiative for Food Education (Philly LIFE)">
      <data key="d0">Local Initiative for Food Education (Philly LIFE)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Philly LIFE is a Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) program launched by Greensgrow in 2010. It is designed to provide food shares to low-income families by integrating with the federal SNAP system and includes a cooking class component.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6576c76d8821b0180981d641c63968e5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP)">
      <data key="d0">Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP)</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) is a U.S. federal government program that provides food-purchasing assistance to low-income individuals and families. Its benefits are compatible with other initiatives, such as the Philly LIFE program. Furthermore, SNAP benefits are utilized within the 'Bounty Bucks' initiative, which enables participants to double their purchasing power for fresh produce.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b688540c900515c3ef10df531de83587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6576c76d8821b0180981d641c63968e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38c9174dd4002f6529026fc7fd3c23f0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Malik Yakini">
      <data key="d0">Malik Yakini</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual named in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Malik Yakini is an activist from Detroit who is cited as an advocate for large-scale urban agriculture, suggesting that cities like Detroit could produce a significant percentage of their own food by converting vacant land into farms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38c9174dd4002f6529026fc7fd3c23f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6576c76d8821b0180981d641c63968e5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural-Foods Movement of the 1970s">
      <data key="d0">Natural-Foods Movement of the 1970s</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Natural-Foods Movement of the 1970s is a historical event mentioned by Mary Seton Corboy. She recalls it as a popular trend that eventually faded, expressing concern that the current local food movement could suffer a similar fate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6576c76d8821b0180981d641c63968e5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Feminism">
      <data key="d0">Feminism</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A social and political movement used by Corboy as an analogy. Its success, exemplified by laws like Title IX, led to its principles becoming so ingrained in society that the term itself can seem archaic."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Feminism is a social and political movement used by Mary Seton Corboy as an analogy. She hopes the principles of the local food movement will become as deeply ingrained in society as feminist principles have, citing Title IX as an example.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6576c76d8821b0180981d641c63968e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd762b4d6c9647db05924d3e745a6991</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Title IX">
      <data key="d0">Title IX</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A 1972 law cited as an example of a feminist achievement that guaranteed protection from gender-based discrimination in educational institutions, illustrating how a movement's goals can become standard practice."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Title IX is a 1972 federal law that prohibited gender-based discrimination in education. It is used by Mary Seton Corboy as a specific example of how a social movement's ideas (feminism) can become successfully integrated into law and society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6576c76d8821b0180981d641c63968e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd762b4d6c9647db05924d3e745a6991</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740833</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Local Senior Center">
      <data key="d0">Local Senior Center</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A local community hub where Greensgrow holds a special market to bring fresh produce to seniors who have difficulty traveling to the main farmers' market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6576c76d8821b0180981d641c63968e5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740833</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Morrison, Ia">
      <data key="d0">Morrison, Ia</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The city in Iowa where The Morrison Publishing is located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2920f4362eb05a4692fa915ca812b425</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740833</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Joel Salatin">
      <data key="d0">Joel Salatin</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Joel Salatin is the owner and visionary leader of Polyface Farm, a central figure in the local food movement, and a prominent advocate for sustainable agriculture. Described as a "firebrand" and a "Christian-libertarian-environmentalist-capitalist-lunatic," he is an author, farmer, and public speaker known for his outspoken criticism of industrial agriculture and government regulations favoring large-scale operations. Salatin champions bioregional, ethics-based food systems. He is focused on land healing through agricultural synergy. He developed sustainable and financially viable models for local food systems and new farmers, such as the "food cluster" concept and debt-free partnership models. Salatin is an innovator, famous for systems-oriented farming innovations like the Eggmobile, pastured egg production, using pigs to create pasture from forest lands and compost, and acorn finishing. His work, including rotational grazing of chickens and small-acreage farming, has been documented by Allan Nation and Mark Neuzil. Salatin is the author of "Pastured Poultry Profits," "You Can Farm," and "Salad Bar Beef." His farming methods, which emphasize community ecology, personal customer service, and seasonal work rhythms, have inspired others, including Jamie Ager. Salatin is also interested in scaling up his business by partnering with other farmers and maintains high quality. He discusses the challenges of scaling a farm without compromising its core values and family life. He was a key figure in establishing the partnership with Chipotle. His article on mob-stocking influenced the students on the Warren Wilson Farm crew.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8da1b16361a783bc112824aaa6fa12fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d31a2f89a77b64e0ae04120df1fdb3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3699752bc52dee1358ad76a26a9c6fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d6381862167ee0d108723409eae36d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f712d3550c8612228f9fb4dc999ba9b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2920f4362eb05a4692fa915ca812b425&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1bfb736a960a0ceee22d5eb6f8e955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c8f3e81fd6708a9852f46f0d4ac0a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab7679e841cce082d6f5f864896c9afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77562613f0c5d12383f7ffab65ce2e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e3df5ce7be88ffd8bdf29e5b896da3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd285deff310269197e8718b28f6076b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740857</data>
    </node>
