    <node id="Rosalie Karp">
      <data key="d0">Rosalie Karp</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Rosalie Karp is the advancement director for Janus Youth Programs, Inc., where she is responsible for writing grants and advancing the organization's mission. As a representative and staff member, Karp explains the organization's core philosophies, which are "strength-based"—emphasizing that all community members have valuable skills and talents—and centered on community ownership and collaborative decision-making. She works alongside Dennis Morrow and believes that communities can easily detect a lack of integrity in organizations that do not genuinely respect them. Karp is also associated with the Food Works program, proudly reporting that teens involved sold over $11,000 worth of produce in 2009, and she has described the positive impact of the community garden on the St. Johns Woods community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f188db350c6a6f2fdb22a9e9283e4dc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45291ea55455adae718c5031c0e8dfff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c9669112f71f37c0273243e8cc59e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edff28cc5d3b6f311f02cd2481c28fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f8b5f47647da9706f2d5877b878fae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fa6369dd0584465f07387131c6d28e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a815073ae837fa29833af41e55990ca</data>
