    <node id="New York">
      <data key="d0">New York</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">New York is a major US city and a significant hub for the publishing industry, serving as the city of publication for numerous books, including Michael Pollan's "The Omnivore's Dilemma" (published by Penguin), Bill McKibben's "Deep Economy", and Robert Putnam's "Bowling Alone". The city is home to numerous publishing houses, including Avon Books, Lyons Press, Macmillan Company, Grosset &amp; Dunlap, John Wiley &amp; Sons, Random House, Harper &amp; Brothers, and Ballantine. Macmillan, the publisher of "Principles of Field Crop Production", is also located in New York. Furthermore, New York is a US state where one of the Northeast Organic Wheat consortium's teams is located, and where the Cornell Farm to School Program operates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d6381862167ee0d108723409eae36d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a25021ab306ceaf5d58e192cc6fc0a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e716e5bd5f06009e0468b77709b834d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1bfb736a960a0ceee22d5eb6f8e955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c575c019780e689390cd685c690159f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f19adc067f85e17ae856f88441c8e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2920f4362eb05a4692fa915ca812b425&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bdeb1a250cfa50c7c4dce2c38964661&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62dde44a553987a2d4deba0864e69eeb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mel Bartholomew">
      <data key="d0">Mel Bartholomew</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Author of 'Cash from Square Foot Gardening' and 'Square Foot Gardening', establishing a popular gardening method.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2920f4362eb05a4692fa915ca812b425</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Raymond P. Poincelot">
      <data key="d0">Raymond P. Poincelot</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Author of 'No-Dig, No-Weed Gardening', a book about organic gardening without tilling.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of 'No-Dig, No-Weed Gardening', a book on organic gardening without tilling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f19adc067f85e17ae856f88441c8e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2920f4362eb05a4692fa915ca812b425</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chelsea Green Publishing">
      <data key="d0">Chelsea Green Publishing</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A publisher based in White River Junction, Vermont, specializing in books on sustainable agriculture, organic gardening, and homesteading. They published works by Elliot Coleman, Leandre and Gretchen Poisson, Lynn Byczynski, Trauger Groh, and Gene Logsdon.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f19adc067f85e17ae856f88441c8e7d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trailblazer Press">
      <data key="d0">Trailblazer Press</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The publisher of Anna Edey's book 'Solviva', located in Martha's Vineyard, MA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f19adc067f85e17ae856f88441c8e7d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Herbs and Flowers">
      <data key="d0">Herbs and Flowers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A subject category for books about the cultivation, marketing, and business of growing and selling organic cut flowers, fresh-cut herbs, and medicinal herbs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f19adc067f85e17ae856f88441c8e7d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dennis Morrow Joining Janus Youth">
      <data key="d0">Dennis Morrow Joining Janus Youth</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The event in 1980 when Dennis Morrow began his employment at Janus Youth Programs, starting a long tenure that would see him become the executive director and significantly shape the organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8fa6369dd0584465f07387131c6d28e6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Morrow">
      <data key="d0">Morrow</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dennis Morrow is a key figure at Janus Youth who narrates the story of the organization's unlikely but successful venture into community gardening. Initially skeptical, he was won over by the passion of his staff and the positive community impact of the gardens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05be2e4c27c7eabe9de8d2ff56b840a5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tera Couchman Wick">
      <data key="d0">Tera Couchman Wick</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A staff member at Janus Youth and a Master Gardener who initiated the organization's first gardening project. Described as passionate and tenacious, she was the driving force behind the creation and expansion of the community gardens, securing a key USDA grant.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual named in the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38c9174dd4002f6529026fc7fd3c23f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05be2e4c27c7eabe9de8d2ff56b840a5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Northwest">
      <data key="d0">Northwest</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">"A region in the US where Cascade Baking Company operates and sources its flour locally."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The geographical region where Janus Youth is described as a major service provider for at-risk youth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05be2e4c27c7eabe9de8d2ff56b840a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104466acc0eb6f55c05f02aa258ea31a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recession of 2003">
      <data key="d0">Recession of 2003</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A major economic downturn that resulted in significant cuts to the Oregon state budget. This event directly impacted Janus Youth, forcing the organization to sell its Harry's Mother property, which housed the first garden.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05be2e4c27c7eabe9de8d2ff56b840a5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="East Africa">
      <data key="d0">East Africa</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A region of origin for many immigrant residents living in the St. Johns Woods public housing community. Their prior farming experience was crucial to the success of the community garden.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05be2e4c27c7eabe9de8d2ff56b840a5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vietnam">
      <data key="d0">Vietnam</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A country of origin for a portion of the immigrant population in the St. Johns Woods community. These residents contributed their agricultural experience to the community garden.&lt;SEP&gt;A country where Australis Aquaculture has expanded its operations, raising barramundi in modern ocean pens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05be2e4c27c7eabe9de8d2ff56b840a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16c3fe8c089550fd16987a1c4f301a2e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lee Sturdivant">
      <data key="d0">Lee Sturdivant</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Author or co-author of two books on the herb business, 'Herbs for Sale' and 'Medicinal Herbs in the Garden, Field, and Marketplace'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f19adc067f85e17ae856f88441c8e7d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
