    <node id="Lynchburg">
      <data key="d0">Lynchburg</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">Lynchburg is a city located in Virginia's southern Piedmont. It is notably the home of the nonprofit urban farm, Lynchburg Grows, which is situated on the site of the former Schenkel's greenhouse complex, also referred to as the historic Schenkel Farm. The city government conducted a preliminary environmental assessment of this site before it was acquired. Lynchburg Grows has a partnership with the city for composting, taking its leaves and wood chips to save the city landfill costs, and it also converts vacant city lots into community gardens. The farm serves the local community through a CSA program, food donations, and by making its space available for events.

In addition to its connection with the farm, Lynchburg is home to one of the oldest indoor farmers' markets in the country and has a Community Court system. The headquarters of The Society of St. Andrew are also located near the city.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b97e15a0b1c4d19efdaa6af5f597519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db735f250cad30d060b6ea644151e172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9189adec7b34964ca2342aea2d2b666e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cee86d7056c73fbe7bdaa432b2abe64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61443c6300dbc7b6e2bd6de269518650&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d076831b7a91bcd605c1e387112d81e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ebf31ca8cf0e8a5dbe6d09c3efa272</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="H. R. Schenkel Sr.">
      <data key="d0">H. R. Schenkel Sr.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">"The businessman who purchased the greenhouse complex in the 1950s and converted it to exclusively grow roses for Lynchburg Wholesale Florist."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b97e15a0b1c4d19efdaa6af5f597519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
