    <node id="Historic Greenhouses">
      <data key="d0">Historic Greenhouses</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"The nine abandoned, century-old glass greenhouses on the industrial site. Despite years of neglect, they housed resilient roses and were restored by Lynchburg Grows to become the center of their urban farm."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Described as Lynchburg Grows' 'greatest asset,' these are nine historic glass-enclosed structures that the organization is restoring. They are used for a wide variety of purposes, including growing vegetables, herbs, flowers, housing historic roses, research into alternative fuels, educational centers, and as a venue for special events.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b97e15a0b1c4d19efdaa6af5f597519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ebf31ca8cf0e8a5dbe6d09c3efa272</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Historic Roses">
      <data key="d0">Historic Roses</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"The resilient rose bushes, originally cultivated by Schenkel's, that survived for years without care in the abandoned greenhouses. Their survival inspired Michael Van Ness and they remain a feature of the Lynchburg Grows farm."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b97e15a0b1c4d19efdaa6af5f597519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
