      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A co-author of 'Rabbit Production, 5th ed.', a guide to raising rabbits.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of 'Rabbit Production, 5th ed.' focused on rabbit production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a25021ab306ceaf5d58e192cc6fc0a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1bfb736a960a0ceee22d5eb6f8e955</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Farmer for a Day">
      <data key="d0">Farmer for a Day</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A program at Lynchburg Grows where individuals aged 16 to 21 can work at the farm once a week to participate in chores, build life skills, and gain self-esteem.&lt;SEP&gt;An innovative youth program run by Lynchburg Grows. It invites school classes to the farm to learn about food, healthy eating, and various farm systems like composting and raised beds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61443c6300dbc7b6e2bd6de269518650&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9189adec7b34964ca2342aea2d2b666e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DDT">
      <data key="d0">DDT</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A persistent, carcinogenic pesticide mentioned as an example of a soil contaminant. Its history is used to illustrate how substances once considered safe were later found to have long-term negative environmental consequences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9189adec7b34964ca2342aea2d2b666e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cunningham's Grandfather">
      <data key="d0">Cunningham's Grandfather</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A double-leg amputee who was a formative figure in Dereck Cunningham's life. He taught Cunningham how to garden from his wheelchair, working side-by-side with him among the vegetables and instilling in him a sense of possibility that later inspired the mission of Lynchburg Grows.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9189adec7b34964ca2342aea2d2b666e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Spina Bifida">
      <data key="d0">Spina Bifida</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A birth defect with which Dereck Cunningham was born. His experience of overcoming the initial prognosis and thriving with this condition gave him a special sensitivity to people with special needs, which became a core principle of Lynchburg Grows.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9189adec7b34964ca2342aea2d2b666e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sustainable Farming Systems">
      <data key="d0">Sustainable Farming Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A category representing the agricultural techniques taught at Lynchburg Grows' 'Farmer for a Day' program. This includes specific systems such as composting, vermiculture, and the use of raised beds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9189adec7b34964ca2342aea2d2b666e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEQ">
      <data key="d0">DEQ</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The DEQ is an organization that conducted an initial assessment of the soil at Lynchburg Grows' farm, which led to the decision to undertake a massive soil replacement project.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2cee86d7056c73fbe7bdaa432b2abe64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Randolph Macon College">
      <data key="d0">Randolph Macon College</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Randolph Macon College is a higher education institution whose student-athletes provided volunteer labor to help Lynchburg Grows with its large-scale soil replacement project.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2cee86d7056c73fbe7bdaa432b2abe64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lynchburg College">
      <data key="d0">Lynchburg College</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Lynchburg College is a higher education institution that supported Lynchburg Grows by providing over 250 student volunteers for the soil replacement project and also supplies over 4,000 pounds of dining hall waste for the composting program.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2cee86d7056c73fbe7bdaa432b2abe64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
