    <node id="Community Development">
      <data key="d0">Community Development</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The core mission of Nuestras Raíces, which aims to improve all aspects of life in Holyoke by empowering residents to increase their economic, environmental, and personal sustainability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Connecticut River">
      <data key="d0">Connecticut River</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A river on whose banks Holyoke was built. It is cited as a local environmental justice issue due to mercury contamination, making fish from the river unsafe to eat.&lt;SEP&gt;A river on whose banks Holyoke was built. It suffers from mercury contamination, making its fish unsafe to eat. The La Finca farm is located along this river.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Holyoke Health Center">
      <data key="d0">Holyoke Health Center</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A local health organization cited in the text for providing data on the high rate of diabetes mortality in Holyoke, which underscores the public health challenges that Nuestras Raíces works to address.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Student Intern with Cerebral Palsy">
      <data key="d0">The Student Intern with Cerebral Palsy</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A key figure in the introductory anecdote who, through his work at a learning farm, learned self-respect and moved beyond feeling sorry for himself.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Holyoke's Mills and Tobacco Farms">
      <data key="d0">Holyoke's Mills and Tobacco Farms</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The core industries in Holyoke during the 1950s and '60s. Their closure in the 1980s resulted in a catastrophic loss of jobs and long-term economic distress for the town.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The American Dream">
      <data key="d0">The American Dream</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The aspirational goal that motivated Puerto Rican immigrants to move to Holyoke for work in its once-thriving industries. This dream was disrupted by the town's economic collapse.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Food Projects">
      <data key="d0">Community Food Projects</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A broader category of initiatives to which Nuestras Raíces belongs. These projects use food as a 'gateway and catalyst' for wider community health and development goals.&lt;SEP&gt;A general category of initiatives that aim to connect communities with land and food. The text presents the farm in the Navajo Nation as a powerful example of such a project, reflecting broader national themes of hope and renewal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Atlantic Magazine">
      <data key="d0">Atlantic Magazine</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A magazine cited in the text for interviewing former executive director Daniel Ross about the work and philosophy of Nuestras Raíces.&lt;SEP&gt;A magazine that featured an explanation from community leader Joel Cortijo about the sense of community ownership over the gardens in Holyoke.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
