    <node id="Brownfields">
      <data key="d0">Brownfields</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A category of land, often with prior industrial use, that can be redeveloped. The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency provides information on using brownfields for urban agriculture projects."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A term for abandoned industrial lots, which are a significant environmental justice concern in Holyoke due to potentially contaminated soil. Nuestras Raíces educates the community about this issue.&lt;SEP&gt;Abandoned industrial lots prevalent in Holyoke with potentially contaminated soils. They represent a significant environmental challenge and are the subject of an educational video project led by Rivera.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16e699b4bb77d0bdc27d883c3cafa88c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69499413d16357f9a2d75749d72ecca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Holyoke">
      <data key="d0">Holyoke</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A city built on the banks of the Connecticut River. It faces environmental challenges such as mercury contamination, brownfields, and poor air quality. It is the location for all of Nuestras Raíces's community projects mentioned in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Holyoke is a city in western Massachusetts and the primary location of Nuestras Raíces's activities. The organization has a significant positive economic impact on the city, particularly its low-income community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ee782c1d8a631cff4fafc639994eb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="La Finca">
      <data key="d0">La Finca</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A 30-acre farm incubator located along the Connecticut River and managed by Nuestras Raíces. It includes individual farm plots, a youth farm, a farm store, a greenhouse, and facilities that celebrate Puerto Rican heritage, serving 20-25 farmers annually.&lt;SEP&gt;La Finca is a farm or agricultural project mentioned in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;La Finca is a farm where graduates of the Nuestras Raíces training course who achieve a high score on their business plan are eligible to receive a plot to begin farming.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ee782c1d8a631cff4fafc639994eb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c9669112f71f37c0273243e8cc59e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Kevin Andaluz">
      <data key="d0">Kevin Andaluz</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">"A representative for Nuestras Raíces."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;An individual mentioned in the index.&lt;SEP&gt;The farm manager for Nuestras Raíces at La Finca. He believes the farms have long-term impacts, serving low-income people and providing food for local schools. He highlights the challenges of teaching farming in Massachusetts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0809b82d4ca6415545d8263dbdcfcf73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trustees of Reservations">
      <data key="d0">Trustees of Reservations</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A nonprofit dedicated to preserving land. It leases 26 acres of the La Finca property to Nuestras Raíces but is unable to provide a long-term lease, which poses challenges for grant applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Joel Cortijo">
      <data key="d0">Joel Cortijo</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A community leader in Holyoke who explained that the community gardens are protected from vandalism because everyone takes ownership of them.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual mentioned in the index.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0809b82d4ca6415545d8263dbdcfcf73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tito Santana">
      <data key="d0">Tito Santana</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">"A representative for Nuestras Raíces."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The interim codirector for Nuestras Raíces. He commented on the challenges presented by the short-term lease agreement with the Trustees of Reservations.&lt;SEP&gt;Tito Santana is associated with Nuestras Raíces and explains the difficulties new farmers have in accessing land and capital in the Holyoke area. He also notes that many participants farm in addition to holding full-time jobs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ee782c1d8a631cff4fafc639994eb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfe2a17435f059c92535241799795b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740836</data>
    </node>
