    </node>
    <node id="Purdue University">
      <data key="d0">Purdue University</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A university that hosts the Indiana Media Distribution Center for agricultural communications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-66bbc17b9fd4fb132a3a76abd2df0690</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Iowa State University">
      <data key="d0">Iowa State University</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A university that is home to the Leopold Center for Sustainable Agriculture.&lt;SEP&gt;Iowa State University is an educational institution in Ames, Iowa, that hosts the MidWest Plan Service.&lt;SEP&gt;A university that published a 2004 brochure with recommendations for producers on how to sell to local foodservice markets, including the suggestion to share their farm's story.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-66bbc17b9fd4fb132a3a76abd2df0690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497b3487d00eabefe426a10fa32f8010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57c24510274e9c9fcb046e6b604285fd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740878</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Franklin D. Roosevelt">
      <data key="d0">Franklin D. Roosevelt</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">"The 32nd President of the United States, mentioned in a historical context."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The 32nd U.S. President, mentioned for creating the Civilian Conservation Corps in 1933. He is used as a historical example of a leader who initiated a large-scale youth work program with lasting national benefits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civilian Conservation Corps">
      <data key="d0">Civilian Conservation Corps</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A historical program from 1933 created by President Franklin D. Roosevelt that employed young men in conservation projects. It is used as an analogy to illustrate the potential transformative impact The Food Project could have if implemented on a national scale.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Leadership">
      <data key="d0">Community Leadership</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A core skill developed in The Food Project's older interns. They learn leadership by managing farmers' markets, running workshops, and presenting to community leaders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internship Program">
      <data key="d0">Internship Program</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The fourth tier of The Food Project's youth programs, created for older youths. Interns in this program take on community leadership roles, such as managing CSAs and farmers' markets, and leading workshops at the Urban Learning Farm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Eat In Act Out Week">
      <data key="d0">Eat In Act Out Week</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific event or campaign run by the interns of The Food Project's BLAST program, intended to promote awareness and action around healthy food.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dust Bowl">
      <data key="d0">Dust Bowl</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A devastating historical period of severe dust storms and soil erosion in the American prairies during the 1930s. The Civilian Conservation Corps was created in part to counteract its effects.&lt;SEP&gt;A historical period of severe drought and famine in America. The text highlights it as a challenge that the Hopi and Navajo successfully overcame due to their resilient and diverse agricultural strategies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a371db96fe54cad23b00f1b8eac0eefc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
