    <node id="Local Food Systems">
      <data key="d0">Local Food Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The network of food production, processing, distribution, and consumption within a specific geographic area. The author speculates on the massive positive impact an organization like The Food Project could have on local food systems if scaled up.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740840</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Health">
      <data key="d0">Public Health</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A field of study and practice that the text suggests can learn valuable lessons from the Navajo experience, which demonstrates a clear, inextricable link between health, spiritual wholeness, and a connection to land and food.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Health is a societal goal that community food projects can contribute to by delivering quality food to populations at risk for diet-related diseases like obesity and diabetes. Growing Power's work is linked to achieving public health goals.&lt;SEP&gt;The health of the population as a whole. The author suggests that a nationwide Food Project-style program could have significant long-term benefits for public health through improved nutrition and food access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b887765fabe568d174cfa581723af5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0adcf3a18e5a064a6ed2b9d46dff75f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740840</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Centers for Disease Control and Prevention">
      <data key="d0">Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A U.S. federal agency that provides data and statistics on public health issues, including Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder and obesity trends.&lt;SEP&gt;A U.S. federal health agency (CDC) that published a 2009 report on halting the obesity epidemic by making health easier.&lt;SEP&gt;A public health agency cited for a 2007 study that calculated the annual 'cost of illness' for ADHD to be between $36 billion and $52 billion in 2005 dollars.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8965f3e3965322fdf5c53aebddde1e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c0dfef7989eab5ae8b58770f9786cac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bdeb1a250cfa50c7c4dce2c38964661</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740840</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEEDS Inc.">
      <data key="d0">SEEDS Inc.</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A nonprofit organization located in Durham, North Carolina, that has found success, similar to The Food Project, by paying teens for their work in the program.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization that tracks its program graduates and seeks to connect them with career-building opportunities like internships in culinary or landscaping fields.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8965f3e3965322fdf5c53aebddde1e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aaeba6a87de6589129068300a4f26db</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740840</data>
    </node>
