      <data key="d0">ADHD Cost of Illness Study</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A 2007 study cited by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention which calculated the annual societal cost of ADHD in 2005 dollars to be between $36 billion and $52 billion. The author uses this figure to advocate for preventative programs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8965f3e3965322fdf5c53aebddde1e14</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
