    <node id="Childhood Obesity">
      <data key="d0">Childhood Obesity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Childhood Obesity is a major public health issue and a significant health crisis that affects one in three U.S. children and is noted for potentially lowering the life expectancy of the current generation. The issue is the central topic of reports from the White House Childhood Obesity Task Force, news articles, and data from the CDC. As a key motivator for action, Childhood Obesity has spurred the creation of community and school-based food programs, such as FoodCorps and the Farm to School movement, which aim to reverse this trend by providing healthier food options and nutrition education to children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7c0dfef7989eab5ae8b58770f9786cac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04be01c6169d0bdd92b10dca615a3936&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aaeba6a87de6589129068300a4f26db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef6f9e3cdaa27cfe32361bcab20e464</data>
