    <node id="Michelle Obama">
      <data key="d0">Michelle Obama</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">As the former First Lady of the United States, Michelle Obama is a public figure known for her initiatives promoting nutrition, health, and combating childhood obesity. She provided top-down support to the grassroots food movement by founding the "Let's Move!" campaign, which advocated for Farm to School programs to improve children's health. A key symbol of her efforts was planting a garden at the White House, and she also encouraged the development of school gardens. Additionally, Michelle Obama created the "Move Chefs to Schools" initiative to further promote healthier eating for children, which involved inviting professionals like Chef Charles Hudson to the White House in recognition of their work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ea6dd73e41a475c9933ac4783be5f57a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef6f9e3cdaa27cfe32361bcab20e464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16c3fe8c089550fd16987a1c4f301a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60071a35b7d93bd331a3e0d32f9f3fe4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740842</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Let's Move! Campaign">
      <data key="d0">Let's Move! Campaign</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A campaign launched by First Lady Michelle Obama in February 2010 with significant media attention, aimed at addressing the childhood obesity epidemic through promoting healthier eating and physical activity.&lt;SEP&gt;An initiative led by Michelle Obama that actively promotes community gardens, school gardens, and Farm to School programs as part of its mission to address childhood obesity.&lt;SEP&gt;Let's Move! is a public health campaign mentioned in the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c9669112f71f37c0273243e8cc59e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6dd73e41a475c9933ac4783be5f57a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef6f9e3cdaa27cfe32361bcab20e464</data>
