    <node id="FoodCorps">
      <data key="d0">FoodCorps</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">FoodCorps is a national non-profit and public service organization that operates as a branch of the AmeriCorps program. It offers year-long public service opportunities for young adults, who act as service members, to provide "people power" to schools. The organization's primary mission is to reverse childhood obesity and improve the health of vulnerable children by connecting them to healthy food, particularly in communities with high rates of obesity.

To achieve its goals, FoodCorps service members build and tend school gardens, support Farm to School initiatives, and conduct educational programs on food, nutrition, and agriculture. Through these efforts, FoodCorps works to bring fresh foods into America's schools, improve children's access to and engagement with healthy food, and invest in the next generation of farmers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fef6f9e3cdaa27cfe32361bcab20e464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04be01c6169d0bdd92b10dca615a3936&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e716e5bd5f06009e0468b77709b834d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79fcf59d7b63a10ed28124a2923fc0f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b79b32f16bacae95e48f2f51ab5dee0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740848</data>
    </node>
    <node id="New York City School District">
      <data key="d0">New York City School District</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A school district cited as an example of a large-scale Farm to School program, having signed a $4.2 million contract with farmers in upstate New York to provide apples to its schools.&lt;SEP&gt;A school district that serves as an example of a large-scale Farm to School initiative, having signed a $4.2 million, three-year contract with farmers to provide apples to its schools.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04be01c6169d0bdd92b10dca615a3936&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef6f9e3cdaa27cfe32361bcab20e464</data>
