    <node id="Nutrition Training Program">
      <data key="d0">Nutrition Training Program</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A pilot program conducted in 2009 by the Obesity Task Force in Birmingham to educate and motivate cafeteria staff about using fresh ingredients. This successful program was later expanded and made mandatory by the county school system under JVUF's management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d971c6976ab8e71370d85b346b00f467</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="County School System">
      <data key="d0">County School System</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The governing educational body in the Birmingham area that, one year after the pilot program, established a new requirement that all its school cafeteria workers participate in JVUF's nutrition training program.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d971c6976ab8e71370d85b346b00f467</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obesity Epidemic">
      <data key="d0">Obesity Epidemic</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"A major public health crisis, explicitly linked to the industrial food system. Its financial cost in the U.S. was reported by the Surgeon General to be $117 billion per year in 2001, highlighting the externalized health costs of cheap food."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;A public health crisis that the author assumed would be the main driver for healthier food in college dining halls, but found that it was less influential than the campus sustainability movement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-419e80efe9993622fcb085a34f66a623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d971c6976ab8e71370d85b346b00f467</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
