      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A college in Vermont noted for its commitment to local sourcing, purchasing all its dairy products, maple syrup, and eggs locally.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bates College">
      <data key="d0">Bates College</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A college in Maine that dedicates 30% of its dining budget to local food and diverts 82% of its dining waste through recycling, composting, or to a local pig farmer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="California State University At Chico">
      <data key="d0">California State University At Chico</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A university in California that operates its own organic farm and dairy, and has a mandate that 25% of its food must be both certified organic and produced within California.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Oberlin College">
      <data key="d0">Oberlin College</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A college in Ohio described as a leading pioneer in the local food movement, purchasing 45% of its food locally and having implemented a wide range of sustainable food initiatives since 1998, such as switching to antibiotic-free meats and cage-free eggs.&lt;SEP&gt;Oberlin College is an educational institution with a noted sustainability initiative related to its dining services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c575c019780e689390cd685c690159f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bill Mckibben">
      <data key="d0">Bill Mckibben</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Author of 'Deep Economy' who argues that the conventional food system is heavily dependent on oil, a key factor supporting the economic case for local food.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740851</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Phil Petrilli">
      <data key="d0">Phil Petrilli</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Phil Petrilli is the Northeast Regional Operations Director for the Chipotle Mexican Grill restaurant chain. He observed that rising oil prices made sourcing local meat more cost-effective when compared to conventionally sourced meat. As a key representative for Chipotle, Petrilli was deeply involved in establishing a partnership with Polyface Farm. He demonstrated a strong personal commitment to this initiative, traveling frequently to the farm to work through logistical challenges directly with Joel Salatin. Drawing from this experience, Petrilli advises small farmers to aggregate into co-ops to meet the volume needs of large buyers and suggests they start small to work out logistical issues before scaling up their operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77562613f0c5d12383f7ffab65ce2e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740851</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chipotle">
      <data key="d0">Chipotle</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Chipotle is a national fast-food restaurant chain that partnered with Polyface Farm to source high-quality, locally and sustainably raised meat, specifically pork for its carnitas, for its Charlottesville restaurant. Under the leadership of Steve Ells, Chipotle showed significant commitment to making the partnership successful by adapting recipes and solving logistical challenges related to transportation and packaging. The company empowered employees such as Joel Holland, Heidi Wederquist, and Petrilli to facilitate the collaboration, which was implemented through a slow, trial-based rollout that highlighted the importance of customer communication. This relationship serves as an example of a large chain sourcing local food, and it also represents the challenge a small, values-driven farm like Polyface faces when working with "big boys" from the mainstream food system without compromising its principles. From Polyface Farm's perspective, while the partnership was real, it also illustrates their philosophy of not actively pursuing large markets for expansion; they would supply a company like Chipotle if asked, but not set them as a sales target.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d31a2f89a77b64e0ae04120df1fdb3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63208f55f5e282db2dc1514f989da622&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740851</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Polyface Farm">
      <data key="d0">Polyface Farm</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Polyface Farm, located at 43 Pure Meadows Lane in Swoope, Virginia's Shenandoah Valley, is a multi-generational, family-owned, and pasture-based farm run by the Salatin family, including prominent author and farmer Joel Salatin and Sheri Salatin. The farm is renowned for its sustainable, non-industrial, and "beyond organic" agricultural techniques, with a core mission to heal the land, food, economy, and culture by operating within its ecological carrying capacity. It raises beef, pork, and chicken, supplying these meat products to a diverse customer base that includes restaurants, a successful direct-to-consumer Buying Club, and a supplier relationship with Chipotle Mexican Grill, which has been highlighted as an example of a farm-to-institution supply chain.

Operating on a unique set of business principles, Polyface Farm prioritizes quality and ecological sustainability over growth, resisting large-scale industrial models and the "Wall Street" business approach. It avoids sales targets, advertising, patents, and IPOs, relying instead on word-of-mouth, direct customer interaction, and an incentivized workforce. The farm's Buying Club defines its local delivery range as a one-day round trip and utilizes specific operational methods like thermal bags and an integrated electronic system for online orders.

Polyface Farm gained national attention after being featured in Michael Pollan's book, "The Omnivore's Dilemma," and serves as an influential model for sustainable agriculture. Its methods are studied by others, and a 1998 visit to the farm was a pivotal moment that inspired farmer Jamie Ager to pursue a profitable farming business. To manage significant public interest, the farm engages in agritourism with an open-door policy, offering self-guided and paid guided tours during specific times and opening its farm store just one day a week.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4d53cc613c52fd5080e556f9abb248a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d31a2f89a77b64e0ae04120df1fdb3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da1b16361a783bc112824aaa6fa12fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d6381862167ee0d108723409eae36d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ecda741e6aebaebfb4bbcd928bb80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f712d3550c8612228f9fb4dc999ba9b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60121fd34d6b068a55f53ef625e1f266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c8f3e81fd6708a9852f46f0d4ac0a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e930a3eb466e9bb1dfa38b0df50bfd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd285deff310269197e8718b28f6076b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740851</data>
    </node>
