    <node id="Widmark">
      <data key="d0">Widmark</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The founder of Diablo Burger. He is a strong advocate for local food systems, believing they are a practical and sustainable future. He focuses on making local food affordable and connecting urban communities with the rural lands that feed them, viewing food as a way to value the landscape differently.&lt;SEP&gt;Widmark is a person who advocates for viewing local food systems as a practical way to 'romance the future.' He believes that recognizing rural areas as sources of food will lead to valuing and preserving those landscapes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-087cef03c5ab256c59a3f536c4533b6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db735f250cad30d060b6ea644151e172</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740879</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diablo Trust Ranches">
      <data key="d0">Diablo Trust Ranches</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A group of local ranches that supply whole cows to Diablo Burger. While the restaurant's consumption is a small part of their total sales, this partnership is seen as an important first step in developing the local market for their products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-087cef03c5ab256c59a3f536c4533b6d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740879</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Colorado Plateau">
      <data key="d0">Colorado Plateau</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">A geographic region whose precious and scarce water resources directly influenced Diablo Burger's decision to operate without a dishwasher, highlighting the restaurant's commitment to environmental sustainability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-087cef03c5ab256c59a3f536c4533b6d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740879</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Local Environmental and Economic Sustainability">
      <data key="d0">Local Environmental and Economic Sustainability</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A core principle guiding Diablo Burger's operations. It is demonstrated through specific practices like sourcing locally, accepting cash to keep money in the community, conserving water, and using local craftsmen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-087cef03c5ab256c59a3f536c4533b6d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740879</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diablo Canyon RPA Model">
      <data key="d0">Diablo Canyon RPA Model</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A regional planning model suggested in the text as a way to create an effective regional plan. It emphasizes a partnership dialogue between agricultural property owners, county government, and the local economic development commission to keep farm and ranch lands economically viable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-087cef03c5ab256c59a3f536c4533b6d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740879</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Agricultural Property Owners">
      <data key="d0">Agricultural Property Owners</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A stakeholder group, specifically farm and ranch owners, identified by the Diablo Canyon RPA model as essential partners in a dialogue to develop strategies for economic viability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-087cef03c5ab256c59a3f536c4533b6d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1753740879</data>
    </node>
