    <edge source="Parasitic Mites" target="North America">
      <data key="d6">25.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Parasitic mites are an invasive species in North America, having been introduced in the mid-1980s, and they pose a significant threat to the continent's honeybee population.&lt;SEP&gt;Parasitic mites are an invasive species that have been spreading throughout North America since the mid-1980s, causing severe problems for honey bees.&lt;SEP&gt;Two types of parasitic mites, the tracheal mite and the Varroa mite, were introduced to North America in the 1980s, becoming a very serious problem for beekeepers.</data>
      <data key="d8">geographic impact,geographical spread,invasive species,regional threat</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c2ef2a61b557f4940ffb63973d9ebeaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96f78f364d74eca8b91a5a10f5f9de4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Parasitic Mites" target="Western Hemisphere">
      <data key="d6">13.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Parasitic mites are not native to the Western Hemisphere, which is why their introduction has had such a significant impact on beekeeping in the Americas.&lt;SEP&gt;The text specifies that the threatening parasitic mites are not native to the Western Hemisphere, highlighting their invasive nature.</data>
      <data key="d8">biogeography,geographical origin,invasive species,species origin</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-96f78f364d74eca8b91a5a10f5f9de4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Parasitic Mites" target="Beekeepers">
      <data key="d6">19.0</data>
      <data key="d7">As government support wanes, beekeepers are forced to accept greater personal responsibility for detecting and controlling parasitic mites.&lt;SEP&gt;Parasitic mites pose a direct and severe threat to beekeepers, as an undetected or untreated infestation can wipe out all of their bee holdings.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeper responsibility,economic threat,pest management,self-regulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-96f78f364d74eca8b91a5a10f5f9de4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc749ae5b6e2c5fae540d31c52a16691</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Parasitic Mites" target="Honeybees">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Parasitic mites are a major threat to honeybees, capable of wiping out entire colonies if they go undetected or untreated.</data>
