    <edge source="Comb Honey" target="Bee Equipment Suppliers">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Bee equipment suppliers provide the necessary packaging, such as square plastic boxes, required for presenting and selling cut comb honey.</data>
      <data key="d8">commercial materials,product packaging,supply chain</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-da9216023ced68a9aa545d43ca1d419f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Comb Honey" target="New Colony">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Producing comb honey is not recommended with a new colony because it requires a large bee population, which new colonies typically lack, leading to a high likelihood of failure and disappointment.</data>
      <data key="d8">beginner advice,colony strength,production feasibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-da9216023ced68a9aa545d43ca1d419f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Comb Honey" target="Comb Foundation">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Comb foundation is the specific, thinner, unwired foundation used to produce comb honey, as the foundation itself is intended to be eaten.</data>
      <data key="d8">material properties,production equipment,specific use</data>
