    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Wag-tail Dance">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The wag-tail dance is performed to communicate the precise distance and direction of a forage source that is more than 100 meters away from the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">complex communication,resource location</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Round Dance">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The round dance is performed to indicate a new forage source is available within 100 meters of the hive and communicates the type of forage through odors and samples.</data>
      <data key="d8">resource notification,simple communication</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Forager">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The primary function of the forager is to locate and collect forage from the environment to sustain the colony.</data>
      <data key="d8">division of labor,resource collection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Dancer">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The dancer provides samples and conveys odors of the forage she has found, allowing hivemates to understand the specific type of food source available.</data>
      <data key="d8">resource identification,sensory communication</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Beekeeper">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper must evaluate the availability of forage in the area before establishing a hive, considering the 1-to-2-mile radius and the presence of other beekeepers.</data>
      <data key="d8">location planning,resource assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Honey Bees">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Honey Bees depend on forage for food, typically traveling 1 to 2 miles to collect it from flowering plants. The proximity and abundance of forage are critical for their success.</data>
      <data key="d8">food source,foraging behavior</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Hive">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The location of the hive should be chosen based on the availability of forage in the surrounding 1-to-2-mile radius to ensure the colony has enough food.</data>
      <data key="d8">location dependency,resource availability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Flowering Plants">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Flowering Plants are the specific source of forage for bees. Their presence in a given area determines the quality and quantity of forage available.</data>
      <data key="d8">botanical component,resource source</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Forage" target="Livestock">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text explains that adequate forage is a critical food source for livestock and can significantly reduce their need for drinking water.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal husbandry,food source,resource management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b</data>
