      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Hive">
      <data key="d6">35.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper's practical work is centered around the Hive, which is the core of the bee colony's life and the beekeeper's management activities. A Beekeeper's responsibilities include the initial setup of the Hive, such as selecting a proper location on level ground with adequate space, and assembling the structure itself. For ongoing management, the Beekeeper directly interacts with the Hive through regular visits, performing physical maintenance and assessment. These tasks include opening the Hive for inspection, checking its weight to gauge the colony's food stores, and keeping the entrances clear. The manner in which the Beekeeper interacts with the Hive is crucial, as gentle handling with minimal thumping directly affects the state of the bees inside.</data>
      <data key="d8">assessment,hands-on care,hive management,inspection,location selection,maintenance,management,management activity,physical interaction,stewardship,work focus</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-60575ab4028f754c314fcbcee392db85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d47730064116b6f4fe93ddb307901d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Bees">
      <data key="d6">30.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is the caretaker of the bees, responsible for their feeding, health, and the maintenance of their hive throughout the seasons.&lt;SEP&gt;The beekeeper's actions, attire, scent, and emotional state directly influence the bees' behavior. The core theme of the text is how the beekeeper can manage themselves to keep the bees calm.&lt;SEP&gt;The fundamental relationship in beekeeping is between the Beekeeper, who learns about, works with, and enjoys the bees, and the Bees themselves, which are the subject of this care.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal husbandry,behavior management,caretaking,central relationship,human-animal interaction,management,safety,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-60575ab4028f754c314fcbcee392db85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f35b518c8481093038a38bf2b64387d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Drone Bee">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Beekeepers often have a negative view of drones and actively destroy them, considering them a drain on hive resources.</data>
      <data key="d8">antagonistic relationship,human intervention,resource management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-14c389aa55b6d5b4c773f2c917b36e7a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Colony">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text describes the beekeeper's practice of culling drones as a 'short-sighted attitude' that is detrimental to the overall well-being and natural processes of the colony.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony health,human impact,mismanagement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-14c389aa55b6d5b4c773f2c917b36e7a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Honey Bees">
      <data key="d6">34.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A Beekeeper serves as the caretaker and manager of Honey Bee colonies, with a wide range of responsibilities that directly affect the bees' well-being and behavior. The Beekeeper's duties include maintaining the health of the colonies by protecting them from diseases such as American Foulbrood and intervening by providing supplementary feed like sugar or pollen substitutes when natural resources are scarce. A Beekeeper's personal demeanor, including their confidence and actions, directly influences the behavior of the Honey Bees; a calm, careful approach results in calmer bees, whereas nervousness can agitate them. Furthermore, the strategic decisions made by the Beekeeper, particularly regarding hive placement in relation to forage and the proximity of other hives, have a significant impact on the success and health of not only their own Honey Bees but also those of other beekeepers in the area.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal husbandry,behavior influence,caretaking,feeding,human-animal interaction,husbandry,management,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-824704426592ed72e9ae44a04bd1ddbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d47730064116b6f4fe93ddb307901d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Smoke">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper uses smoke as a tool to pacify the bee colony during an inspection, ensuring safety and reducing disruption to the cluster.&lt;SEP&gt;The beekeeper utilizes the 'judicious application of smoke' as a management tool to bring about a set pattern of responses in the bees, namely calming them and reducing their defensive reactions.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal handling,behavior management,safety procedure,stimulus application,tool usage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d47730064116b6f4fe93ddb307901d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Honey Bee Colony">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A beekeeper's primary goal is to understand the activities and behaviors of the honey bee colony to be more effective at their job.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,observation,study</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Worker Bee">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text advises that a beekeeper's understanding is greatly improved by observing the worker bee, which is described as the colony's 'primary life force'.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,observation,study subject</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="The Colony">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper interacts with and manages the colony, but their management perspective and schedule (the 'beekeeper's year') are distinct from the colony's own natural, continuous cycle.</data>
      <data key="d8">human interaction,management,observation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Pollen">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A beekeeper can collect pollen from the bees using a pollen trap, and then feed it back to the bees in times of need.</data>
      <data key="d8">feeding,harvesting,resource management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-824704426592ed72e9ae44a04bd1ddbd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Pollen Traps">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A beekeeper uses pollen traps to collect pure pollen from the hive entrance.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping practice,harvesting,tool usage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-824704426592ed72e9ae44a04bd1ddbd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Sugar">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A beekeeper may feed sugar to a bee colony when necessary, but must use pure forms like granulated sugar to avoid harming the bees.&lt;SEP&gt;The beekeeper utilizes sugar to prepare life-saving emergency food, either as syrup or candy, when the colony's natural stores are depleted.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping practice,feed preparation,feeding,husbandry,intervention,resource management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-824704426592ed72e9ae44a04bd1ddbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Dance Language">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text states that the dance language contributes to the success of a bee colony, which in turn is important to the beekeeper, although the beekeeper cannot directly influence the dancing.</data>
      <data key="d8">apiculture,ecosystem services</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3ca6767b0793c7530226a6b224d0f21b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Beekeeping Equipment">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper must select and use beekeeping equipment. The text advises the beekeeper, especially a novice, to learn the basics and work with standard equipment before experimenting.</data>
      <data key="d8">equipment selection,user guidance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Standard Equipment">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text strongly advises the novice Beekeeper to use Standard Equipment for the first 2-3 years to learn the basics before experimenting with other types.</data>
      <data key="d8">best practices,user guidance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Beekeeping Catalog">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper uses the Beekeeping Catalog to see available equipment, but is warned that its offerings can be confusing and overwhelming without prior experience.</data>
      <data key="d8">consumer information,purchasing decisions</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Veil">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is the user of the veil, which is described as an essential part of their protective attire to prevent stings to the head and face.&lt;SEP&gt;The veil is a recommended piece of safety equipment for the beekeeper. It is meant to protect the face, which is described as a primary and vulnerable target for angry bees.</data>
      <data key="d8">personal protection,risk mitigation,safety equipment,user role</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f11f928b6b6595520556e61b690ad234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f35b518c8481093038a38bf2b64387d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Gloves">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text advises the beekeeper to have gloves for emergencies but to try working without them to be more attuned to the bees and less likely to crush them.</data>
      <data key="d8">best practices,equipment use</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a9465e78f869f57a714827f88ed9c132</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Queen Excluder">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text advises beginner beekeepers that they will rarely need a queen excluder in their first year and should resist buying one.</data>
      <data key="d8">equipment advice,purchasing recommendation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a9465e78f869f57a714827f88ed9c132</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Package of Bees">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text recommends a package of bees as a primary option for a beginning beekeeper to acquire bees, noting they are easy for a novice to handle.</data>
      <data key="d8">bee acquisition,beginner recommendation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a9465e78f869f57a714827f88ed9c132</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Nucleus Hive">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A nucleus hive is presented as an excellent choice for a beekeeper, as they can grow in confidence and skill alongside the small, manageable, but already functioning colony.&lt;SEP&gt;The text recommends a nucleus hive as one of the two primary options for a beginning beekeeper to acquire bees.</data>
      <data key="d8">bee acquisition,beginner recommendation,beginner suitability,parallel growth</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9465e78f869f57a714827f88ed9c132</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Beekeeping catalogs">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text cautions the beekeeper, particularly a beginner, to resist the temptation of buying too much equipment from catalogs until they have more experience.</data>
      <data key="d8">consumer caution,purchasing advice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a9465e78f869f57a714827f88ed9c132</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Package Bees">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Package bees are recommended for novice beekeepers because they are easy to handle and less defensive. However, they are completely dependent on the beekeeper for initial resources and proper installation.</data>
      <data key="d8">beginner suitability,management dependency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Established Colony">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An established colony is described as a poor choice for a novice beekeeper because its large size can be intimidating and its potential for neglect or hidden problems is high.</data>
      <data key="d8">intimidation,suitability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Diseases">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper must be aware of and protect their colonies against diseases, a factor that should influence their choice of starter unit.</data>
      <data key="d8">disease prevention,hive management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Mites">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is responsible for taking precautions against mites, which are identified as a potential problem in bee colonies.</data>
      <data key="d8">hive management,pest control</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-18646221e86ea90ee41e4d859e5ef7b1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Experienced Beekeeper Mentor">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text advises a novice beekeeper with reservations to find an experienced mentor to guide them through their first hive inspection to build confidence and knowledge.</data>
      <data key="d8">guidance,mentorship,training</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Local Exterminator">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A local exterminator can be a valuable source of leads for a beekeeper looking to acquire unwanted honey bee colonies, as the exterminator may prefer not to handle them.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony referral,networking,sourcing</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Nectar Flow">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Beekeepers are advised to work with their hives during a nectar flow because the bees are preoccupied and more docile, making the activity safer and less disruptive.</data>
      <data key="d8">bee behavior,hive management,optimal timing</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Foragers">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">On days with no nectar flow, idle foragers, with their fully functional venom glands, pose the main threat to a beekeeper, as they may become aggressive during a hive inspection.</data>
      <data key="d8">bee behavior,hive inspection,safety risk</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Protective Beekeeping Gear">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text describes the choice of wearing protective gear as a variable practice among beekeepers when working with their hives.</data>
      <data key="d8">personal preference,safety equipment,work practice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3d621a8bb4b7eb07600bbbfbdafcad0b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Experienced Beekeeper">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An experienced beekeeper can act as a consultant or mentor to a struggling beekeeper by observing their technique to diagnose and solve problems with bee handling.</data>
      <data key="d8">mentorship,problem-solving,skill development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7f35b518c8481093038a38bf2b64387d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Propolis">
      <data key="d6">14.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper must deal with propolis when it glues parts of the hive, like the outer cover, shut. They must use a 'good upward whack' to break the seal, an action that could potentially disturb the bees.&lt;SEP&gt;The beekeeper's role includes scraping away excess propolis from the hive and frames to ensure easier access and management of the colony.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping task,cleaning,hive maintenance,interaction,obstacle</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7f35b518c8481093038a38bf2b64387d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Installation of the Package">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is the agent who performs all the steps of the installation process described in the text.</data>
      <data key="d8">action,procedure</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Protective Gear">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is instructed to put on protective gear, like a veil, before beginning the installation for personal safety.</data>
      <data key="d8">equipment use,safety</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="New Colony">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is directly responsible for the initial management and long-term survival of the New Colony.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,responsibility,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="The First Inspection">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper performs The First Inspection to check on the new colony's status, specifically the queen's release.</data>
      <data key="d8">action,inspection,management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Delayed Queen Release">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper utilizes the Delayed Queen Release technique to ensure the queen's safety and successful integration into the new colony.</data>
      <data key="d8">management technique,safety procedure</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6706ffd7485284387c77b1f38a66ce9c</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="First Inspection">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper is the person who performs the First Inspection, following the text's instructions to check on the queen and the hive's condition.</data>
      <data key="d8">action,management,procedure</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Smoker">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper is responsible for lighting, maintaining, and using the Smoker as the primary tool to calm the bees before and during an inspection.</data>
      <data key="d8">hive management,safety,tool usage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Veil and Protective Gear">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper is instructed to don a Veil and Protective Gear for personal safety before opening the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">equipment usage,safety procedure</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Colony Health">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper is responsible for monitoring and maintaining Colony Health, which may involve administering Medication to combat diseases and mites.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony management,disease prevention,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="The Queen">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper actively evaluates the performance of The Queen and may decide to replace her through requeening to improve the colony's chances of survival.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony management,evaluation,intervention</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Fall Requeening">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The beekeeper is the agent who makes the decision to requeen and performs the action based on their evaluation of the current queen's performance."&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;The Beekeeper is the person who performs the action of Fall Requeening as a management practice to strengthen the hive before winter.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony management,decision making,intervention,management action,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-349ce4585e93cae4853e6da2e815c494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Food Stores">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The beekeeper is responsible for evaluating the amount of food stores in the hive and determining if supplementary fall feeding is necessary for the colony's winter survival."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d8">intervention,resource assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Hive Protection">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The beekeeper is responsible for implementing all hive protection measures, such as creating windbreaks and installing mouse guards, to safeguard the colony during winter."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d8">stewardship,winterization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Bee Colony">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is the caretaker of the bee colony, responsible for monitoring its health, managing its environment, and intervening with support like feeding to ensure its survival through the winter.</data>
      <data key="d8">caretaking,management,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Hive Inspection">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper performs hive inspections as a primary method of assessing the colony's status, including its location within the hive and the level of its food reserves.</data>
      <data key="d8">assessment,diagnostic activity,monitoring</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Frames">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper manipulates the frames within the hive to inspect the colony and to add frames of supplemental feed like sugar syrup.</data>
      <data key="d8">hive manipulation,inspection,management practice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b30dd2b72067de8dc8358baf75e16d21</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Spring Chores">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is the one who must perform the essential spring chores to prepare the hive for the new season.</data>
      <data key="d8">hive maintenance,seasonal labor</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3646f7feb4b27315450c6eb80594e753</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Burr Comb">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is responsible for removing burr comb during hive cleanup to prevent future obstructions and maintain the hive's internal structure.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping task,hive maintenance,structural management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Bee Brush">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper uses the bee brush as a tool, particularly during honey harvesting, to safely remove bees from the frames.</data>
      <data key="d8">bee management,harvesting technique,tool usage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Honey Extraction">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is the individual who performs the honey extraction, a central activity of their practice that requires significant preparation and specific equipment.</data>
      <data key="d8">process execution,role</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Beekeeping Equipment Suppliers">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Beekeepers interact with beekeeping equipment suppliers to purchase or rent specialized gear like extractors.</data>
      <data key="d8">procurement,supplier relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Plastic Pails">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A beekeeper requires numerous plastic pails for collecting and storing honey, a fundamental piece of equipment for managing the product.</data>
      <data key="d8">equipment need,storage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Crushing Method">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The crushing method is a technique for honey extraction available to a beekeeper, although the text describes it as a messy and impractical option.</data>
      <data key="d8">methodology choice,technique evaluation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Hive Products">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is the central figure who interacts with, collects, and processes all hive products mentioned in the text.</data>
      <data key="d8">interaction,role,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b652e467f32b1db6fbb1cf5b9315586e</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="American Foulbrood (AFB)">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper is responsible for managing American Foulbrood through inspection, prevention with antibiotics, treatment of early-stage infections, and destruction of heavily infected colonies.&lt;SEP&gt;The beekeeper is described as the 'first defense' against American Foulbrood, responsible for understanding, identifying, and treating the disease to prevent its spread to other colonies.</data>
      <data key="d8">disease management,prevention,responsibility,treatment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b71c661e88d96156e87449e9332b56ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="State Apiary Inspector">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A beekeeper is advised to contact a state apiary inspector for assistance when they are unable to diagnose a disease or condition within their hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">consultation,diagnosis,professional support</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b71c661e88d96156e87449e9332b56ce</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Destruction of Diseased Equipment">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper is the person who must carry out the Destruction of Diseased Equipment, a process that involves burning infected materials in a pit to eliminate the AFB pathogen.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping practice,disease control,sanitation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Colony Infection">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A Colony Infection with AFB requires immediate action from the Beekeeper, who must decide whether to treat the colony or destroy it based on the severity and state regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">decision-making,disease response,management action</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="State Regulations">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Beekeeper must be aware of and comply with their local State Regulations regarding the treatment or destruction of colonies infected with AFB.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping rules,legal compliance,regulatory impact</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Honey Supers">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Beekeepers manage the placement and removal of honey supers. This action is critical for timing mite treatments, as no medication should be used when supers are present to collect honey.&lt;SEP&gt;The Beekeeper is responsible for adding and removing Honey Supers from the hive, a decision that directly impacts the timing of disease treatment with medications like Terramycin.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping practices,equipment use,hive management,treatment timing</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Inspection Programs">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text advises that a Beekeeper should not be totally dependent on formal Inspection Programs and must also conduct their own thorough inspections for diseases.</data>
      <data key="d8">disease detection,personal responsibility,professional reliance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Tracheal Mite">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text establishes that the control of Tracheal mites is the direct responsibility of individual beekeepers, as centralized programs to certify bees as mite-free have been abandoned.</data>
      <data key="d8">individual responsibility,pest management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740489</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Miticur">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Beekeepers use Miticur as a treatment for mites, and they are instructed to read the label carefully and apply it only after honey supers have been removed.</data>
      <data key="d8">chemical application,pest control,safety protocol</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740489</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Menthol">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Beekeepers may use Menthol to treat mites, but its application is restricted by weather conditions and is prohibited when honey supers are on the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">chemical application,pest control,treatment constraints</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740491</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Western Honey Bee">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Beekeepers caused the crossover of the Varroa mite to the Western Honey Bee by intermingling it with the Eastern Honey Bee.</data>
      <data key="d8">disease transmission,species management,unintentional consequence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740491</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Varroa Mite">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Beekeepers actively try to detect and control Varroa mite populations in their hives to prevent colony loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Beekeepers are responsible for managing Varroa mite infestations in their hives. The text also identifies beekeeper activities, such as transporting colonies and intermingling species, as primary drivers of the Varroa mite's spread.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping practices,disease vector,human impact,intervention,pest management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740492</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Colony Damage and Mortality">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Intervention by a beekeeper is described as essential to prevent the high probability of colony mortality caused by Varroa mites.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping,hive management,prevention</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c856302a8c65c144c91bc5d8547cf8ed</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740498</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Beekeeper" target="Bee Colony/Hive">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The beekeeper is responsible for all aspects of managing the bee colony/hive, including its protection from pesticides, movement, and feeding.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,protection,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d711f27560f7987b017b85fa9c8a2e56</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740508</data>
    </edge>
