    <edge source="North America" target="Honey Bees">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Honey bees are not native to North America; they were transported there by humans during the Second Era of Beekeeping, arriving on the East Coast around 1628.</data>
      <data key="d8">geographical migration,species introduction</data>
