    </edge>
    <edge source="Bees" target="Feeder Can">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The feeder can provides sustenance for the bees during their transport within the package.</data>
      <data key="d8">provision,sustenance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bees" target="Candy">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The bees interact directly with the candy by eating it, which is the action that leads to the queen's release from her cage.</data>
      <data key="d8">interaction,queen release</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f6b1093c60c117041d669d3950218419</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bees" target="Wild Comb">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Bees are the actors who build the Wild Comb in spaces that violate 'bee space', creating problems that the beekeeper must manage.</data>
      <data key="d8">bee behavior,construction,hive maintenance</data>
