    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="Family Labor">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Children are identified as a component of family labor who can be taught to perform useful, age-appropriate tasks on the farm with proper supervision.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are the central focus of the 'Family Labor' section. The text provides extensive guidance on how to involve children in farm work, making them a primary component of the family's labor contribution.</data>
      <data key="d8">farm succession,labor contribution,labor source,skill development,youth education</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2f0a967dcad41868e71ff8891a86b69b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d72291c86cdc15cc9b42dccc6b106a1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="Livestock">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text details the relationship between children and livestock, explaining how to teach them to perform chores like collecting eggs while staying safe, and when to keep them away from larger animals like hogs and cattle.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal husbandry,child safety,farm education</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2f0a967dcad41868e71ff8891a86b69b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="Farm Machinery">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The relationship is one of risk and safety. The text explicitly warns against allowing children near farm machinery until they are old enough to understand the inherent dangers, to prevent accidents.</data>
      <data key="d8">equipment hazard,risk management,safety protocol</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2f0a967dcad41868e71ff8891a86b69b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="4-H Program">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The 4-H Program is recommended as a formal structure for children to learn about agriculture and marketing, complementing the informal education they receive on the family farm.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural education,community program,youth development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2f0a967dcad41868e71ff8891a86b69b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="Grassroots Food Movement">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The core conviction of the grassroots food movement is the need to change children's relationship with their food in order to protect their health and longevity.</data>
      <data key="d8">health intervention,primary target</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ea6dd73e41a475c9933ac4783be5f57a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="Childhood Obesity Epidemic">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Children are the demographic group most severely affected by the obesity epidemic, with rates having doubled in the last 10 years and one-third of all U.S. children being obese or overweight.</data>
      <data key="d8">affected population,health crisis</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ea6dd73e41a475c9933ac4783be5f57a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="Farm to School Movement">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Farm to School movement directly benefits children by introducing fresh, local food into their school meals and providing education on nutrition and agriculture.</data>
      <data key="d8">health and education,program beneficiary</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ea6dd73e41a475c9933ac4783be5f57a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="School Food">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">32 million children in the nation's school cafeterias are the daily consumers of school food, making their health directly dependent on its quality.</data>
      <data key="d8">consumer relationship,daily impact</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ea6dd73e41a475c9933ac4783be5f57a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="The Community Farm">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The success and positive atmosphere of the Community Farm are having a 'ripple effect' on the community's children, inspiring them to volunteer and show interest in farming.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural transmission,generational impact,positive influence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Children" target="Mainstream America">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text describes a cultural shift where children are turning away from the influence of 'mainstream America' and are being drawn back to traditional activities like farming.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural shift,generational values,rejection of assimilation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Humans" target="Royal Jelly">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Humans collect and consume royal jelly as a health supplement, based on the unproven extrapolation that the benefits it provides to a queen bee will also apply to them.</data>
      <data key="d8">health belief,product consumption,unsubstantiated claim</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b71c661e88d96156e87449e9332b56ce</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Humans" target="Propolis">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Humans use propolis as a natural health aid in products like toothpaste and tinctures, a practice supported largely by anecdotal evidence rather than scientific proof.</data>
      <data key="d8">alternative medicine,anecdotal evidence,product utilization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b71c661e88d96156e87449e9332b56ce</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Humans" target="Bee Venom">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Bee venom has a dual relationship with humans: it is used medically to desensitize them to sting allergies, but it is also the cause of these serious allergic reactions.</data>
      <data key="d8">allergen,human health,medical treatment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b71c661e88d96156e87449e9332b56ce</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Humans" target="Pollen">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Humans consume pollen that is offered for sale, but the text raises a concern about its safety due to the potential for pesticide contamination from unknown plant sources.</data>
      <data key="d8">consumer risk,food safety,pesticide contamination</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b71c661e88d96156e87449e9332b56ce</data>
