      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Worker Bee" target="Guarding">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Guarding the hive is listed as one of the sequential tasks performed by a worker bee during its life, occurring before it begins foraging.</data>
      <data key="d8">hive defense,task progression</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Worker Bee" target="Feeding Brood">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Feeding brood is a key, time-limited task performed by young worker bees when their specific glands are functional, highlighting the age-based division of labor.</data>
      <data key="d8">biological development,brood care,task limitation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Worker Bee" target="Secreting Wax">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Secreting wax is a task that a worker bee can perform once its glands have matured, linking its physical development to its role in hive construction.</data>
      <data key="d8">biological development,hive construction</data>
