    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Field Bee">
      <data key="d6">36.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Field Bee and House Bee represent two sequential phases in the life of a single worker bee. A bee begins its life as a House Bee, a stage dedicated to performing internal hive duties. As the worker bee matures and ages, it undergoes a physiological and behavioral progression, effectively 'graduating' to become a Field Bee. This transition marks a shift from indoor responsibilities to external tasks, where the Field Bee is responsible for foraging for resources outside the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">division of labor,life cycle,life cycle progression,maturation,progression,role change,role transition,task progression</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-14c389aa55b6d5b4c773f2c917b36e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bf03b457112a6e1094db904efcfe2d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="The Brood Nest">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The house bee is born in the brood nest and performs her first duties there, making it her point of origin and initial workplace.</data>
      <data key="d8">development,origin,workplace</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Orientation Flights">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">House bees are the specific type of worker bee that undertakes orientation flights to prepare for life outside the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">developmental activity,training</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="The Hive Entrance">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The work of a house bee gradually progresses towards the hive entrance, which is the location from which it takes its orientation flights.</data>
      <data key="d8">movement,spatial progression,transition point</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Brood Rearing">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Brood rearing is a fundamental task performed by house bees as part of their phase of development within the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">division of labor,life stage,primary function</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Colony Disruption">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">In response to a colony disruption that kills foragers, house bees will mature early to graduate and take up foraging, restoring the colony's balance.</data>
      <data key="d8">accelerated maturation,adaptive response,social resilience</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Comb Building">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Comb building is a seasonal task performed by house bees inside the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">division of labor,hive construction,seasonal task</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Nectar">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">House Bees are responsible for receiving loads of Nectar from foraging bees and performing the crucial task of processing it to convert it into honey.</data>
