      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Foraging">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">House Bees influence the collective Foraging behavior by providing feedback to field bees on nectar quality; they unload high-quality nectar eagerly and low-quality nectar reluctantly, thus guiding foragers to better sources.</data>
      <data key="d8">behavioral influence,feedback loop,quality control</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6f51ec44f0c17ad5253b21395cf12591</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Forager Bee">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Forager Bees transfer their collected nectar to House Bees inside the hive. The speed of this transfer provides feedback to the Forager Bee about the quality of the nectar.</data>
      <data key="d8">communication,quality control,resource transfer</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6f51ec44f0c17ad5253b21395cf12591</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="House Bee" target="Honey Processing">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">House Bees are the members of the colony that perform the event of Honey Processing, converting nectar into honey.</data>
      <data key="d8">agent of action,resource conversion,role</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6f51ec44f0c17ad5253b21395cf12591</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Field Bee" target="Foraging">
      <data key="d6">30.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Foraging for nectar, pollen, and other resources is the primary and defining activity of a field bee.&lt;SEP&gt;Foraging is the primary activity and purpose of the field bee phase of a worker's life.&lt;SEP&gt;The primary and defining activity of a field bee is to engage in foraging, where it collects essential resources for the colony.</data>
      <data key="d8">behavior,division of labor,food gathering,primary function,resource collection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65de87b95deadb72c4827d5a3bd2f316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c389aa55b6d5b4c773f2c917b36e7a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Field Bee" target="Orientation Flights">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Orientation flights are a necessary preparation for a house bee to become a field bee, as they allow the bee to learn its way home and strengthen its flight muscles.</data>
      <data key="d8">life stage transition,preparation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-78182a0a75dac1ecf9d9f1cc16f3a0ff</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Field Bee" target="Nectar">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Field bees are responsible for collecting nectar from flowers, one of the key raw materials for the colony.</data>
