    </edge>
    <edge source="Brood Nest" target="Frames">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The brood nest is physically located on the frames within the hive; the number of frames containing brood is a direct measure of the nest's size and colony's strength.&lt;SEP&gt;The brood nest is the area of the hive where young are raised, and it is physically located on and expands across multiple frames within the hive bodies.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony assessment,colony structure,containment,spatial organization,spatial relationship,structural component</data>
