      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Swarm Control" target="The New Season">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text identifies swarm control as a new or emphasized technique that a beekeeper must learn and apply during 'The New Season' as the colony matures.</data>
      <data key="d8">advanced management,seasonal challenge,skill development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0385df8773cab416fd9b294da95cf91d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Workers">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Workers control the queen's condition before a swarm by reducing her food intake to slim her down for flight and ceasing stimulation to halt her egg-laying. They also harass her to prepare her for departure.</data>
      <data key="d8">behavioral control,colony dynamics,swarm preparation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ee196747c63e46006af016f7f2104f8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Package Of Bees">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A commercial package of bees contains a queen, who is housed separately in her own small cage within the package.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony structure,component</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f3a9f95df2c28cf16cc0339d5b436227</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Queen Cage">
      <data key="d6">39.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Queen Cage is a specific piece of equipment used to house and transport a Queen. It is designed for her safety and to facilitate her safe and gradual introduction to a new colony. The Queen is initially housed within the Queen Cage, a process which allows the hive's bees to acclimate to her presence. Once the bees have accepted her, the Queen can be released from the cage into the colony.</data>
      <data key="d8">acceptance,containment,equipment,housing,introduction,introduction method,queen acceptance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6b1093c60c117041d669d3950218419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50100ec9bbd638fb693fc24eeb2b3110&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Worker Bees">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Worker bees act as attendants to the queen within the queen cage, keeping her groomed and fed.</data>
      <data key="d8">care,hierarchy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Supplier">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The supplier is responsible for providing a live, healthy queen and is expected to replace her if she arrives dead.&lt;SEP&gt;The supplier is responsible for providing a live, healthy queen and must be contacted if she is dead on arrival.</data>
      <data key="d8">provision,responsibility,warranty</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Installing A Package Of Bees">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The careful installation of the queen in her cage is a critical first step in the overall process of installing a package of bees.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony establishment,process component</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f6b1093c60c117041d669d3950218419</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="First Inspection">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The primary goal of the First Inspection is to check on the Queen and confirm that she has been released from her cage.</data>
      <data key="d8">inspection goal,queen release,verification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Second Inspection">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The main objective of the Second Inspection is to verify that the Queen is laying eggs, which is the key indicator of her successful integration into the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">inspection goal,queen laying,verification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Hive Inspection">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The primary purpose of a hive inspection is to verify the queen's health and productivity, which is done by looking for the brood she has laid rather than finding the queen herself.</data>
      <data key="d8">assessment,monitoring,verification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-50100ec9bbd638fb693fc24eeb2b3110</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Eggs">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The queen is the sole producer of eggs within the colony. The text explicitly states to look for eggs as the primary evidence of her activity.</data>
      <data key="d8">creation,evidence,reproduction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-50100ec9bbd638fb693fc24eeb2b3110</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Brood Pattern">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The quality of the brood pattern on the comb is a direct indicator of the queen's health and laying effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d8">health indicator,performance assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-50100ec9bbd638fb693fc24eeb2b3110</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Fall Requeening">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"Fall requeening is the management practice of actively replacing the colony's current queen with a new, young one to correct performance issues and prepare the colony for winter."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d8">colony management,queen replacement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen" target="Drones">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Drones are male bees whose purpose is to mate with the queen during her mating flights, providing the sperm she stores in her spermatheca.</data>
      <data key="d8">mating,reproduction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6550c1217ac242a6cb1c3d9a5de5ee35</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740511</data>
    </edge>
