      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Honey Super">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The addition of a honey super is timed to coincide with the main nectar flow, allowing the bees to store surplus honey. Beekeepers should stop feeding the hive when supers are on.</data>
      <data key="d8">honey production,resource management,timing</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="The Beekeeper's Area">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The specific timing and characteristics of the nectar flow are dependent on the flora within the beekeeper's geographical area.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental dependency,local conditions,seasonality</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Feeding">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The start of a primary nectar flow is the natural signal for a beekeeper to stop feeding the colony, as the bees will switch to the abundant natural resources.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping trigger,resource management,seasonality</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b902e3da084c9ce16ad8c497c00c21e2</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Supering">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The success and timing of supering are directly dependent on the Nectar Flow, as bees will not produce wax or draw out comb to store honey without the stimulus of incoming nectar.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony activity,resource management,timing dependency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Bee Colony">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Bee Colony's behavior is heavily influenced by the Nectar Flow; its presence stimulates wax production and expansion, while its absence halts these activities.</data>
      <data key="d8">behavioral trigger,environmental stimulus,resource dependency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Geographic Area">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The characteristics of the Nectar Flow, including its timing, duration, and whether there are multiple flows, are determined by the beekeeper's Geographic Area.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental dependency,local conditions,seasonality</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Wax Production">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text explicitly states that Wax Production is stimulated by the incoming nectar of a Nectar Flow, establishing a direct causal link: 'no nectar, no wax'.</data>
      <data key="d8">biological trigger,causal relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-96d3190b056360cfac9d6ae0c079078e</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Fall Requeening">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"Fall requeening should be completed before the nectar flow ends for the year to ensure the new queen is established and laying eggs while resources are still available."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d8">colony management,timing</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Food Stores">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"The end of the nectar flow signals the time for beekeepers to evaluate the hive's food stores and determine if feeding is necessary to ensure the colony has enough resources for winter."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d8">resource assessment,seasonal trigger</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-59970fe46f1c3b11508247730ae6145d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nectar Flow" target="Supers">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The absence of a nectar flow is a condition that leads to supers being unoccupied by bees, creating an ideal environment for wax moths to move in.</data>
