    <edge source="Water" target="Livestock">
      <data key="d6">39.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Based on the information provided, water is critical for the survival and health of livestock. This is because animals are largely composed of water and can die from a loss of just one-tenth of it. Livestock have a direct dependency on water, requiring vast amounts daily, with a single cow, for example, drinking 50 to 90 gallons. This high consumption rate makes a reliable water source crucial for any farm with animals. While natural sources like rain and snow can provide this fundamental requirement for free, the importance of this relationship is formally recognized through index entries such as 'Water for livestock'.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal husbandry,biological need,dependency,resource,resource dependency,resource management,resource requirement,survival,water consumption</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef577d840302c2f3d95d7cb5a8f77433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f3d99de4967b60e7e74b3639abc430c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a7d4e49c6e48a2727071f21a879ba</data>
