    </edge>
    <edge source="Comb" target="Crushing Method">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text identifies a major disadvantage of the crushing method is that it destroys the comb, forcing the bees to rebuild it from scratch the next season.</data>
      <data key="d8">destruction,process impact</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Comb" target="New Foundation">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">When the comb is destroyed by a process like the crushing method, beekeepers must provide a new foundation for the bees to build upon in the following season.</data>
      <data key="d8">consequence,replacement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9fe3ef9f53a3c23c8d05dafdfe1c88f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Comb" target="Frames">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Frames are the structures that hold the comb, which is the delicate beeswax structure containing the honey.</data>
