      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hive Location" target="Exposure">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The quality of a Hive Location is determined by its Exposure to environmental factors like sun, wind, and traffic. The text advises choosing a location that minimizes negative exposure.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental factors,site assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-048ad5fead1e52a66cfd2e40b5467d7b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hive Location" target="Neighbors">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The choice of a Hive Location must take into account the potential apprehension of Neighbors, implying that a discreet or well-placed hive is preferable to avoid conflict.</data>
      <data key="d8">community relations,site consideration</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-048ad5fead1e52a66cfd2e40b5467d7b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hive Location" target="Wind">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A suitable Hive Location must offer protection from excessive Wind, especially during winter. If the location is naturally windy, a windbreak is recommended.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental protection,site selection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-048ad5fead1e52a66cfd2e40b5467d7b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Animals" target="Beekeeper's Attire">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text advises that a beekeeper's choice of attire should not resemble animal fur (woolly or hairy fabrics) to avoid triggering a defensive response from bees that may have been previously harassed by animals like skunks or bears.</data>
      <data key="d8">material choice,mimicry avoidance,threat association</data>
