    <edge source="Livestock" target="Farm Labor">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The selection and management of livestock are directly influenced by the need to minimize farm labor. The author chooses self-sufficient animals, like Katahdin Hair sheep, to reduce tasks such as shearing and intensive health care.&lt;SEP&gt;The text provides detailed charts on the farm labor, measured in hours per animal unit per year, required to raise various types of livestock.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal husbandry,labor reduction,labor requirement,livestock management,operational efficiency</data>
