      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Time Management">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Time management is applied to livestock breeding cycles, such as limiting a bull's time with cows to 60 days, in order to achieve a close calving season and a uniform calf crop.</data>
      <data key="d8">breeding cycle,herd management,scheduling</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9b7a7522a05ce3cf5aba22a772ae6607</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Farmer Skills">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Farmer skills, especially veterinary and stockman skills, are directly applied to maintain the health of livestock, assist with births, and handle the animals efficiently and with low stress.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal care,health management,husbandry</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9b7a7522a05ce3cf5aba22a772ae6607</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Farm Resources">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Livestock are dependent on farm resources for their survival and well-being, requiring adequate shelter (buildings), feed (pastures), and access to a good water system.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal welfare,resource dependency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9b7a7522a05ce3cf5aba22a772ae6607</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Record Keeping">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Record keeping is used to track the performance and costs associated with individual livestock, such as feed costs and birth rates, which is essential for calculating profitability.</data>
      <data key="d8">performance tracking,profitability analysis</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9b7a7522a05ce3cf5aba22a772ae6607</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Gentle Livestock">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Gentle livestock are presented as the ideal type of livestock to raise, as their temperament leads to better productivity, easier handling, and reduced stress for both the animals and the farmer.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal behavior,herd management,productivity</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9b7a7522a05ce3cf5aba22a772ae6607</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Culling">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Culling is presented as an important and necessary management practice when raising herd-type livestock.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal selection,herd management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9b7a7522a05ce3cf5aba22a772ae6607</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Water System">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A good water system is described as essential for livestock, and having one where animals can access water directly is preferable to the farmer hauling it.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal welfare,infrastructure,resource provision</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9b7a7522a05ce3cf5aba22a772ae6607</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Norfolk Rotation">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Norfolk Rotation is noted for its ability to integrate Livestock, such as sheep and cattle, by including a legume for grazing or hay.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural system,livestock integration</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5b320d4bf5bae3f28f4bca97246cd735</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740867</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Long-Term Crop Rotations">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Long-term crop rotations are distinguished by their common inclusion of hay and sod crops, which are utilized by livestock.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural system,livestock integration</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5b320d4bf5bae3f28f4bca97246cd735</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740867</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Crop Rotation">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text argues that livestock are a necessary component of a balanced rotation, as they contribute to soil fertility and help manage labor and land use effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;The text presents crop rotation, which includes pasture, as a system that provides the opportunity for feeding livestock.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural synergy,animal feed,integrated farming,system balance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ee261677ef65b4f0bf53fae46bfcfb75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66ffae2696b4f9024085ef90af5320a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740867</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Pasture">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Pasture's main purpose, as described in the text, is to serve as feed for livestock, either through direct grazing or by being cut for hay.</data>
      <data key="d8">food source,land use</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b66ffae2696b4f9024085ef90af5320a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740867</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Livestock" target="Southwestern Texas">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The region of Southwestern Texas is used as an example of how a specific arid climate supports a particular type of agriculture, namely the year-round grazing of livestock on native grasses.</data>
      <data key="d8">climate adaptation,grazing,regional agriculture</data>
