    <edge source="Skunks" target="Beehive">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Skunks are predators that attack the beehive entrance at night to catch and eat individual bees, weakening the colony and causing it to become more irritable.</data>
      <data key="d8">colony attrition,hive attack,predator-prey</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740508</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Skunks" target="Skunk Defenses">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Skunk Defenses, such as poultry netting or tacks, are specifically designed to deter skunks by creating uncomfortable footing, thereby preventing them from attacking the hive.</data>
      <data key="d8">defense mechanism,deterrent,predator control</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
