      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Honey Supers" target="Frames">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Frames are a necessary internal component of Honey Supers, just as they are for hive bodies, holding the foundation for honey comb.&lt;SEP&gt;Honey supers are the boxes designed to hold frames for honey collection. The text emphasizes the importance of using the correct size frames for the chosen super size to ensure proper fit and function.</data>
      <data key="d8">equipment compatibility,hive component,hive components,internal structure</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0a230cf3f43e673f8797237bc5d97548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a7084302d57591ff02e89969b4c3abd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Honey Supers" target="Terramycin">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The administration of Terramycin is explicitly forbidden when Honey Supers are on the hive, to prevent the contamination of honey.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping practice,honey safety,treatment restriction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-850b95b5ab1cf1d4aef287383ef1ecfe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Honey Supers" target="Menthol">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text explicitly forbids the use of Menthol treatment while honey supers are on the hive to prevent the contamination of the honey crop.&lt;SEP&gt;The text explicitly states that there can be no honey supers on the hive during the 14 days of menthol treatment to avoid contaminating the honey crop.</data>
      <data key="d8">contamination risk,food safety,treatment constraint,treatment restriction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a9a7dd90fa19da1cc0a36d8589ee8cd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Honey Supers" target="Miticur">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Miticur treatment is required to be applied only after the honey supers have been removed from the hive to prevent contamination of the honey crop.&lt;SEP&gt;The use of Miticur is prohibited while honey supers are in place to protect the honey from contamination. It is intended for use after the honey crop has been removed.</data>
      <data key="d8">application timing,contamination risk,food safety,treatment constraint,treatment restriction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4c20cb47e818c53af03d9f00b71d1b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a9a7dd90fa19da1cc0a36d8589ee8cd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Honey Supers" target="Honey Crop">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The honey crop is the surplus honey that bees store in the honey supers, which are later removed from the hive for harvesting.</data>
      <data key="d8">beekeeping equipment,harvesting,honey production</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7a9a7dd90fa19da1cc0a36d8589ee8cd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
