    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen Cage" target="Candy Plug">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The candy plug is a functional component of the queen cage, used as food and to facilitate a delayed release of the queen.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,timed release</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen Cage" target="Metal Disk">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The metal disk is the mechanism used to suspend the queen cage inside the package and must be manipulated to remove the cage.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,suspension</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen Cage" target="Tools">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A tool like a thin nail or jackknife is used to poke a hole in the candy plug of the queen cage to assist the bees.</data>
      <data key="d8">assistance,manipulation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen Cage" target="Candy">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Candy acts as a consumable plug for the Queen Cage, creating a timed release as the bees eat through it.&lt;SEP&gt;The candy serves as a timed-release plug for the queen cage, which the bees must eat through to free the queen.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,function,release mechanism</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f6b1093c60c117041d669d3950218419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen Cage" target="Drawn Comb">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text gives a specific instruction not to jam the queen cage's screen into the drawn comb to ensure the colony's bees can communicate with the queen before her release.</data>
      <data key="d8">bee communication,placement instruction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f6b1093c60c117041d669d3950218419</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Queen Cage" target="First Inspection">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A primary task during the First Inspection is for the beekeeper to locate and remove the empty Queen Cage after the queen has been released.</data>
      <data key="d8">hive maintenance,object removal,procedure</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ff7d8f22cb1bb72cdb48f20d4975e8d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Feeder Can" target="Tools">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Tools such as pliers (or the beekeeper's fingers) are used to pull the feeder can out of the package.</data>
      <data key="d8">manipulation,removal</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c3e0c4c99d600e81552689af79afdcd</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740472</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Candy Plug" target="Marshmallow">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A marshmallow is suggested as a direct replacement for the candy plug if the original is missing or consumed.</data>
      <data key="d8">contingency,substitution</data>
