    </edge>
    <edge source="The Africanized Bee" target="European Honey Bees">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Africanized bee is a crossbreed that resulted from the mating of escaped African bee drones with the queens of European honey bee colonies kept in the Americas.</data>
      <data key="d8">crossbreeding,hybridization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740508</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="The Africanized Bee" target="Experimental Breeding Program">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An accidental error during the experimental breeding program, which allowed African queens to escape and swarm, was the direct cause of the creation of the Africanized bee population.</data>
      <data key="d8">accidental release,causality,origin event</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ee734f0540c7fd5dab112e837ae5a36b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740508</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="The Africanized Bee" target="Central America">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Africanized bee's migration path from South America went through Central America on its way north.</data>
      <data key="d8">geographic spread,species migration</data>
