    <edge source="Corn" target="Rye">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An example of a short-term rotation involves seeding Rye into a standing Corn crop.&lt;SEP&gt;Rye is sown as a cover crop in standing corn. After the corn harvest, the rye provides ground cover and is later plowed under to make its absorbed nitrogen available for the next crop.</data>
      <data key="d8">cover cropping,crop rotation,crop sequence,nutrient cycling</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8b6332789cdbd68f546cf7328c6217fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b320d4bf5bae3f28f4bca97246cd735</data>
