    <edge source="Corn" target="_ka-tunqwa_">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Hopi term _ka-tunqwa_ is used to describe a dead corn stalk, creating a direct linguistic and spiritual link between the life cycle of corn and the life cycle of humans.</data>
