    </edge>
    <edge source="Small Farms" target="Rural Crisis of the 1980s">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Rural Crisis of the 1980s prompted a reevaluation of industrial farming, leading many surviving and new farmers to adopt the diversified, niche-market strategies characteristic of modern Small Farms.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural shift,economic catalyst,resilience</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fbeff72000d21039cdbac6ba65f75077</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Small Farms" target="Consolidation of Agricultural Processing">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The rise of Small Farms, which often use direct marketing, represents a counter-movement to the trend of Consolidation of Agricultural Processing by creating alternative food systems outside the control of large corporations.</data>
      <data key="d8">corporate control,market dynamics,opposing trends</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fbeff72000d21039cdbac6ba65f75077</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Small Farms" target="Paul B. Frederic">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Paul B. Frederic's theory that proximity to markets is critical for farm function helps explain the success of modern Small Farms, which are often located within 40-50 miles of cities for direct marketing.</data>
      <data key="d8">academic theory,geographical influence,market strategy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fbeff72000d21039cdbac6ba65f75077</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Small Farms" target="Terminator Gene">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The terminator gene technology directly threatens the self-sufficiency of farms, particularly small farms, by making it impossible to save seeds and forcing reliance on large seed companies.</data>
      <data key="d8">corporate dependence,economic threat,seed sovereignty</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fbeff72000d21039cdbac6ba65f75077</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Small Farms" target="West">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text contrasts the direct-market small farms that thrive near cities with the traditional, large-scale cattle ranching that occurs in the more remote ranges of the West.</data>
      <data key="d8">farming models,geographical contrast</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fbeff72000d21039cdbac6ba65f75077</data>
