    <edge source="Small Farms" target="Appalachian">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text contrasts the direct-market small farms located near cities with the traditional subsistence farming practiced by Appalachian farmers in more remote areas.</data>
      <data key="d8">farming models,geographical contrast</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fbeff72000d21039cdbac6ba65f75077</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Knowledge" target="Farm Resources">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text explicitly identifies knowledge as a key on-farm resource, alongside land, labor, and capital, that is supplied by the operator.</data>
      <data key="d8">intellectual capital,resource identification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-17984d082222b7d2f1526b0b77119804</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Knowledge" target="Balanced Farming">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text explains that a balanced farming operation provides the farmer with the necessary time to acquire knowledge, which in turn improves the farm's procedures and profitability.</data>
      <data key="d8">operational improvement,synergistic relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-17984d082222b7d2f1526b0b77119804</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Knowledge" target="The Author">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Author identifies knowledge as the single most important resource for a farmer, stating that it underpins all successful management decisions.</data>
      <data key="d8">core principle,resource management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f0a5052e04a7b64a097459ad1bd8a957</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Knowledge" target="Sustainable Agriculture">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text implies that applying principles of sustainable agriculture requires the farmer to first acquire knowledge through reading, attending seminars, and other forms of learning.</data>
      <data key="d8">enabling principle,informed practice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f0a5052e04a7b64a097459ad1bd8a957</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Knowledge" target="University Libraries">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The author recommends University Libraries as a key place for farmers to acquire historical knowledge and research to inform their management practices.</data>
      <data key="d8">information source,research</data>
