      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The historical consolidation of grain production and processing in the Midwest led to the decline of local grain economies in other parts of the country, creating the need for the rebuilding efforts described in the text.</data>
      <data key="d8">cause and effect,economic consolidation,historical context</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-5d4150698732f393c235b8b3e1cb2d88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Midwest" target="Country Natural Beef">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The cooperative model of Country Natural Beef was established as an alternative to the massive Midwest feedlots, contrasting small-scale, humane ranching with industrial agriculture.</data>
      <data key="d8">alternative model,ideological contrast</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-104466acc0eb6f55c05f02aa258ea31a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Midwest" target="Doc and Connie Hatfield">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Hatfields sought to create a ranching model that was a viable alternative to the dominant system of massive Midwest feedlots.</data>
      <data key="d8">founding motivation,ideological contrast</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-104466acc0eb6f55c05f02aa258ea31a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Midwest" target="Oren Molovinsky">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Oren Molovinsky found it illogical for D.C. restaurants to buy meat from the Midwest when high-quality products were available locally in Virginia, a realization that drove his farm-to-table initiative.</data>
      <data key="d8">regional sourcing,supply chain critique</data>
