      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Climate Zones">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Climate zones are a critical factor in determining which crops can be successfully cultivated in a specific location based on plant hardiness.</data>
      <data key="d8">agriculture,climate suitability,planning</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2f3d99de4967b60e7e74b3639abc430c</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Microclimates">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Microclimates allow a farmer to cultivate specific crops that would not normally survive in the larger climate zone, creating opportunities for a niche market.</data>
      <data key="d8">climate adaptation,cultivation,niche market</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2f3d99de4967b60e7e74b3639abc430c</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Free Energy Sources">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Practices related to crops, such as crop rotations and using green manure, are listed as examples of free energy sources that improve soil health and sustainability.</data>
      <data key="d8">resource management,soil health,sustainable agriculture</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-2f3d99de4967b60e7e74b3639abc430c</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="University Extension Office">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The University Extension Office is a resource for farmers seeking advice on which crops will work best in their local area.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural guidance,expert advice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-454a001b38f4bf2cba51915cb1f4804e</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Temperature">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Temperature is a primary factor that determines which crops can grow in a region, what their life cycle is (annual or perennial), and how much water they lose through transpiration.</data>
      <data key="d8">climate dependency,plant growth,regional agriculture</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740869</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Mesophytes">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mesophytes, which require moderate water, are described as the category that includes most commonly grown crops, such as corn.</data>
      <data key="d8">agriculture,classification,plant science</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740869</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Wheat">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Wheat is an example of a crop whose growth cycle is specifically tied to cold temperatures and snow.</data>
      <data key="d8">classification,climate dependency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740869</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Transpiration">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Transpiration is described as a key biological process in crops (and all plants) through which they lose immense amounts of water.</data>
      <data key="d8">biological process,water loss</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740870</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Soil">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text establishes a fundamental relationship where crops grow in soil, relying on it for physical support and for the transfer of water and minerals to their roots.</data>
      <data key="d8">dependency,growth medium,nutrient source</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-033bfeab9bfaed05ef236ddef40c557b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740870</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Climate">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"Climate dictates the viability and needs of crops. The text explains that crop choice depends on climate and that water requirements are highest during specific growth periods, making the timing of rainfall crucial."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural dependency,water management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-50ae2b642515d199b40d344346490776</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740870</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Parasites">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">"Parasites, in the form of diseases like tomato blight and rust, directly attack and damage crops, leading to yellowing leaves, reduced production, or even death of the plant. Rust is noted to cut wheat yield in half."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d8">crop disease,yield loss</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-50ae2b642515d199b40d344346490776</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740870</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Windbreak">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text explains that windbreaks are used to protect crops from wind, which helps them retain heat and moisture and use nutrients more efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural practice,crop protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-1cbfa7273b78ee011a6cb142bb82745a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740870</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Anna Edey">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Anna Edey's primary business involves growing crops, specifically producing 80 to 100 pounds of salad greens per week in her greenhouse.</data>
      <data key="d8">commercial farming,crop production</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-419d5c5d2a7c161df014b3fadb6e4529</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740875</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Solviva">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Solviva greenhouse is used for the large-scale production of crops, yielding 80 to 100 pounds of salad greens weekly.</data>
      <data key="d8">agriculture,food production</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-419d5c5d2a7c161df014b3fadb6e4529</data>
