      <data key="d11">1753740879</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Soil Health">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text establishes a direct link between soil health practices (like using cover crops and fertilizer) and the successful cultivation of primary cash crops, positioning soil preparation as a prerequisite for planting.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural practice,crop yield,soil preparation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bfed52d46f5bf9d5489c4d6b6dddd2cb</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740879</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Diversity">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The principle of diversity is partially defined by the practice of 'raising both crops and livestock, and more than one kind of each,' making crops a fundamental component of a diversified farm.</data>
      <data key="d8">definitional,enterprise selection,farm composition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-04b17869172fff33b1c7bc2284173657</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740880</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crops" target="Reserves">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Crops, such as hay and potatoes, are used as a direct example of how to build reserves by storing surplus from a good year to cover a bad one or by adding value.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural practice,economic stability,resource storage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8c58f4785be38b80316bcdb547edbe48</data>
