    <edge source="Crop Rotation" target="Soil Fertility">
      <data key="d6">29.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Crop Rotation is presented as a primary method for maintaining and improving Soil Fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Crop rotations are a key method for enhancing soil fertility, specifically by using legumes to fix nitrogen and by building up humus in the soil.&lt;SEP&gt;The text explicitly and repeatedly states that the primary purpose of crop rotation is to maintain and improve soil fertility by managing nutrients, organic matter, and soil structure.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural benefit,agricultural practice,core principle,soil health,soil improvement,soil management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ee261677ef65b4f0bf53fae46bfcfb75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bb17f477fad911f5e90130ee2a67840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b320d4bf5bae3f28f4bca97246cd735</data>
