      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crop Rotation" target="Soil">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Crop rotation is a primary method for maintaining and improving soil health. It builds organic matter, restores nitrogen, improves drainage and water-holding capacity, and reduces erosion.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural practice,fertility,soil management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f407f39fbfb8d8caa0eba09a242cee00</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740865</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Crop Rotation" target="Legumes">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Legumes are a fundamental component of the crop rotation systems described in the text, used to add nitrogen and improve soil fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Legumes are a key component of crop rotation systems because they fix nitrogen in the soil, replenishing a nutrient that other crops, like corn, deplete.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural cycle,agricultural system,crop synergy,nitrogen fixation,soil improvement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f407f39fbfb8d8caa0eba09a242cee00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66ffae2696b4f9024085ef90af5320a</data>
