    <edge source="Soil Fertility" target="Agriculture">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Maintaining and improving soil fertility is described as a fundamental, long-term goal essential for the sustainability and productivity of an agricultural operation.</data>
      <data key="d8">core goal,land management,sustainability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e9d3e2ae9649f6dc7e9301ed98bc01d7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740876</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Soil Fertility" target="Soil-Conserving Tillage Methods">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Soil-conserving tillage methods, such as using cover crops and green manures, are the practical techniques employed to achieve the long-term goal of improving soil fertility.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural technique,land management,soil health</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e9d3e2ae9649f6dc7e9301ed98bc01d7</data>
