    <edge source="Bacteria" target="Rhizobium">
      <data key="d6">19.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Rhizobium is explicitly called a 'nitrogen-fixing bacterium'.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhizobium takes nitrogen from the air and converts it to a form that plants can utilize, which is a key function performed by bacteria in the soil.</data>
