    <edge source="Alternative Agriculture" target="Traditional Agriculture">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Alternative agriculture is presented as a distinct approach that is less dependent on climate than traditional agriculture, highlighting a key difference between the two farming philosophies.&lt;SEP&gt;The text defines Alternative Agriculture in direct opposition to Traditional Agriculture, contrasting their approaches to market identification, pricing (retail vs. wholesale), and product form (value-added vs. commodity). A central theme is the superiority of the alternative model for small farm profitability.</data>
