    <edge source="Elk" target="Chickens, Broilers">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">This relationship compares two enterprises based on labor efficiency (profit per hour). The Elk operation is extremely efficient, generating approximately $396 per hour of labor ($3566/9hrs), while the Broiler Chicken operation is one of the least efficient, at about $9 per hour ($4688/500hrs). This highlights a critical metric for assessing business viability.</data>
      <data key="d8">Labor Efficiency,Profit per Hour,Return on Investment</data>
