    <edge source="Troy Gardens" target="The Coalition">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Coalition was formed specifically to prevent the development of the land that became Troy Gardens. They created the collaborative plan that defined its five distinct functions: farm, gardens, prairie, wilderness, and affordable housing.&lt;SEP&gt;The development of Troy Gardens into its current form, including affordable housing, was a direct result of compromises and agreements made among the members of the original coalition.</data>
      <data key="d8">advocacy,collaborative design,creation,land use planning,negotiation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-463bc71b9c03d72246d0c3904090b54a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Troy Gardens" target="Madison, Wisconsin">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Troy Gardens is located within the city limits of Madison, Wisconsin. The city also provided a crucial low-interest loan that allowed the coalition to purchase the land.</data>
      <data key="d8">financial support,location,municipal partnership</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-463bc71b9c03d72246d0c3904090b54a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
