    </edge>
    <edge source="Lynchburg Grows" target="Van Ness">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Van Ness is a co-founder of Lynchburg Grows who used his professional expertise as an environmental lawyer to acquire the land and lead the effort to address its soil contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Van Ness is a representative or member of Lynchburg Grows who is quoted expressing pride in the organization's community-centric approach to its projects.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental remediation,founding,leadership,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a0ebf31ca8cf0e8a5dbe6d09c3efa272&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9189adec7b34964ca2342aea2d2b666e</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lynchburg Grows" target="Virginia Department of Environmental Quality (DEQ)">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Lynchburg Grows received critical assistance from the DEQ, which managed the brownfields program that funded and conducted the full site assessment, enabling the farm to operate safely.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental regulation,government assistance,site assessment</data>
