    <edge source="Chefs" target="Molovinsky">
      <data key="d6">23.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky acts as a mentor to other chefs, teaching them how to work with whole animals, create dishes from various cuts, and helping them transition their restaurants towards this model.&lt;SEP&gt;Molovinsky explains that the way to appeal to chefs is by offering them unique, high-quality local meats, which appeals to their desire to be distinctive and creates a competitive advantage.&lt;SEP&gt;Molovinsky plans to focus on helping more chefs learn how to cook 'whole animal' once the cooperative has dedicated administrative staff.</data>
      <data key="d8">education,industry development,mentorship,professional motivation,skill development,strategic influence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7ef5e8f2029677f15d6ee8815b5828c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65dc312cbeeaa82060b27a69060e671d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9f558ccef1d0a97c2f1550636dc3f28</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chefs" target="Whole-Animal Approach">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky argues that chefs have the immense buying power to lead and accelerate the whole-animal movement, more so than consumers.</data>
      <data key="d8">industry leadership,purchasing power</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7ef5e8f2029677f15d6ee8815b5828c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chefs" target="Purveyors">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
