    <edge source="Sheep (Ewe And Lamb)" target="Sheep, Feeder Lamb">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">These represent two different approaches to sheep farming. The 'Ewe and Lamb' model involves breeding, while the 'Feeder Lamb' model involves fattening purchased lambs. The breeding model has a higher net profit ($90.25) than the fattening model ($14.02) per unit, but also higher labor.</data>
      <data key="d8">business model comparison,livestock production</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a6d072f41d662cb326c1c528ac3c5c51</data>
