    <edge source="Appalachian Sustainable Agriculture Project (ASAP)" target="Charlie Jackson">
      <data key="d6">50.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Charlie Jackson founded the Appalachian Sustainable Agriculture Project (ASAP) in 1995 and serves as its director. In his leadership role, he is responsible for shaping the organization's strategic direction and initiatives, articulating its philosophy and goals, and speaking on its behalf. Jackson leads ASAP's mission to create local markets for farmers, with a particular focus on cultivating the next generation of farmers. He also provides high-level commentary on the program's success. The Appalachian Sustainable Agriculture Project (ASAP) is the parent organization of the Growing Minds program.</data>
      <data key="d8">employment,founder,leadership,mission-driven,organizational oversight,organizational strategy,strategic vision</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-30c38b37fe24e15bfa43a713c9e38509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fee18f76430d121ab613984069f209e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5944a88ca415780f3d4838a47d068512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6eed415e2d01ca41ab07d4cac89623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c16ea96bc625614680cc6d8276e6ca</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
