    <edge source="Amy Ager" target="Hickory Nut Gap Farm">
      <data key="d6">49.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Amy Ager is the co-owner of Hickory Nut Gap Farm, which she co-manages and co-runs with her husband, Jamie Ager. Serving as a key spokesperson and representative for the farm, she articulates its business philosophy and strategies, particularly regarding agritourism and marketing. Ager also shares insights based on the farm's experiences and discusses its diversified business plan as a key to achieving long-term stability.</data>
      <data key="d8">business strategy,farm management,leadership,ownership,partnership,personnel,representation,spokesperson,stewardship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4d53cc613c52fd5080e556f9abb248a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f188db350c6a6f2fdb22a9e9283e4dc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcbabc72a18ceaedb14452609db7d256&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e970626c7a63b367949cb5600957bcab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e930a3eb466e9bb1dfa38b0df50bfd3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Amy Ager" target="Livestock Production">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Amy Ager provides expert advice on the business aspects of livestock production, based on her experiences.</data>
      <data key="d8">business advice,expertise</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bcbabc72a18ceaedb14452609db7d256</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Amy Ager" target="Starting Small">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Amy Ager's concluding advice for farmers is to adopt the strategy of starting small and growing slowly to learn the business effectively.</data>
      <data key="d8">business strategy,expert advice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bcbabc72a18ceaedb14452609db7d256</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Amy Ager" target="Business Savvy">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Amy Ager emphasizes that farmers need to develop business savvy, including understanding all aspects of the meat business, to be treated as professionals by customers.</data>
      <data key="d8">expert advice,professional development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bcbabc72a18ceaedb14452609db7d256</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
