    <edge source="Amy Ager" target="Jamie Ager">
      <data key="d6">60.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Amy Ager and Jamie Ager are a husband and wife who work as partners to co-own and operate Hickory Nut Gap Farm and the associated Hickory Nut Gap Meats business. Their professional partnership began when they attended college together, which led them to co-write the business plan and co-found the farm. As a family, they run the farm by fulfilling complementary roles and sharing a unified philosophy and vision for post-industrial agriculture. Amy and Jamie Ager also share insights on the challenges and opportunities of agritourism.</data>
      <data key="d8">association,business collaboration,business partnership,collaboration,family business,family farming,family partnership,family relationship,marriage,partnership,shared philosophy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4d53cc613c52fd5080e556f9abb248a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f188db350c6a6f2fdb22a9e9283e4dc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f712d3550c8612228f9fb4dc999ba9b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e970626c7a63b367949cb5600957bcab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062d9ac74f75199c91576d982ab5a9f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14c8f3e81fd6708a9852f46f0d4ac0a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e930a3eb466e9bb1dfa38b0df50bfd3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
