    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Polyface Farm">
      <data key="d6">33.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm and the Chipotle restaurant chain had a key supplier partnership in which Polyface Farm supplied pork to a local Chipotle restaurant in Charlottesville. This direct farm-to-business supply chain serves as a central case study for bridging the gap between small-scale sustainable agriculture and large-scale commercial demand. The relationship also highlights the challenges and pressures that a small, values-driven producer like Polyface Farm faces when working with a large, mainstream corporate customer. Additionally, the partnership with Chipotle is used as an example to explain Polyface Farm's guiding principle of not having sales targets and not actively pursuing market expansion.</data>
      <data key="d8">business partnership,business principle,farm-to-table,hypothetical relationship,local sourcing,market strategy,scaling challenge,supplier relationship,supply chain</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d31a2f89a77b64e0ae04120df1fdb3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80590371c3ba416132df035a1f48358</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Polyface">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Chipotle and Polyface formed a business partnership where the restaurant chain sourced pork from the small farm. This required significant collaboration on cooking methods, transportation, and packaging to overcome logistical hurdles.</data>
      <data key="d8">business partnership,collaboration,supply chain</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-63208f55f5e282db2dc1514f989da622</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Steve Ells">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Steve Ells is the leader of Chipotle, and his personal commitment and vision for food sourcing were the driving force that empowered his team and enabled the difficult partnership with Polyface to succeed.</data>
      <data key="d8">corporate vision,empowerment,leadership</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-63208f55f5e282db2dc1514f989da622</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Salatin">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Salatin, the owner of Polyface, was the direct supplier to Chipotle. He worked with the company to solve problems like inadequate packaging and expressed deep admiration for Chipotle's commitment and collaborative spirit.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,mutual respect,supplier relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-63208f55f5e282db2dc1514f989da622</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Charlottesville">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Chipotle's restaurant in Charlottesville served as the pilot location for its partnership with Polyface Farm, testing the introduction of locally sourced pork.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chipotle restaurant in Charlottesville served as the pilot location for the partnership with Polyface, implementing new equipment and recipes and ultimately becoming a top-performing store for pork sales.</data>
      <data key="d8">business location,local sourcing,market trial,pilot program</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63208f55f5e282db2dc1514f989da622</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Polyface's Buying Club">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Chipotle's ability to source beef from Polyface is directly challenged by Polyface's Buying Club, which offers Polyface a higher price for its beef, creating a supply and pricing conflict.</data>
      <data key="d8">market competition,pricing,supply chain conflict</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-63208f55f5e282db2dc1514f989da622</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="The Cold Chain">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Chipotle could not accept meat deliveries from Polyface without the assurance that the 'cold chain' was continually maintained at the proper temperature, making it a critical requirement for the partnership.</data>
      <data key="d8">food safety,quality control,supply chain requirements</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-63208f55f5e282db2dc1514f989da622</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Whole Animal Sales">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Chipotle's specific demand for pork hams/shoulders and beef middle portions helped Polyface Farm achieve its goal of Whole Animal Sales by creating a market for cuts that were slower-moving with other customers.</data>
      <data key="d8">market diversification,product utilization,supply and demand</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Petrilli">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Petrilli is a representative of Chipotle who manages the relationship with Polyface Farm and shares the lessons learned by the company from the experience.</data>
      <data key="d8">employment,management,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chipotle" target="Charlottesville Customers">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The feedback and confusion from Charlottesville Customers, who were not initially told about the Polyface pork experiment, forced Chipotle to change its strategy and become more transparent in its customer communications.</data>
      <data key="d8">communication strategy,customer feedback,market reaction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Virginia's Shenandoah Valley">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm is located in Virginia's Shenandoah Valley, a key part of its identity.</data>
      <data key="d8">location,regional agriculture</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dd285deff310269197e8718b28f6076b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Chipotle Mexican Grill">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm has a business relationship with Chipotle Mexican Grill, supplying the restaurant chain with its products.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyface Farm has a supplier relationship with Chipotle Mexican Grill, which serves as a key example in the text for the dynamics between small local farms and large corporate buyers.</data>
      <data key="d8">business partnership,case study,local sourcing,supplier relationship,supply chain</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd285deff310269197e8718b28f6076b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Pigs">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Pigs are integrated into the operations at Polyface Farm to serve the specific function of turning the farm's compost through their natural rooting instinct.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal labor,system integration</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dd285deff310269197e8718b28f6076b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Wall Street">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm's entire business model is defined by its opposition to the 'Wall Street' ethos of prioritizing scale and profit over ethics, land, and community.</data>
      <data key="d8">business ethics,core values,philosophical opposition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0d31a2f89a77b64e0ae04120df1fdb3b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Regulation">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The existing regulatory structure for meat processing directly and negatively impacts Polyface Farm's pricing. It forces the farm to pay significantly higher processing costs per pound than its industrial competitors, making it difficult to compete on price alone.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance burden,cost structure,economic disadvantage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0d31a2f89a77b64e0ae04120df1fdb3b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Ethics-Based Anti–Wall Street Contrarian Business Practices">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm created and operates under this specific set of principles. They were developed by the Salatin family to ensure the farm does not lose its core values as it faces pressures to scale up its operations.</data>
      <data key="d8">guiding principles,operational philosophy,value preservation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0d31a2f89a77b64e0ae04120df1fdb3b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Salatin">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Salatin is the farmer and public face of Polyface Farm, articulating its core philosophies on sustainable agriculture, biological time, and business strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;Salatin is the primary architect and spokesperson for Polyface Farm's guiding principles and business philosophy, shaping its entire operational model.</data>
      <data key="d8">business philosophy,founder,leadership,ownership,philosophy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="The Omnivore's Dilemma">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm was prominently featured as a model of sustainable agriculture in the book 'The Omnivore's Dilemma', which served as the primary driver of its national fame.</data>
      <data key="d8">case study,media feature,publicity</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Concentrated Animal Feeding Operations (CAFOs)">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm's methods are defined in direct opposition to the practices of CAFOs, particularly concerning waste management and operating within the land's ecological carrying capacity.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural model,philosophical contrast,sustainability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="U.S. Marketplace">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm's business model, particularly its openness and lack of patents, is presented as a direct alternative to the standard competitive practices of the wider U.S. marketplace.</data>
      <data key="d8">alternative model,business ethics,economic contrast</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Guiding Principles Of Polyface Farm">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm's entire operation and business philosophy are built upon its unique set of guiding principles, which dictate its approach to markets, growth, and sustainability.</data>
      <data key="d8">business model,core values,operational philosophy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Autonomous Workforce">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm uses the 'Autonomous Workforce' model for its staff, preferring a team of incentivized collaborators over traditional employees with salaries or hourly wages.</data>
      <data key="d8">compensation,employment model,labor strategy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Word Of Mouth">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm relies entirely on word of mouth for promotion, which forces the farm to maintain high quality and ensures its growth is based on customer satisfaction.</data>
      <data key="d8">customer evangelism,marketing strategy,quality control</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Ecological Carrying Capacity">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm's operations are strictly defined by the principle of ecological carrying capacity, which dictates that it must manage its own waste and support its local community's health.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental limits,operational principle,sustainability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Healing The Land">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">'Healing the land' is a core, stated mission of Polyface Farm, guiding its sustainable agricultural practices.</data>
      <data key="d8">land stewardship,mission,sustainability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Industrial Processing Plants">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm's community-focused model is contrasted with industrial processing plants, which Salatin argues harm the 'community ecology' through poor labor practices.</data>
      <data key="d8">community impact,labor ethics,philosophical contrast</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Initial Public Offerings (IPOs)">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm deliberately avoids IPOs as a matter of principle, believing they lead to unsustainable growth and compromise core values.</data>
      <data key="d8">business ethics,financial principle,growth strategy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c8b5f0f35b6bfccad911410ecdcdb7c1</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Tyson">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm's philosophy and operational model are positioned in direct opposition to the industrial, large-scale model represented by Tyson.</data>
      <data key="d8">business model contrast,ideological opposition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="Polyface Buying Club">
      <data key="d6">19.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Polyface Farm operates the Polyface Buying Club as its direct-to-consumer distribution model to deliver products to surrounding communities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Polyface Buying Club is an integral part of Polyface Farm's business model, serving as a direct-to-consumer sales channel that complements its larger institutional clients.</data>
      <data key="d8">business model,business operations,customer diversification,direct-to-consumer,distribution channel,distribution model</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e930a3eb466e9bb1dfa38b0df50bfd3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polyface Farm" target="White-Tablecloth Restaurants">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">White-tablecloth restaurants are a key customer segment for Polyface Farm, buying premium cuts like loin, which helps the farm sell the entire hog as part of its diversified patron portfolio.</data>
      <data key="d8">customer segment,product diversification,symbiotic sales</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
