      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diné (The People)" target="Fort Sumner">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Diné people were forcibly interned at Fort Sumner in New Mexico for four years as a result of the US government's campaign against them.</data>
      <data key="d8">displacement,forced internment,historical trauma</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diné (The People)" target="'Scorched Earth' Campaign">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The 'scorched earth' campaign was specifically targeted at the Diné people to force them into submission.</data>
      <data key="d8">historical conflict,subjugation,victimization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diné (The People)" target="Treaty of 1868">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The signing of the Treaty of 1868 was the event that secured the release of the Diné people from their forced internment.</data>
      <data key="d8">historical agreement,liberation,political resolution</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diné (The People)" target="Government Food Handouts">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">After losing their farmlands, the Diné were forced to depend on government food handouts for survival, marking a critical shift in their diet and health.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural loss,dietary shift,forced dependency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diné (The People)" target="Indigenous Nations">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Diné are presented as a specific example of the larger group of indigenous nations who are urgently working to save their cultures from being lost due to disconnection from land and food.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural preservation,group membership,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diet-Related Diseases" target="Government Food Handouts">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text explicitly links the introduction of government food handouts and the deviation from a traditional diet to the subsequent rise of diabetes and other degenerative diseases among the Diné.</data>
      <data key="d8">causation,nutritional impact,public health crisis</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Heirloom Seeds" target="Traditional Crops">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Traditional crops, such as a specific type of squash, are grown at the farm using heirloom seeds, which are essential for preserving this agricultural heritage.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural method,biodiversity,crop cultivation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fort Sumner" target="Treaty of 1868">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Treaty of 1868 officially ended the four-year forced internment of the Diné people at Fort Sumner.</data>
      <data key="d8">end of internment,historical resolution</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8155414292dfdc925038049e610bde08</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
