    <edge source="Hopi Culture" target="Traditional Hopi Farming">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Traditional Hopi Farming is described as being the very essence of Hopi Culture, not just a part of it but 'the life itself.' The decline of this farming practice is therefore portrayed as a direct threat to the survival of the culture.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural foundation,identity,way of life</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0f2f20c947452e869eb15dd25d5bcaf7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hopi Culture" target="Volksgeist">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The concept of 'Volksgeist' is applied directly to explain the unique and indefinable spirit of Hopi Culture, suggesting it is more than the sum of its observable parts.</data>
      <data key="d8">analytical framework,cultural theory</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0f2f20c947452e869eb15dd25d5bcaf7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hopi Culture" target="Cultural Identity">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Hopi Culture is presented as the specific example of a Cultural Identity that is under threat, with the text exploring its core components and the dangers it faces.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural analysis,specific example</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0f2f20c947452e869eb15dd25d5bcaf7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Traditional Hopi Farming" target="Climate Change">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Carl Honeyestewa identifies Climate Change as a direct threat to Traditional Hopi Farming, as altered weather patterns disrupt the delicate balance required for dry farming.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural impact,environmental threat</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0f2f20c947452e869eb15dd25d5bcaf7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Traditional Hopi Farming" target="Wildlife Change">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The described Wildlife Change, especially the arrival of new pest birds, directly harms the corn crops, posing a tangible threat to the success of Traditional Hopi Farming.</data>
      <data key="d8">crop damage,ecological threat</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0f2f20c947452e869eb15dd25d5bcaf7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Traditional Hopi Farming" target="Modernization">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Modernization is presented as a major societal force undermining Traditional Hopi Farming, as the need for jobs and modern conveniences competes with the traditional agricultural lifestyle.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural erosion,socioeconomic pressure</data>
