    <edge source="Climate Change" target="Hopi Farming">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Hopi farming is described as being in peril directly due to the effects of climate change, such as lack of rain and unseasonable cold, which threaten the corn crops.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural threat,environmental impact,prophecy fulfillment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Climate Change" target="Hopi Prophecy">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The prophecy explicitly foretells the environmental changes now being witnessed, such as the failure of rain and extreme cold, linking them to the coming starvation and cultural collapse.</data>
      <data key="d8">divine will,environmental prediction,prophecy fulfillment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Marie" target="Carl">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Marie and Carl are a married couple from the Honeyestewa family who share deep concerns about the decline of their Hopi culture and traditions.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural preservation,family,shared beliefs</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Marie" target="Hopi Prophecy">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Marie recounts the Hopi prophecy of cultural decline, explaining that although she disbelieved it as a child, she now sees it coming true through events in her life and community.</data>
      <data key="d8">belief,cultural transmission,prophecy fulfillment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Marie" target="Piki Bread">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Marie engages in the difficult traditional art of making piki bread, a skill that requires precision and experience.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural practice,food preparation,traditional skill</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Marie" target="Marie's Uncle">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Marie's uncle was the source of prophecies about environmental decline that she now believes are coming true, shaping her perspective.</data>
      <data key="d8">familial influence,oral tradition,prophecy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fa7136637ee2d131a4ae76b9cf2f5717</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Marie" target="Environmental Prophecies">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Marie was told these prophecies as a child, and her observation that the prophecies are coming true (e.g., a wash drying up) validates her concerns and her hope for change.</data>
      <data key="d8">belief validation,personal observation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fa7136637ee2d131a4ae76b9cf2f5717</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Carl" target="Honeyestewas">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Carl is a member of the Honeyestewa family and feels the weight of being the last farmer in his line, representing the family's-and the culture's-struggle to maintain their traditions.</data>
      <data key="d8">family heritage,farming,tradition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Carl" target="Carl's Father">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Carl expresses a deep reverence for his father and feels a personal responsibility to continue the family's farming tradition so that it does not end with his father's generation.</data>
      <data key="d8">family heritage,filial piety,legacy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hopi Prophecy" target="Snake Dance">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The failure of the Snake Dance to bring rain serves as concrete proof for Carl and Marie that the prophecy is coming true and that the Hopi's spiritual connection to the land is weakening.</data>
      <data key="d8">prophecy fulfillment,spiritual decline,symbolic event</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hopi Prophecy" target="Hopi Language">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The prophecy is shown to be coming true as Hopi children no longer know the words to ceremonial songs, demonstrating a breakdown in the transmission of the Hopi language and culture.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural erosion,language loss,prophecy fulfillment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hopi Prophecy" target="Marie's Uncle">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Marie's uncle was a key figure in transmitting the Hopi prophecy to her, fulfilling the traditional role of an elder passing down oral history.</data>
      <data key="d8">family lineage,knowledge transmission,oral tradition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0875465d0b75e1a7aada73d20c5bbe6b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
