      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ojibwe" target="Wild Rice">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Wild rice is a central part of the Ojibwe's cultural heritage and a traditional food source, which they have fought to protect through legal and legislative action against commercial exploitation and genetic modification.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural heritage,food sovereignty,legal protection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef9c9aefa244f3e5e6f50b424cd984c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ojibwe" target="Anishinabeg">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text identifies the Ojibwe as part of the broader Anishinabeg group of Indigenous peoples, whose culture the White Earth Land Recovery Project seeks to preserve.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural affiliation,indigenous group,tribal identity</data>
