    <edge source="White Earth Land Recovery Project" target="Anishinabeg">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The White Earth Land Recovery Project advocates on behalf of the Anishinabeg tribe by taking legal action to protect native wild rice, a food central to their culture and survival.&lt;SEP&gt;The White Earth Land Recovery Project's entire mission is to preserve the food heritage and culture of the Anishinabeg people and to reclaim their traditional lands.</data>
      <data key="d8">advocacy,community support,cultural preservation,cultural protection,indigenous rights,land reclamation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef9c9aefa244f3e5e6f50b424cd984c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac6f2d596c9d9fe2bc3b9afda4f10df</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="White Earth Land Recovery Project" target="Cultural Food Heritage">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The White Earth Land Recovery Project is a primary example in the text of an organization actively working to preserve and revitalize cultural food heritage to bring about positive change.</data>
      <data key="d8">activism,food sovereignty,heritage preservation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef9c9aefa244f3e5e6f50b424cd984c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="White Earth Land Recovery Project" target="1867 Treaty">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The White Earth Land Recovery Project's land reclamation efforts are directly aimed at recovering land that was originally granted to the Anishinabeg people by the 1867 treaty but was subsequently lost.</data>
      <data key="d8">historical treaty,land reclamation,restorative justice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef9c9aefa244f3e5e6f50b424cd984c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="White Earth Land Recovery Project" target="Type 2 Diabetes">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The White Earth Land Recovery Project actively works to combat the high rates of type 2 diabetes in the Native American community by providing food packages with traditional, healthier foods.</data>
      <data key="d8">community health,health intervention,traditional diet</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef9c9aefa244f3e5e6f50b424cd984c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="White Earth Land Recovery Project" target="Sturgeon">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The White Earth Land Recovery Project collaborates with fisheries biologists to reintroduce sturgeon into reservation waters, as part of its mission to restore the native ecosystem and cultural connections.</data>
      <data key="d8">cultural practice,ecological restoration,species reintroduction</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef9c9aefa244f3e5e6f50b424cd984c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
