    <edge source="Green Revolution" target="Petroleum">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Green Revolution constructed a food system that is now completely integrated with and dependent on petroleum.</data>
      <data key="d8">causality,resource dependency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fac6f2d596c9d9fe2bc3b9afda4f10df</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Green Revolution" target="Gulf of Mexico">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The agricultural practices popularized by the Green Revolution, particularly the heavy use of fertilizers, are identified as the cause of the annual dead zone in the Gulf of Mexico due to water pollution.</data>
      <data key="d8">consequence,environmental impact,pollution</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-59a4b4194753d7082d9b1d100574c96f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Green Revolution" target="Centers for Disease Control">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Centers for Disease Control's findings on an 'obesogenic' society are linked as a long-term public health consequence of the food system created by the Green Revolution, which produced abundant, cheap, and unhealthy processed foods.</data>
      <data key="d8">dietary impact,public health,system consequence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-59a4b4194753d7082d9b1d100574c96f</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Green Revolution" target="Jamie Ager">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Jamie Ager acknowledges the efficiency of the Green Revolution's industrial model but criticizes its negative ramifications, such as the disconnect between people and their food, which his own farming methods aim to correct.</data>
      <data key="d8">alternative model,critique</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f712d3550c8612228f9fb4dc999ba9b7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Green Revolution" target="Norman Borlaug">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Norman Borlaug is identified as the leader of the Green Revolution, having developed the high-yield crops that were central to its success.</data>
      <data key="d8">historical movement,leadership</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f712d3550c8612228f9fb4dc999ba9b7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Green Revolution" target="Food Waste">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The text argues that the Green Revolution, while increasing food production, was paradoxically accompanied by a massive increase in food waste.</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural paradox,historical trend,unintended consequence</data>
