    </edge>
    <edge source="Walking Fish" target="Josh Stoll">
      <data key="d6">48.0</data>
      <data key="d7">While he was a graduate student at Duke University, Josh Stoll co-founded the Walking Fish CSF in 2008 along with a group of fellow students. In addition to being one of its founders, Josh Stoll also serves as a representative for the Walking Fish organization and acts as a spokesperson for its mission and philosophy.</data>
      <data key="d8">academic initiative,founder,founding,leadership,personnel,representation,student project</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a7a0cfcfab5c2708055ae5c22dacee5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0fadd2de5cdd877a432eba713a59ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-062d9ac74f75199c91576d982ab5a9f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef2c308d995bae34c938de2dff3f5cf9</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Walking Fish" target="Bill Rice">
      <data key="d6">38.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Bill Rice is a co-founder and representative of the Walking Fish organization, where he also serves as the president of its board. He collaborated with Josh Stoll to establish Walking Fish as a means to support the local fishermen he worked with. Additionally, Bill Rice's market, Fishtowne, processes the co-op's seafood.</data>
      <data key="d8">business support,collaboration,founding,leadership,operational partnership,personnel,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-062d9ac74f75199c91576d982ab5a9f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81005569d65546868c017fed474ad248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0fadd2de5cdd877a432eba713a59ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a0cfcfab5c2708055ae5c22dacee5f</data>
