    <edge source="Feathernet" target="Millennium Feathernet">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Millennium Feathernet is the next-generation model after the Feathernet, adding more labor-saving features like self-watering and feeding systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">innovation,technological succession</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dd285deff310269197e8718b28f6076b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pigs" target="The Forest">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The pigs are taken to the forest for acorn finishing, and their activity of rooting on the forest floor is described as beneficial to the forest's ecosystem, creating a symbiotic relationship.</data>
      <data key="d8">animal habitat,ecosystem management,symbiotic relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ab7679e841cce082d6f5f864896c9afe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pigs" target="Acorn Finishing">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Pigs are the specific animals that undergo the acorn finishing process at Polyface farm, which is said to improve the flavor of the pork and save costs.</data>
      <data key="d8">finishing process,livestock management,product quality</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ab7679e841cce082d6f5f864896c9afe</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pigs" target="Polyface">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Pigs are an integral part of Polyface's intertwined systems, used for both composting and producing high-quality pork through the acorn finishing method.</data>
      <data key="d8">farm operations,integrated systems,livestock management</data>
