    <edge source="Appalachian Sustainable Development" target="Anthony Flaccovento">
      <data key="d6">49.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Anthony Flaccovento founded Appalachian Sustainable Development in 1995 and served as its executive director. As the founder and former director, he was instrumental in shaping the organization's mission, philosophy, and strategy, which is focused on building a local food system in Appalachia. Flaccovento is a key source for the organization's operational details and has articulated its strategies, such as starting small to build capacity and its key insights gained from working with supermarkets. He is also the listed representative for Appalachian Sustainable Development.</data>
      <data key="d8">contact person,founder,founding,leadership,organizational perspective,organizational strategy,representation,staff</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b26f04bc8df6a747ead835cc8d210eec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d3d51c80e398fde0d7a70a89888fa0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad0d4e7d44014acab56e26cbaa12a896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b16258e5de8192443e482a18e2beeb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Appalachian Sustainable Development" target="Scaling Up To Meet Large-Volume Demand">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Appalachian Sustainable Development provides a nuanced perspective on scaling up, suggesting that for some large buyers, reliability and predictability are more important than achieving maximum volume.</data>
      <data key="d8">alternative growth strategy,market needs,supplier reliability</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Appalachian Sustainable Development" target="Supermarkets">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Appalachian Sustainable Development has a working relationship with supermarkets, providing them with products from local growers and finding them to be patient partners who value reliability.</data>
      <data key="d8">local sourcing,market linkage,supply chain partnership</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-07373ff8a8e2c42149614780aa736a26</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Appalachian Sustainable Development" target="Small To Medium-Sized Grocery Stores">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Appalachian Sustainable Development used small to medium-sized grocery stores as their initial market to 'cut their teeth' and develop their systems for cooling, packaging, and grading.</data>
      <data key="d8">business development,initial partnership,market entry</data>
