    <edge source="Oren Molovinsky" target="Whole Animal Utilization">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Oren Molovinsky pioneers a business model for restaurants that is built on the principle of whole animal utilization, thereby solving a critical problem for farmers who need to sell the entire animal, not just prime cuts.</data>
      <data key="d8">economic solution,supply chain innovation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-09e000817f207794412f1a62763dda17</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Virginia Department of Agriculture and Consumer Services" target="Catherine Cash">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Catherine Cash is a staff member of the Virginia Department of Agriculture and Consumer Services.</data>
      <data key="d8">employment,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c9f558ccef1d0a97c2f1550636dc3f28</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Virginia Department of Agriculture and Consumer Services" target="Molovinsky">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Virginia Department of Agriculture and Consumer Services provided critical assistance to Molovinsky by helping him find reliable farmers and establish program criteria.</data>
      <data key="d8">government support,partnership</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-217f96b464101a2919ccf861b25fe27c</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Whole Animal Utilization" target="Farm to Table D.C. Restaurant Cooperative">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The cooperative's success is dependent on its ability to practice Whole Animal Utilization, as it buys entire animals from farmers. This principle is central to its operational and financial model.</data>
      <data key="d8">core principle,operational requirement,sustainable practice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Whole Animal Utilization" target="Local Food Supply Chain">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Whole Animal Utilization is a foundational concept of the Local Food Supply Chain, as it ensures farmers can sell their entire product, which makes the local system economically sustainable for them.</data>
      <data key="d8">economic viability,foundational principle,symbiotic relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Australian International Meat Distributor" target="Molovinsky">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A conversation with a representative from this distributor provided Molovinsky with a key insight into the workings and perceived irrationality of the global meat trade, strengthening his resolve to create an alternative.</data>
      <data key="d8">conceptual development,information source</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Farm to Table D.C. Restaurant Cooperative">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky is the founder and central organizer of the cooperative, having conceived the idea, managed the logistics, and recruited the members.</data>
      <data key="d8">founder,leadership,system creation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Miller">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky, the manager, and Miller, the chef, collaborated to reengineer the menu at Mie N Yu, which was a critical first step in making the plan to use whole animals from local farms feasible.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,menu innovation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Local Food Supply Chain">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky is the primary architect and advocate for the Local Food Supply Chain described in the text, turning his critique of the global system into a functioning, alternative model.</data>
      <data key="d8">advocacy,innovation,system design</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Virginia Agriculture Agency">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky worked with the Virginia agriculture agency to find suitable farms that could supply the products needed by the cooperative's member restaurants.</data>
      <data key="d8">government collaboration,sourcing</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Global Meat Market System">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky is a vocal critic of the Global Meat Market System, viewing it as illogical and costly. His entire initiative was a direct response to its perceived failings.</data>
      <data key="d8">criticism,motivation,system opposition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="D.C. Restaurant Association">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky leveraged his affiliation with the D.C. Restaurant Association to connect with other restaurants, which became the first members of his cooperative.</data>
      <data key="d8">networking,professional affiliation,recruitment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Catherine Cash">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky collaborated with Catherine Cash to develop specific animal welfare rules and labeling criteria for the cooperative's meat suppliers.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,regulation development</data>
