      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Harry's Tap Room">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky is actively assisting Harry's Tap Room in learning how to source local ingredients and redesign its menu, acting as a consultant or mentor.</data>
      <data key="d8">consulting,knowledge transfer</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c9f558ccef1d0a97c2f1550636dc3f28</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Restaurant Cooperative">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky is a strong advocate for the restaurant cooperative model, stating it is the 'only way' for independent restaurants to sustainably source local products.</data>
      <data key="d8">advocacy,conceptual leadership</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c9f558ccef1d0a97c2f1550636dc3f28</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Cooperative-supplying Farmers">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky builds personal, family-like relationships with the farmers, works with them to meet criteria, and handles difficult conversations about payments and charges.</data>
      <data key="d8">negotiation,partnership,relationship management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c9f558ccef1d0a97c2f1550636dc3f28</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Capital Meat Company">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky's efforts to expand local food distribution are exemplified by Capital Meat Company's new practice of buying whole animals from local farms.</data>
      <data key="d8">industry influence,market expansion</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c9f558ccef1d0a97c2f1550636dc3f28</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Saval Foods">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky's work to expand local distribution is shown through Saval Foods' recent venture into offering naturally grown beef from a local farm cooperative.</data>
      <data key="d8">industry influence,market expansion</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c9f558ccef1d0a97c2f1550636dc3f28</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Existing Distributors">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky states that his cooperative model cannot rely on typical distributors, but also suggests engaging them when possible to avoid creating adversarial relationships.</data>
      <data key="d8">industry navigation,strategic relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c9f558ccef1d0a97c2f1550636dc3f28</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Whole-Animal Approach">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky is a strong advocate for the whole-animal approach, viewing it as the most effective way for restaurants to support local farmers and drive change in the food industry.</data>
      <data key="d8">advocacy,industry reform</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7ef5e8f2029677f15d6ee8815b5828c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Diners">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky provides the insight that diners are motivated to buy local meat dishes because they perceive a connection to a specific farm as an indicator of higher quality and uniqueness.</data>
      <data key="d8">consumer psychology,quality perception</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7ef5e8f2029677f15d6ee8815b5828c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Local Farmers' Market">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky is critical of restaurants that limit their 'local' program to buying cuts from a farmers' market, as he believes it does not provide the same level of support to farmers as the whole-animal model.</data>
      <data key="d8">critique,sustainable practice</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7ef5e8f2029677f15d6ee8815b5828c4</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="D.C. Restaurant Cooperative">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky was the founder and driving force behind the D.C. Restaurant Cooperative, spending 6-8 months visiting farms and plants to get it started.</data>
      <data key="d8">establishment,founder,initiative</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-65dc312cbeeaa82060b27a69060e671d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Culinary Schools">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky advocates for culinary schools to change their curriculum to include traditional slow-cooking methods to address a skill gap among chefs, which he sees as crucial for the success of whole-animal programs.</data>
      <data key="d8">advocacy,critique,educational reform</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-65dc312cbeeaa82060b27a69060e671d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Virginia Farms">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky personally visited and established the foundational supply chain relationships with numerous farms in Virginia for his cooperative.</data>
      <data key="d8">partnership,sourcing,supply chain development</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-65dc312cbeeaa82060b27a69060e671d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="Processing Plants">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">As part of the effort to establish the D.C. restaurant cooperative, Molovinsky visited processing plants to understand and organize the entire supply chain from farm to restaurant.</data>
      <data key="d8">due diligence,operational setup,supply chain logistics</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-65dc312cbeeaa82060b27a69060e671d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Molovinsky" target="D.C. restaurant cooperative">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Molovinsky was the founder and primary manager of the D.C. restaurant cooperative, spending months establishing its operations and supply chain.</data>
      <data key="d8">founder,program management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-217f96b464101a2919ccf861b25fe27c</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Catherine Tatman" target="Farm to Table D.C. Restaurant Cooperative">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Catherine Tatman is a farmer who supplies meat to the cooperative. The cooperative's model provides her with a stable income and reduced risk, making her a key beneficiary and proof of the concept's success.&lt;SEP&gt;Catherine Tatman is a supplier to the cooperative. The relationship provides her with a stable market and guaranteed prices for her whole animals, significantly reducing her business risk and increasing profits.</data>
      <data key="d8">economic stability,farmer benefit,supplier relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Catherine Tatman" target="Hilldale Farm">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Catherine Tatman is the farmer who operates Hilldale Farm, which supplies meat to the cooperative.</data>
      <data key="d8">farming,ownership</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Farm to Table D.C. Restaurant Cooperative" target="D.C. Central Kitchen (Dcck)">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The cooperative established a key partnership by contracting DCCK as its sole distributor, providing DCCK with a crucial business opportunity and creating a synergistic relationship.</data>
      <data key="d8">distribution,nonprofit collaboration,strategic partnership</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Farm to Table D.C. Restaurant Cooperative" target="Cooperative Operation Start">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Cooperative Operation Start in October 2008 is the formal launch of the cooperative, marking the transition from an idea to a functioning business that channels money into the local farm economy.</data>
      <data key="d8">inception,launch event,milestone</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Farm to Table D.C. Restaurant Cooperative" target="D.C.">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The cooperative was formed by and serves restaurants located in D.C., delivering locally-sourced meat to this urban market.</data>
      <data key="d8">market location,service area</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Farm to Table D.C. Restaurant Cooperative" target="'Just-in-Time' Inventory">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The cooperative had to develop a new logistics system that could provide chefs with the flexibility they were used to from the 'Just-in-Time' Inventory model, while also accommodating the realities of local farming and processing.</data>
      <data key="d8">operational alternative,systemic challenge</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-912655071bfb31832bd5d960fea37c88</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1753740886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="D.C. Central Kitchen (Dcck)" target="Shenandoah Valley Produce Auction">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Enabled by its delivery contract with the cooperative, DCCK was able to expand its own sourcing and became the largest single buyer at the Shenandoah Valley Produce Auction, demonstrating the ripple effects of the new supply chain.</data>
